    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1498d3e9274c335c6068",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The labels to fields transformer is internally two separate transformations. The first acts on single series and extracts labels to fields. The second is the [merge](#merge) transformation that joins all the results into a single table. The merge transformation tries to join on all matching fields. This merge step is required and cannot be turned off.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Transform data",
        "Transformation functions",
        "Labels to fields",
        "Merging behavior"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/query-transform-data/transform-data/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "9cd072609170b1783ea50740845dd11e18b0fede",
        "sha256": "73ae12b953aaf13c6df7b5a072cc18677d57c977343a108001752487a81b2800",
