    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c6dedb9c62aeee953b37",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Use this transformation to rename parts of the query results using a regular expression and replacement pattern.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Transform data",
        "Transformation functions",
        "Rename by regex"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/query-transform-data/transform-data/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "9cd072609170b1783ea50740845dd11e18b0fede",
        "sha256": "73ae12b953aaf13c6df7b5a072cc18677d57c977343a108001752487a81b2800",
        "lineStart": 1323,
        "lineEnd": 1323,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/query-transform-data/transform-data/index.md#L1323-L1323"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0d311c020a1093101ae4",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can specify a regular expression, which is only applied to matches, along with a replacement pattern that support back references. For example, let's imagine you're visualizing CPU usage per host and you want to remove the domain name. You could set the regex to '/^([^.]+).\\*/' and the replacement pattern to '$1', 'web-01.example.com' would become 'web-01'.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Transform data",
        "Transformation functions",
        "Rename by regex"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/query-transform-data/transform-data/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "9cd072609170b1783ea50740845dd11e18b0fede",
        "sha256": "73ae12b953aaf13c6df7b5a072cc18677d57c977343a108001752487a81b2800",
        "lineStart": 1325,
        "lineEnd": 1325,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/query-transform-data/transform-data/index.md#L1325-L1325"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7cc48f03a8bbe0698d86",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "> **Note:** The Rename by regex transformation was improved in Grafana v9.0.0 to allow global patterns of the form '/<stringToReplace>/g'. Depending on the regex match used, this may cause some transformations to behave slightly differently. You can guarantee the same behavior as before by wrapping the match string in forward slashes '(/)', e.g. '(._)' would become '/(._)/'.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Transform data",
        "Transformation functions",
        "Rename by regex"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/query-transform-data/transform-data/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "9cd072609170b1783ea50740845dd11e18b0fede",
        "sha256": "73ae12b953aaf13c6df7b5a072cc18677d57c977343a108001752487a81b2800",
        "lineStart": 1327,
        "lineEnd": 1327,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/query-transform-data/transform-data/index.md#L1327-L1327"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6485152f620a9491b15e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In the following example, we are stripping the 'A-' prefix from field names. In the before image, you can see everything is prefixed with 'A-':",
      "headingPath": [
        "Transform data",
        "Transformation functions",
        "Rename by regex"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/query-transform-data/transform-data/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "9cd072609170b1783ea50740845dd11e18b0fede",
        "sha256": "73ae12b953aaf13c6df7b5a072cc18677d57c977343a108001752487a81b2800",
        "lineStart": 1329,
        "lineEnd": 1329,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/query-transform-data/transform-data/index.md#L1329-L1329"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3e96638fac909bb40b3e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "With the transformation applied, you can see we are left with just the remainder of the string.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Transform data",
        "Transformation functions",
        "Rename by regex"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/query-transform-data/transform-data/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "9cd072609170b1783ea50740845dd11e18b0fede",
        "sha256": "73ae12b953aaf13c6df7b5a072cc18677d57c977343a108001752487a81b2800",
        "lineStart": 1333,
        "lineEnd": 1333,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/query-transform-data/transform-data/index.md#L1333-L1333"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6961dd30455b34631c68",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Use this transformation to convert rows into separate fields. This can be useful because fields can be styled and configured individually. It can also use additional fields as sources for dynamic field configuration or map them to field labels. The additional labels can then be used to define better display names for the resulting fields.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Transform data",
        "Transformation functions",
        "Rows to fields"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/query-transform-data/transform-data/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "9cd072609170b1783ea50740845dd11e18b0fede",
        "sha256": "73ae12b953aaf13c6df7b5a072cc18677d57c977343a108001752487a81b2800",
        "lineStart": 1341,
        "lineEnd": 1341,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/query-transform-data/transform-data/index.md#L1341-L1341"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d651279e197c77ae6a51",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This transformation includes a field table which lists all fields in the data returned by the configuration query. This table gives you control over what field should be mapped to each configuration property (the **Use as** option). You can also choose which value to select if there are multiple rows in the returned data.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Transform data",
        "Transformation functions",
        "Rows to fields"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/query-transform-data/transform-data/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "9cd072609170b1783ea50740845dd11e18b0fede",
        "sha256": "73ae12b953aaf13c6df7b5a072cc18677d57c977343a108001752487a81b2800",
