      "id": "grafana.candidate.3e3d51866effde0a17ea",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "**Soft min** and **soft max** settings can prevent blips from turning into mountains when the data is mostly flat, and hard min or max derived from standard min and max field options can prevent intermittent spikes from flattening useful detail by clipping the spikes past a defined point.",
      "headingPath": [
