    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.393fb6a32eeb185b2bc8",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The candlestick visualization allows you to visualize data that includes a number of consistent dimensions focused on price movements, such as stock prices. The candlestick visualization includes an [Open-High-Low-Close (OHLC) mode](#open-high-low-close), as well as support for additional dimensions based on time series data.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Candlestick"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/visualizations/candlestick/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ea3b660d4134adcfd2fa5b60a61b1ce9ca72ac03",
        "sha256": "7e951850c53252a9a8966f33d32e244bbd9aaf9c1f556e0c570465492b1e68bd",
        "lineStart": 46,
        "lineEnd": 46,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/visualizations/candlestick/index.md#L46-L46"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.50c3147fc6a09ab2886f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Candlestick visualizations build upon the foundation of the [time series visualization](ref:time-series-visualization) and include many common configuration settings.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Candlestick"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/visualizations/candlestick/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ea3b660d4134adcfd2fa5b60a61b1ce9ca72ac03",
        "sha256": "7e951850c53252a9a8966f33d32e244bbd9aaf9c1f556e0c570465492b1e68bd",
        "lineStart": 48,
        "lineEnd": 48,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/visualizations/candlestick/index.md#L48-L48"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ef361ff6ad06768c7aac",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can use a candlestick if you want to visualize, at a glance, how a price moved over time, whether it went up, down, or stayed the same, and how much it fluctuated:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Candlestick"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/visualizations/candlestick/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ea3b660d4134adcfd2fa5b60a61b1ce9ca72ac03",
        "sha256": "7e951850c53252a9a8966f33d32e244bbd9aaf9c1f556e0c570465492b1e68bd",
        "lineStart": 50,
        "lineEnd": 50,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/visualizations/candlestick/index.md#L50-L50"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.80e9fb924143065f6021",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Each candlestick is represented as a rectangle, referred to as the _candlestick body_. The candlestick body displays the opening and closing prices during a time period. Green candlesticks represent when the price appreciated while the red candlesticks represent when the price depreciated. The lines sticking out the candlestick body are referred to as _wicks_ or _shadows_, which represent the highest and lowest prices during the time period.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Candlestick"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/visualizations/candlestick/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ea3b660d4134adcfd2fa5b60a61b1ce9ca72ac03",
        "sha256": "7e951850c53252a9a8966f33d32e244bbd9aaf9c1f556e0c570465492b1e68bd",
