    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.cff5e480b556a17883f7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "By default, the visualization [calculates](#value-options) a single value per column or series and displays only the last row of data. However, it derives the minimum and maximum from the full dataset, even if those values aren't visible.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Gauge",
        "Supported data formats",
        "Example - Multiple rows and values"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/visualizations/gauge/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f93201fcfc0254672ca2ebc6f3763e46a0c1d600",
