    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a0d0c5d637ffd4aa48fe",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can access the first three options from the log line details or from the log line menu:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Logs"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/visualizations/logs/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "85e2c4734572a18668063acf060c2fbdefc96d36",
        "sha256": "40291edffa29c16ef9a5b28f5f4e947999533dabfd6a6f36408b50ec775ab7a0",
        "lineStart": 50,
        "lineEnd": 50,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/visualizations/logs/index.md#L50-L50"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.bbed313109bd75c6ffeb",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Typically, you use logs with a graph visualization to display the log output of a related process. If you have an incident in your application or systems, such as a website disruption or code failure, you can use the logs visualization to help you figure out what went wrong, when, and even why.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Logs"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/visualizations/logs/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "85e2c4734572a18668063acf060c2fbdefc96d36",
        "sha256": "40291edffa29c16ef9a5b28f5f4e947999533dabfd6a6f36408b50ec775ab7a0",
        "lineStart": 56,
        "lineEnd": 56,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/visualizations/logs/index.md#L56-L56"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.34730f13fa24239d901c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The following video provides a walkthrough of creating a logs visualization. You'll also learn how to customize some settings and log visualization caveats:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Logs",
        "Configure a log visualization"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/visualizations/logs/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "85e2c4734572a18668063acf060c2fbdefc96d36",
        "sha256": "40291edffa29c16ef9a5b28f5f4e947999533dabfd6a6f36408b50ec775ab7a0",
        "lineStart": 60,
        "lineEnd": 60,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/visualizations/logs/index.md#L60-L60"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b9be22b752ec89d21cbe",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The preferred dataplane log format uses a `timestamp` time field and a `body` string field. It can also include optional `severity`, `id`, and `labels` fields.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Logs",
        "Supported data formats"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/visualizations/logs/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "85e2c4734572a18668063acf060c2fbdefc96d36",
        "sha256": "40291edffa29c16ef9a5b28f5f4e947999533dabfd6a6f36408b50ec775ab7a0",
        "lineStart": 68,
        "lineEnd": 68,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/visualizations/logs/index.md#L68-L68"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.cd6437f754b527ba4ebb",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can also build legacy log-formatted data from other data sources as long as the first field is a time type followed by string, number, and time fields. The leading time field is used to sort and timestamp the logs and if the data contains other time-type fields, they’re included as elements of the logged record.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Logs",
        "Supported data formats"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/visualizations/logs/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "85e2c4734572a18668063acf060c2fbdefc96d36",
        "sha256": "40291edffa29c16ef9a5b28f5f4e947999533dabfd6a6f36408b50ec775ab7a0",
        "lineStart": 70,
        "lineEnd": 70,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/visualizations/logs/index.md#L70-L70"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.bd3342a92b5ca453f33c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The second field is used as the log record title regardless of whether it’s a time, numeric, or string field. Usually the second field is a text field containing multiple string elements, but if the message level (or `lvl`) is present, the visualization uses the values in it to add colors to the record, as described in [Log levels integration](ref:log-levels).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Logs",
        "Supported data formats"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/visualizations/logs/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "85e2c4734572a18668063acf060c2fbdefc96d36",
        "sha256": "40291edffa29c16ef9a5b28f5f4e947999533dabfd6a6f36408b50ec775ab7a0",
        "lineStart": 72,
        "lineEnd": 72,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/visualizations/logs/index.md#L72-L72"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d4c5f29214d88aa7ec0a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To limit the number of log lines rendered in the visualization, you can use the **Max data points** setting in the panel **Query options**. If that option isn't set, then the data source typically enforces its own default limit.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Logs",
        "Supported data formats"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/visualizations/panels-visualizations/visualizations/logs/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "85e2c4734572a18668063acf060c2fbdefc96d36",
        "sha256": "40291edffa29c16ef9a5b28f5f4e947999533dabfd6a6f36408b50ec775ab7a0",
        "lineStart": 76,
