    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2865eba99eb76fb660f3",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In subsequent releases, we’ll be refining and enhancing the user interface for Correlations, to provide a more streamlined user experience.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.0",
        "Correlations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "744b2d1230211f70aa6158231d9505e732ac0315",
        "sha256": "dd311853975cca7ef6ad474588f832614dd9c445856343920d238a1ddf183739",
        "lineStart": 52,
        "lineEnd": 52,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md#L52-L52"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.589bf157fda6dd90e9d7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Scenes is a new front-end library by Grafana that empowers Grafana plugin developers to effortlessly build stunning dashboard-like experiences into their Grafana app plugins. With Scenes, you can easily create apps that mirror the Grafana dashboarding experience, complete with template variable support, flexible layouts, dynamic panel rendering, and so much more.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.0",
        "Scenes"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "744b2d1230211f70aa6158231d9505e732ac0315",
        "sha256": "dd311853975cca7ef6ad474588f832614dd9c445856343920d238a1ddf183739",
        "lineStart": 60,
        "lineEnd": 60,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md#L60-L60"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8cc17321f72779f8dc70",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can now try out creating subfolders in Grafana for organizing your dashboards and alerts. You can enable this new feature in your development environment to create, read, update, and delete subfolders, making it easier to sort resources by business units, departments, and teams.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.0",
        "Subfolders"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "744b2d1230211f70aa6158231d9505e732ac0315",
        "sha256": "dd311853975cca7ef6ad474588f832614dd9c445856343920d238a1ddf183739",
        "lineStart": 72,
        "lineEnd": 72,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md#L72-L72"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.07f90ee082f877d16ec9",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can also set up permissions using Role-Based Access Control (RBAC). Folder permissions cascade, being inherited from the parent folder, which simplifies access management.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.0",
        "Subfolders"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "744b2d1230211f70aa6158231d9505e732ac0315",
        "sha256": "dd311853975cca7ef6ad474588f832614dd9c445856343920d238a1ddf183739",
        "lineStart": 74,
        "lineEnd": 74,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md#L74-L74"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e5b5720cf48a265aed25",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The ability to add subfolders is currently in preview, with more functionality coming in subsequent releases. This includes creating subfolders using Terraform, and displaying the full folder tree when creating and moving resources through Grafana’s UI. We recommend that you enable this feature only on test or development instances, rather than in production environments.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.0",
        "Subfolders"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "744b2d1230211f70aa6158231d9505e732ac0315",
        "sha256": "dd311853975cca7ef6ad474588f832614dd9c445856343920d238a1ddf183739",
        "lineStart": 76,
        "lineEnd": 76,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md#L76-L76"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ab4d7b02f86cd5e4113d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To get started creating subfolders, enable the `nestedFolders` feature toggle. If you’re using Grafana Cloud, and would like to enable this feature, please contact customer support.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.0",
        "Subfolders"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "744b2d1230211f70aa6158231d9505e732ac0315",
        "sha256": "dd311853975cca7ef6ad474588f832614dd9c445856343920d238a1ddf183739",
        "lineStart": 78,
        "lineEnd": 78,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md#L78-L78"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.52ca2ecc2d4475c0d42c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We're promoting the canvas panel out of public preview and into general availability. Over the past several months we've introduced multiple enhancements to the panel such as the ability to draw connections between elements, the ability to set the color and size of connections based on data, and the ability to add data links. We're excited to include Canvas as a first class citizen in Grafana’s core panel library. To learn more about the panel, refer to our [Canvas documentation](../../panels-visualizations/visualizations/canvas/). Also, check out our [latest blog post about canvas](https://grafana.com/blog/2023/05/11/use-canvas-panels-to-customize-visualizations-in-grafana/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.0",
        "Dashboards and visualizations",
        "The Canvas panel is GA"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "744b2d1230211f70aa6158231d9505e732ac0315",
        "sha256": "dd311853975cca7ef6ad474588f832614dd9c445856343920d238a1ddf183739",
        "lineStart": 90,
        "lineEnd": 90,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md#L90-L90"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.5996079c26487ff3fd96",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The Trends panel allows you to display trends where the x-axis is numeric and not time. This experimental panel addresses gaps that were not solved by either the Time series or XY Chart panels. For example, you can plot function graphs, rpm/torque curves, supply/demand relationships, and more. To learn more about the Trend panel, refer to the [Trend documentation](../../panels-visualizations/visualizations/trend/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.0",
        "Dashboards and visualizations",
        "New Trend Panel"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "744b2d1230211f70aa6158231d9505e732ac0315",
        "sha256": "dd311853975cca7ef6ad474588f832614dd9c445856343920d238a1ddf183739",
        "lineStart": 100,
        "lineEnd": 100,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md#L100-L100"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6a7e9a2796ed686b4272",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Datagrid is a new panel that allows you to edit your data within a Grafana dashboard. Imagine having a spreadsheet-like view where you can fine-tune data pulled from a data source or create your own dataset from scratch and use it within your dashboard to update your panels in real time. That's what Datagrid provides. You can also use the Datagrid panel as a data source used by other panels to augment other data.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.0",
        "Dashboards and visualizations",
        "New Datagrid panel"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "744b2d1230211f70aa6158231d9505e732ac0315",
        "sha256": "dd311853975cca7ef6ad474588f832614dd9c445856343920d238a1ddf183739",
        "lineStart": 110,
        "lineEnd": 110,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md#L110-L110"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a4b7f89089353e50aa46",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Currently, the Datagrid Panel supports the following features in Grafana version 10.0:",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.0",
        "Dashboards and visualizations",
        "New Datagrid panel"
      ],
