    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.aaac2ff300c7b8477938",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To try it out, enable the `newTraceViewHeader` feature toggle. This feature is enabled by default in Grafana Cloud.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.0",
        "Tracing",
        "Span filtering for traces"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "744b2d1230211f70aa6158231d9505e732ac0315",
        "sha256": "dd311853975cca7ef6ad474588f832614dd9c445856343920d238a1ddf183739",
        "lineStart": 311,
        "lineEnd": 311,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md#L311-L311"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a3024daee50b6b027a90",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The Azure Monitor data source now supports visualizing Application Insights Traces. A new query type, `Traces`, has been added to the service list. This can be used against Application Insights resources to query and visualize traces in both a tabular format and using the built-in Traces visualization.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.0",
        "Data sources",
        "Azure Monitor data source"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "744b2d1230211f70aa6158231d9505e732ac0315",
        "sha256": "dd311853975cca7ef6ad474588f832614dd9c445856343920d238a1ddf183739",
        "lineStart": 329,
        "lineEnd": 329,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md#L329-L329"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.501d9c845bd9af2210c8",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This also includes support for a new Azure API that will correlate trace IDs against all Application Insights resources that are accessible to the principal that the data source is configured with. To support this feature, a new query builder has been added with support for querying the Application Insights resource using an `Operation ID` or visualizing and filtering the data based on the event type and a subset of the properties available on the trace.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.0",
        "Data sources",
        "Azure Monitor data source"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "744b2d1230211f70aa6158231d9505e732ac0315",
        "sha256": "dd311853975cca7ef6ad474588f832614dd9c445856343920d238a1ddf183739",
        "lineStart": 331,
        "lineEnd": 331,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md#L331-L331"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4decf9e94db961cd5a24",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The Prometheus data source now supports delta (incremental) querying, in which values from data frames are cached and leveraged to modify future requests to avoid requesting duplicate values in dashboards with now-relative (that is, any dashboard querying until \"now\") queries. This feature is disabled by default as it is still experimental, but can be enabled and configured in the Prometheus data source configuration.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.0",
        "Data sources",
        "Prometheus dashboard performance improvements"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "744b2d1230211f70aa6158231d9505e732ac0315",
        "sha256": "dd311853975cca7ef6ad474588f832614dd9c445856343920d238a1ddf183739",
        "lineStart": 339,
        "lineEnd": 339,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md#L339-L339"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ff634a8242d5f4a8de40",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We've renamed the Phlare data source _Grafana Pyroscope_ data source as part of the ongoing unification of the Phlare and Pyroscope projects. This data source supports both Phlare and Pyroscope backends. Existing instances of the data source should not be affected. When you create a new instance of the data source, the backend type will be autodetected on the configuration page, or you can select it manually.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.0",
        "Data sources",
        "Phlare renamed to Grafana Pyroscope"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "744b2d1230211f70aa6158231d9505e732ac0315",
        "sha256": "dd311853975cca7ef6ad474588f832614dd9c445856343920d238a1ddf183739",
        "lineStart": 349,
        "lineEnd": 349,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md#L349-L349"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.31905e35a5f58a7dde2b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Data types are now being defined to create a data plane layer between producers and consumers of data. By defining data types as part of Grafana's platform, plugin and application developers can use these data types to achieve more reliable interoperability across the platform.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.0",
        "Data sources",
        "Data plane"
      ],
      "source": {
