    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a6779c1b4fbd4125c91f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To query these data sources from Grafana Cloud, you've had to open your private network to a range of IP addresses, a non-starter for many IT Security teams. The challenge is, how do you connect to your private data from Grafana Cloud, without exposing your network?",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.0",
        "Security",
        "Private data source connect"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "744b2d1230211f70aa6158231d9505e732ac0315",
        "sha256": "dd311853975cca7ef6ad474588f832614dd9c445856343920d238a1ddf183739",
        "lineStart": 415,
        "lineEnd": 415,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md#L415-L415"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.cf5fd69ad70572949d64",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The answer is Private Data Source Connect (PDC), available now in public preview in Grafana Cloud Pro and Advanced. PDC uses SOCKS over SSH to establish a secure connection between a lightweight PDC agent you deploy on your network and your Grafana Cloud stack. PDC keeps the network connection totally under your control. It’s easy to set up and manage, uses industry-standard security protocols, and works across public cloud vendors and a wide variety of secure networks. Learn more in our [Private data source connect documentation](/docs/grafana-cloud/data-configuration/configure-private-datasource-connect).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.0",
        "Security",
        "Private data source connect"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "744b2d1230211f70aa6158231d9505e732ac0315",
        "sha256": "dd311853975cca7ef6ad474588f832614dd9c445856343920d238a1ddf183739",
        "lineStart": 417,
        "lineEnd": 417,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md#L417-L417"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2bbab2781c39d7b6d397",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We've added support for using `react-router` v6 in app plugins. However, we still support the use of `react-router` v5 for plugins that need to support a minimum Grafana version earlier than v10. For more information, refer to our [react-router migration guide](https://grafana.com/developers/plugin-tools/migration-guides/update-from-grafana-versions/migrate-9_x-to-10_x#update-to-react-router-v6).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.0",
        "Plugins",
        "App plugins can start using react-router v6"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "744b2d1230211f70aa6158231d9505e732ac0315",
        "sha256": "dd311853975cca7ef6ad474588f832614dd9c445856343920d238a1ddf183739",
        "lineStart": 423,
        "lineEnd": 423,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-0.md#L423-L423"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f74427ba551306be188e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Welcome to Grafana 10.1! Read on to learn about changes to dashboards and visualizations, data sources, security and authentication and more. We're particularly excited about a set of improvements to visualizing logs from [Loki](https://grafana.com/products/cloud/logs/) and other logging data sources in Explore mode, and our Flame graph panel, used to visualize profiling data from [Pyroscope](https://grafana.com/blog/2023/03/15/pyroscope-grafana-phlare-join-for-oss-continuous-profiling/?pg=oss-phlare&plcmt=top-promo-banner) and other continuous profiling data sources.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
