    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1f28493c2614b6cc52bc",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This experimental feature introduces a clear distinction between two different categories of panel plugin types: visualization panels that consume a data source and a new type, called _widgets_, that don't require a data source.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Dashboards and visualizations",
        "Distinguish widgets from visualizations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 63,
        "lineEnd": 63,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L63-L63"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7200fbfd10b231bd0342",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Now, you can easily add widgets like Text, News, and Annotation list without the need to select a data source. The plugins list and library panels are filtered based on whether you've selected a widget or visualization, providing a streamlined editing experience.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Dashboards and visualizations",
        "Distinguish widgets from visualizations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 65,
        "lineEnd": 65,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L65-L65"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b29319220dd789deef59",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To see the widget editor in Grafana OSS or Enterprise, enable the `vizAndWidgetSplit` feature toggle. If you’re using Grafana Cloud and would like to enable this feature, please contact customer support.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Dashboards and visualizations",
        "Distinguish widgets from visualizations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 67,
        "lineEnd": 67,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L67-L67"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2cd2921954f168076f32",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When working with date and time data, it can be useful to have different time formats. With the new Format Time transformation, you can convert any time format to any other one supported by [Moment.js](https://momentjs.com/docs/#/displaying/). When used in conjunction with the _Group by_ transformation, this can also be used to bucket days, weeks, and other time windows together.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Dashboards and visualizations",
        "Format Time transformation"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 87,
        "lineEnd": 87,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L87-L87"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2ca5736f9b0ba4c535c7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The Join by field transformation has a new option: outer join (tabular). This option is a true outer join for tabular (SQL-like) data. Data can now be joined on a field value that is not distinct. This is different from the previous outer join, which is optimized for time-series data where the join values are never repeated.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Dashboards and visualizations",
        "Join by fields transformation outer join (tabular) option"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 97,
        "lineEnd": 97,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L97-L97"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8ce270d348b40a8cd84b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can now choose whether to set a threshold above which values in the data should be disconnected. This can be useful in cases where you have sensors that report a value at a set interval, but you want to disconnect the values when the sensor does not respond. This feature complements the existing [connect null values functionality](../../panels-visualizations/visualizations/time-series/#connect-null-values).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Dashboards and visualizations",
        "Disconnect values in Time series, Trend, and State timeline visualizations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 105,
        "lineEnd": 105,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L105-L105"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c2d6839249f2207997db",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can now display network data in the Geomap visualization by using the new beta Network layer. This layer supports the same data format as the [Node graph visualization](../../panels-visualizations/visualizations/node-graph/#data-api).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Dashboards and visualizations",
        "Geomap Network layer"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 117,
        "lineEnd": 117,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L117-L117"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.180fb7475c52de90fdbf",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can now add data links to Heatmap visualizations. This allows you to add links to other dashboards, panels, or external URLs that are relevant to the data in your heatmap. We're pleased to highlight that this feature was a community contribution.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Dashboards and visualizations",
        "Heatmap visualizations now support data links"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 129,
        "lineEnd": 129,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L129-L129"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d1b8ed9ef153a8157df8",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To learn more, refer to both our [Heatmap documentation](../../panels-visualizations/visualizations/heatmap/) and our [Configure data links documentation](../../panels-visualizations/configure-data-links/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Dashboards and visualizations",
        "Heatmap visualizations now support data links"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
