    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e69aaa446255de5ecab9",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We've improved the Loki query editor by adding a new **Step** editor field. This field allows you to specify a value for the `step` parameter in Loki queries. You can use this parameter when making metric queries to Loki or when you want a matrix response from your queries.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Data sources",
        "Step editor in Loki"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 153,
        "lineEnd": 153,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L153-L153"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f783eb639040df609d08",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "By default, the `step` parameter is set to the value of the `$__interval` variable. This variable is calculated based on the time range and the width of the graph (in pixels). To learn more about the Loki `step` parameter, refer to our [Loki step parameter documentation](/docs/loki/latest/api/#step-versus-interval).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Data sources",
        "Step editor in Loki"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 155,
        "lineEnd": 155,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L155-L155"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4003cd3285ebb2c83d49",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "New functionality for linking of Loki log lines in Explore allows you to quickly navigate to specific log entries for precise analysis. By clicking the **Copy shortlink** button for a log line, you can generate and copy a [short URL](../../developers/http_api/short_url/) that provides direct access to the exact log entry within an absolute time range. When you open the link, Grafana automatically scrolls to the corresponding log line and highlights it, making it easy to identify and focus on the relevant information.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Data sources",
        "Copy link to a Loki log line"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 165,
        "lineEnd": 165,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L165-L165"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.12ea643a24c1853217bc",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana's Tempo data source now supports _streaming_ responses to TraceQL queries. With this feature, you can now see partial query results as they come in, so you no longer have to wait for the whole query to finish. This is perfect for big queries that take a long time to return a response.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Data sources",
        "TraceQL response streaming in Tempo"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 175,
        "lineEnd": 175,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L175-L175"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.15be30414118c1b2afe8",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To use this feature, enable the `traceQLStreaming` feature toggle. If you’re using Grafana Cloud and would like to enable this feature, please contact customer support.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Data sources",
        "TraceQL response streaming in Tempo"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 177,
        "lineEnd": 177,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L177-L177"
      },
