    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b9bcccb13a0545903d13",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The Loki and Elasticsearch data source configuration pages have been redesigned to make getting started and setting up data sources as simple and easy to understand as possible. You can now find new subsections with links to documentation pages, as well as tooltips to assist you with configuring and customizing data sources.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Data sources",
        "Configuration page redesign for Loki and Elasticsearch"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 224,
        "lineEnd": 224,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L224-L224"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.260709abcd57ec8ff428",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The Elasticsearch query editor now allows convenient switching between logs, metrics, and raw data directly from the top, eliminating the need to go through the metric selector.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Data sources",
        "Easier to use query editor for Elasticsearch"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 232,
        "lineEnd": 232,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L232-L232"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3dacd54ca9f21a0ce8cc",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The Metrics explorer is a new feature that enhances metrics browsing in the Prometheus query builder. The Metrics explorer makes it easier for you to find the right metric and get comfortable with PromQL. You can now explore metrics with additional metadata, perform fuzzy search on the metric name or description, and filter on the Prometheus type.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Data sources",
        "Metrics explorer"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 240,
        "lineEnd": 240,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L240-L240"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a0f9c2686ef216e9521f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Async query data support in Redshift and Athena makes queries over multiple requests (starting, checking status, and fetching the results) instead of in a single request query. This is useful for queries that can potentially run for a long time and time out. This feature was previously available behind a feature toggle and is now be generally available and enabled by default.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Data sources",
        "Redshift and Athena: Async query data support"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 250,
        "lineEnd": 250,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L250-L250"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.265efe9e3be9499a6860",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This feature adds support for query caching of async queries in the Athena and Redshift data source plugins. To try this feature, enable both the `useCachingService` and `awsAsyncQueryCaching` feature toggles. If you’re using Grafana Cloud and would like to enable this experimental feature, please contact customer support.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Data sources",
        "Redshift and Athena: Async query caching"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 258,
        "lineEnd": 258,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L258-L258"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4029c6e4bb2bf3458d72",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The CloudWatch logs query editor is moving from being a Slate-based editor to a Monaco-based editor. This new Monaco-based editor provides improved syntax highlighting, and auto-completion. To use the Monaco-based query editor, enable the `cloudWatchLogsMonacoEditor` feature toggle. If you’re using Grafana Cloud and would like to enable this feature, please contact customer support.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Data sources",
        "CloudWatch logs Monaco query editor"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 266,
        "lineEnd": 266,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L266-L266"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2b40777a6ddebc211283",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Previously, InfluxDB backend mode was available, however, there were compatibility issues that needed to be addressed. In this release, we've addressed these issues and promoted this feature from experimental to public preview. In the future, backend mode will be the default, and we'll deprecate frontend mode. To try backend mode, enable the `influxdbBackendMigration` feature toggle. If you’re using Grafana Cloud and would like to enable this feature, please contact customer support.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Data sources",
        "InfluxDB backend mode"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 274,
        "lineEnd": 275,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L274-L275"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b2e1d865c73a2a60867a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When you're browsing logs in Explore, you can now click the eye icon within a row to replace the log line's contents with the value of one or more of the log fields or labels. This is helpful for scanning through your logs.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Explore",
        "Logs: Choose which fields to display in a log line"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 285,
        "lineEnd": 285,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L285-L285"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.958a397ae3d69786e3a9",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Log context allows you to view additional lines surrounding a specific log entry. With this enhancement, you can access as many log lines as needed within the log context. As you scroll through the logs, Grafana dynamically loads more log lines, ensuring a seamless and continuous viewing experience.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Explore",
        "Logs: See more log lines in log context"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
