    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4ecf7e1324317ad39ec0",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This update facilitates file provisioning and maintenance for notification policies. The feature implements the provisioning API export endpoints for exporting notification policies as well as adding an export button to the root notification policy in the UI.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Alerting",
        "Notification policies",
        "Notification policy provisioning file export"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 380,
        "lineEnd": 380,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L380-L380"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.915b913f2e87410a7173",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We've added support for different time zones and locations as well as a visual selector for week days, made improvements to loading and error handling, and provided better validation for time ranges.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Alerting",
        "Alert management",
        "Support for time zones in mute timings"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 388,
        "lineEnd": 388,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L388-L388"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ed7ec380c7943e3a010a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Previously, if no organization role mapping was found for a user when they connected using OAuth, Grafana didn’t update the user’s organization role.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "OAuth role mapping enforcement"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 406,
        "lineEnd": 406,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L406-L406"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d01a14161bcc22bf42d1",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Now, on every login, if the `role_attribute_path` property doesn't return a role, then the user is assigned the role specified by the `auto_assign_org_role` option or the default role for the organization, which is Viewer by default.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "OAuth role mapping enforcement"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 408,
        "lineEnd": 408,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L408-L408"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8ca121896943cad48be5",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To avoid overriding manually set roles, enable the `skip_org_role_sync` option in the Grafana configuration for your OAuth provider before affected users log in for the first time.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "OAuth role mapping enforcement"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 410,
        "lineEnd": 410,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L410-L410"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.16ac7bdf0b9051e6d886",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This change impacts all instances that use an external authentication provider and have role mapping enabled.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Prevent manual role updates for externally synced roles"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 418,
        "lineEnd": 418,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L418-L418"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c3c911b938fd6902d72b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Previously, it was possible to manually update a user's organization role (Viewer, Editor, Admin, or Grafana Admin) even if this role was managed by an external authentication provider. This means that roles could be manually set for the duration of a user's session, but were overridden by the external authentication provider the next time the user logged in. If the `onlyExternalOrgRoleSync` feature toggle was enabled, only then were manual role updates for externally managed roles not allowed.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Prevent manual role updates for externally synced roles"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 420,
        "lineEnd": 422,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L420-L422"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f09e28c5bc3c6ad8bcb0",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Now, you can no longer manually update externally managed organization roles. We've removed the `onlyExternalOrgRoleSync` feature toggle, and have defaulted to locking the organization role of users authenticated by an external provider.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Prevent manual role updates for externally synced roles"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 424,
        "lineEnd": 425,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L424-L425"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d2287286d6f20e4f44bb",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you prefer to manage your users' organization roles manually, enable the `skip_org_role_sync` option in the Grafana configuration for your authentication provider.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Prevent manual role updates for externally synced roles"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 427,
        "lineEnd": 427,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L427-L427"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3f93078898bbe9e60b3e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana now supports GitLab OIDC through the `GitLab` OAuth provider in addition to the existing `GitLab` OAuth2 provider. This allows you to use GitLab OIDC to authenticate users in Grafana.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "GitLab OIDC support"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 437,
        "lineEnd": 437,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L437-L437"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4689fe8e860fbfbcdac7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This change also allows Grafana to reduce the access scope to only the required scopes for authentication and authorization, instead of full read API access.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "GitLab OIDC support"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 439,
        "lineEnd": 440,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L439-L440"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.181899085dc96edf82b0",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To learn how to migrate your GitLab OAuth2 setup to OIDC, refer to our [GitLab authentication documentation](../../setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/gitlab/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "GitLab OIDC support"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 442,
        "lineEnd": 442,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L442-L442"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.340a5dcc56eeb07a7ef1",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana now supports Google OIDC through the `Google` OAuth provider in addition to the existing `Google` OAuth2 provider. This allows you to use Google OIDC to authenticate users in Grafana, which in turn, lets Grafana reduce the access scope to only the required scopes for authentication and authorization.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Google OIDC and Team Sync support"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 450,
        "lineEnd": 450,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L450-L450"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.56a8d8286538f8e29f06",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This release also adds support for Google OIDC in Team Sync. You can now easily add users to teams by using their Google groups.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Google OIDC and Team Sync support"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
        "lineStart": 452,
        "lineEnd": 452,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md#L452-L452"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0d786b29dde4b4973b4d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To learn how to migrate your Google OAuth2 setup to OIDC and how to set up Team Sync, refer to our [Google authentication documentation](../../setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/google/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.1",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Google OIDC and Team Sync support"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1cce8d3829f244debae74e6d7e86f19383fbe67b",
        "sha256": "40a1d463d9e4ed934cc589acc91dd3389003b006f1e2c5413c162996faf92d1a",
