    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d39df71d153c08d37234",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Public dashboards allow you to share your visualizations and insights with a broader audience without the requirement of a login. You can effortlessly use our current sharing model and create a public dashboard URL to share with anyone using the generated public URL link. To learn more, refer to the [Public dashboards documentation](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/dashboards/share-dashboards-panels/shared-dashboards), as well as the following video demo:",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Share your dashboard with the world: Public dashboards are generally available"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 49,
        "lineEnd": 49,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L49-L49"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8981e90ca0c8881cca21",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Introducing Content Outline in Grafana Explore. It's easy to lose track of your place when you're running complex mixed queries or switching between logs and traces. Content outline is our first step towards seamless navigation from log lines to traces and back to queries, ensuring quicker searches while preserving context. Experience efficient, contextual investigations with this update in Grafana Explore. To learn more, refer to the [Content outline documentation](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/explore/#content-outline), as well as the following video demo.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Navigate lengthy, mixed data in Explore with Content Outline"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 59,
        "lineEnd": 59,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L59-L59"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.01f42fd40577c5daca6b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana Correlations is a new public preview feature you can use to establish links from any data source query to any other, carrying forward data like namespace, host, or label values. This is extremely powerful for performing root cause analysis with a diverse set of data sources. For more information, refer to [the documentation](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/administration/correlations/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Correlations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 65,
        "lineEnd": 65,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L65-L65"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4e2d545323d633cdb533",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Creating correlations has just become easier. Try out our new correlations editor in Explore by selecting the **+ Add > Add correlation** option from the top bar or from the command palette. The editor shows all possible places where you can place data links and guides you through building and testing target queries. For more information, refer to [the documentation](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/administration/correlations/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Correlations",
        "Create Correlations the easy way in Grafana Explore"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
