    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.191a77cfc04d1989a7de",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can now zoom in on the y-axis of your time series and candlestick visualizations. This is useful when you want to focus on a specific range of values. To zoom in on the y-axis on supported visualizations, hold the Shift key while clicking and dragging; double-click to reset the zoom.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Dashboards and visualizations",
        "Zoom in on the y-axis of the time series and candlestick visualizations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 143,
        "lineEnd": 143,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L143-L143"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.073cb45233200b49fe50",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When visualizing multiple fields with a wide spread of values, calculating the min or max value of the visualization based on all fields can hide useful details.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Dashboards and visualizations",
        "Calculate visualization min/max individually per field"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 153,
        "lineEnd": 153,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L153-L153"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c729809e3635eec13458",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Now, you can automatically calculate the min or max of each visualized field based on the lowest and highest value of the individual field. This setting is available in the standard options of most visualizations.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Dashboards and visualizations",
        "Calculate visualization min/max individually per field"
      ],
      "source": {
