    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3c08927019c8efadf6ab",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The [TraceQL query editor](https://grafana.com/docs/tempo/latest/traceql/#traceql-query-editor) has been improved to facilitate the creation of TraceQL queries. In particular, it now features improved autocompletion, syntax highlighting, and error reporting.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Data sources and querying",
        "Tempo data source",
        "Query traces more easily with the Improved TraceQL editor"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 222,
        "lineEnd": 222,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L222-L222"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.5d51e9a8bda54cbeafa3",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The [TraceQL query editor](https://grafana.com/docs/tempo/<TEMPO_VERSION>/traceql/#traceql-query-editor) has been improved to facilitate the grouping of multiple spans per trace in TraceQL queries. For example, when `by(resource.service.name)` is added to your TraceQL query, it will group the spans in each trace by `resource.service.name`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Data sources and querying",
        "Tempo data source",
        "Group multiple spansets per trace"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 232,
        "lineEnd": 232,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L232-L232"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1a249557a4a0a6cf5e69",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The Tempo data source now supports query-type template variables. With this update, you can create variables for which the values are a list of attribute names or attribute values seen on spans received by Tempo.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Data sources and querying",
        "Tempo data source",
        "Create query-type template variables for the Tempo data source"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 242,
        "lineEnd": 242,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L242-L242"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3965563f53887aaa5c36",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The SAP HANA® data source now supports tenant database connections by using the database name and/or instance number. This is helpful because these are less likely to change than the port for your database. For more information, refer to our [SAP HANA® configuration documentation](/docs/plugins/grafana-saphana-datasource/latest/#configuration).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Data sources and querying",
        "SAP HANA®: Configure your data source with tenant database instance name and number"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 254,
        "lineEnd": 254,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L254-L254"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4e8729dadc5adb1fd48b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The Datadog data source now supports log aggregation. This feature helps aggregate logs/events into buckets and compute metrics and time series. For more information, refer to [Datadog log aggregation](/docs/plugins/grafana-datadog-datasource/latest#logs-analytics--aggregation).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Data sources and querying",
        "Datadog: Aggregate logs to compute metrics and time series"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 264,
        "lineEnd": 264,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L264-L264"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6511a4497740bb2ec354",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In the Datadog data source, you can now block API requests for metric queries based on upstream rate limits. With this update, you can set a rate limit percentage at which the plugin stops sending queries.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Data sources and querying",
        "Datadog: Rate-limit requests from the Datadog data source"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 274,
        "lineEnd": 274,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L274-L274"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.43878573594e7c9e315b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To learn more, refer to [Datadog data source settings](/docs/plugins/grafana-datadog-datasource/latest#configure-the-data-source), as well as the following video demo.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Data sources and querying",
        "Datadog: Rate-limit requests from the Datadog data source"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 276,
        "lineEnd": 276,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L276-L276"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3bcfa1bcc62ad0b8158d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We've added support for Azure Authentication (Service principal/MSI) on our MS SQL plugin to authenticate and allow querying of content stored in SQL Managed Instance databases.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Data sources and querying",
        "Microsoft SQL Server: Support for Azure Authentication (Service principal/MSI)"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 286,
        "lineEnd": 286,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L286-L286"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9f411c60ad1e292ce628",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Enable this feature by setting the `managed_identity_enabled` property to `true` under the `Azure` heading in your configuration file (/conf/<your_config_file>.ini). Then take the following steps in your Microsoft SQL Server data source configuration UI:",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Data sources and querying",
        "Microsoft SQL Server: Support for Azure Authentication (Service principal/MSI)"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 288,
        "lineEnd": 288,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L288-L288"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d3140e4e3aa9897fcf3f",
      "syntaxRole": "procedural-step",
      "sourceText": "1. Under **Authentication**, select **Azure AD Authentication** in the drop-down to reveal the **Azure Authentication Settings** section.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Data sources and querying",
        "Microsoft SQL Server: Support for Azure Authentication (Service principal/MSI)"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 290,
        "lineEnd": 290,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L290-L290"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.de351990d7b95b30d9e6",
      "syntaxRole": "procedural-step",
      "sourceText": "2. In this section, select either **Managed Identity** or **App Registration**.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Data sources and querying",
        "Microsoft SQL Server: Support for Azure Authentication (Service principal/MSI)"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
