    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9a73e75b742be5810ff5",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We've added initial support to detect situations in which various transformations won't work appropriately based on current data. Previously, selecting the appropriate transformation and configuring it correctly required a process of trial and error or already knowing how a given transformation worked. Now, transformations that we've detected can't be used are shaded in the interface to indicate this, along with a helpful message explaining why.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Transformations",
        "See which transformations will work with your data"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 356,
        "lineEnd": 356,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L356-L356"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.62b98ac62f64b62bcf50",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you have the `transformationsRedesign` feature flag set, you'll be able to access this functionality right away. If you'd like to try it, enable this feature flag in your [Grafana configuration](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/setup-grafana/configure-grafana/#feature_toggles).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Transformations",
        "See which transformations will work with your data"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 360,
        "lineEnd": 360,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L360-L360"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.bd1273efa44536d909f7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We've added support for setting timezones manually when formatting times as strings using the **Format time** and **Convert field type** transformations. This allows times to be formatted relative to any timezone across the globe.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Transformations",
        "Choose your timezome in the Format time and Convert field type transformations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 368,
        "lineEnd": 368,
