    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ec24a6654e1ee5935d74",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Use the Grafana Alerting - Grafana OnCall integration to effortlessly connect alerts generated by Grafana Alerting with Grafana OnCall. From there, you can route them according to defined escalation chains and schedules.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Alerting",
        "Grafana OnCall integration for Alerting"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 380,
        "lineEnd": 380,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L380-L380"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a821d4662838cd9568ca",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To learn more, refer to the [Grafana OnCall integration for Alerting documentation](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/alerting/configure-notifications/manage-contact-points/integrations/configure-oncall/), as well as the following video demo.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Alerting",
        "Grafana OnCall integration for Alerting"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 382,
        "lineEnd": 382,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L382-L382"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8144c3a4065d1f54faac",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Export your alerting resources, such as alert rules, contact points, and notification policies as Terraform resources. A new “Modify export” mode for alert rules enables you to edit provisioned alert rules and export a modified version.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Alerting",
        "Export alerting resources to Terraform"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 392,
        "lineEnd": 392,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L392-L392"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3912ebee2c0c9f88f123",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We've added support for the Microsoft Teams contact points when using an external Alertmanager.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Alerting",
        "Additional contact points for external Alertmanager"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 400,
        "lineEnd": 400,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L400-L400"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.46cb75c6007058118081",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We're excited to introduce the \"No basic role,\" a new basic role with no permissions. A basic role in Grafana dictates the set of actions a user or entity can perform, known as permissions. This new role is especially beneficial if you're aiming for tailored, customized RBAC permissions for your service accounts or users. You can set this as a basic role through the API or UI.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "No basic role"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 408,
        "lineEnd": 408,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L408-L408"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9fcf3174d874be357f19",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "[Service accounts](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/administration/service-accounts/) allow you to create tokens to access Grafana's API and dashboards. Service accounts are a powerful tool for authenticating with Grafana's API and accessing data sources. However, without proper access controls, service accounts can pose a security risk to your Grafana instance. In Grafana 10.2, we've added new tools to limit service accounts to just the resources they need to access.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "New service account permissions"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 416,
        "lineEnd": 416,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L416-L416"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.631cbb14f3cafc895157",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In this release, we've added the ability to assign dashboard and folder permissions to service accounts. This means that you can now create a service account that can be used to access a specific dashboard and nothing else.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "New service account permissions",
        "Add dashboard and folder permissions to service accounts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 424,
        "lineEnd": 425,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L424-L425"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.055365b8cba5724b5b8c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This is useful if you want to limit the access service accounts have to your Grafana instance.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "New service account permissions",
        "Add dashboard and folder permissions to service accounts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 427,
        "lineEnd": 427,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L427-L427"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0e62e3e4caebfc3a3194",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana 10.2 also introduces the ability to assign _data source_ permissions to service accounts, for Grafana CLoud and Enterprise users. With this feature, you can create a service account that has access to a specific data source and nothing else. This is useful in scenarios where you want to limit the access service accounts have to your Grafana instance.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "New service account permissions",
        "Add data source permissions to service accounts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 437,
        "lineEnd": 439,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L437-L439"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.af758ce906656bc90311",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For example, imagine you have a team of developers who need to access a specific data source to develop a new feature. Instead of giving them full access to your Grafana instance, you can create a service account that has access only to that data source. This way, you can limit the potential damage that could be caused by a compromised service account.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "New service account permissions",
        "Add data source permissions to service accounts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 441,
        "lineEnd": 443,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L441-L443"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9d721a6f9f7d31654845",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can now map Google groups to Grafana organizational roles when using Google OIDC. This is useful if you want to limit the access users have to your Grafana instance.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Role mapping support for Google OIDC"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 455,
        "lineEnd": 456,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L455-L456"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c314c0192de7da3d601a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We've also added support for controlling allowed groups when using Google OIDC.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Role mapping support for Google OIDC"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 458,
        "lineEnd": 458,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L458-L458"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.edd3ed60aba34fa1df73",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Refer to the [Google Authentication documentation](http://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/google/) to learn how to use these new options.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Role mapping support for Google OIDC"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 460,
        "lineEnd": 460,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L460-L460"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c6aa7e145d24569babef",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "With Grafana v9.3, we introduced a [feature toggle](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/setup-grafana/configure-grafana/feature-toggles/) called `accessTokenExpirationCheck`. It improves the security of Grafana by checking the expiration of the access token and automatically refreshing the expired access token when a user is logged in using one of the OAuth providers.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Configure refresh token handling separately for OAuth providers"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 468,
        "lineEnd": 468,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L468-L468"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.bec8f457c4925fea6b6c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "With the current release, we've introduced a new configuration option for each OAuth provider called `use_refresh_token` that allows you to configure whether the particular OAuth integration should use refresh tokens to automatically refresh access tokens when they expire. In addition, to further improve security and provide secure defaults, `use_refresh_token` is enabled by default for providers that support either refreshing tokens automatically or client-controlled fetching of refresh tokens. It's enabled by default for the following OAuth providers: `AzureAD`, `GitLab`, `Google`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Configure refresh token handling separately for OAuth providers"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 470,
        "lineEnd": 470,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L470-L470"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.76a9c688a80baa2865f2",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For more information on how to set up refresh token handling, please refer to [the documentation of the particular OAuth provider.](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.2",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Configure refresh token handling separately for OAuth providers"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7d4ec24043eb9bcda5315a42539dff326de3311d",
        "sha256": "7b87afe9eb18608849e77d623cc25d90d705d2d30805424878e3a2ce9d2c71b5",
        "lineStart": 472,
        "lineEnd": 472,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-2.md#L472-L472"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
