    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e1766f9898cd7f7af0f6",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can now plot enum values in your time series and state timeline visualizations. This feature is useful when you want to visualize the state of a system, such as the status of a service or the health of a device. For example, you can use this feature to visualize the status of a service as `ON`, `STANDBY`, or `OFF`. To display enum values you can [use the convert field transform](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/panels-visualizations/query-transform-data/transform-data/#convert-field-type).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.3",
        "Dashboards and visualizations",
        "Plot enum values in your time series and state timeline visualizations\\*"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e43fdcd331e25519da2fbdea223ad59ec4f7ad4c",
        "sha256": "0e1c94c3c83b280306b5bf6a8543bb3a2707c17132691f3d48d3818f08b029c7",
        "lineStart": 150,
        "lineEnd": 150,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md#L150-L150"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4c7059848e86f9d1721b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can now view percent change in stat visualizations. This makes it easier to understand your data by showing how metrics are changing over time.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.3",
        "Dashboards and visualizations",
        "View percent change in stat visualizations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e43fdcd331e25519da2fbdea223ad59ec4f7ad4c",
        "sha256": "0e1c94c3c83b280306b5bf6a8543bb3a2707c17132691f3d48d3818f08b029c7",
        "lineStart": 160,
        "lineEnd": 160,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md#L160-L160"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c2e0746778f325e5de5d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can now apply data transformations to annotation data. For example, you can now configure how exemplar data is displayed in tooltips.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.3",
        "Dashboards and visualizations",
        "View percent change in stat visualizations",
        "Apply data transformations to annotations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e43fdcd331e25519da2fbdea223ad59ec4f7ad4c",
        "sha256": "0e1c94c3c83b280306b5bf6a8543bb3a2707c17132691f3d48d3818f08b029c7",
        "lineStart": 172,
        "lineEnd": 172,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md#L172-L172"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c2ce1be275fd3c463b31",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In the past, transformations were applied through a dropdown menu, indicated solely by text names like Merge, Sort, JoinByLabels, etc. Now, we've introduced a much more user-friendly interface. A convenient drawer allows seamless access to all transformation options, each accompanied by visual/graphical representations and a brief description. These enhancements are designed to enhance the user's comprehension of their data transformation choices.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.3",
        "Dashboards and visualizations",
        "New Transformations UI experience and documentation upgrades",
        "Improved UI\\*"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e43fdcd331e25519da2fbdea223ad59ec4f7ad4c",
        "sha256": "0e1c94c3c83b280306b5bf6a8543bb3a2707c17132691f3d48d3818f08b029c7",
        "lineStart": 186,
        "lineEnd": 186,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md#L186-L186"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b35aafa9e0855fdea774",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We've also streamlined the user experience by integrating documentation directly into the core Grafana application. Gone are the days of navigating to a separate browser page for Transformation documentation. Now, users can conveniently access documentation within the app interface, providing a more seamless and efficient way to understand and utilize various features. This enhancement aims to save time and enhance user convenience, ensuring that valuable information is readily available at their fingertips.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.3",
        "Dashboards and visualizations",
        "New Transformations UI experience and documentation upgrades",
        "In-App documentation"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e43fdcd331e25519da2fbdea223ad59ec4f7ad4c",
        "sha256": "0e1c94c3c83b280306b5bf6a8543bb3a2707c17132691f3d48d3818f08b029c7",
        "lineStart": 192,
        "lineEnd": 192,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md#L192-L192"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.cf1b7bf478275555d361",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Copying and pasting time range in the time range picker is now available. For example, you can copy a time range in **Explore** and paste it into **Dashboards** and vice versa. You can also copy and paste a time range using the new keyboard shortcuts `t+c` and `t+v`, respectively.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.3",
        "Dashboards and visualizations",
        "Copy and paste time range"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e43fdcd331e25519da2fbdea223ad59ec4f7ad4c",
        "sha256": "0e1c94c3c83b280306b5bf6a8543bb3a2707c17132691f3d48d3818f08b029c7",
        "lineStart": 202,
        "lineEnd": 202,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md#L202-L202"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d9a6dc434047ec499be7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Using Trace to profiles, you can use Grafana’s ability to correlate different signals by adding the functionality to link between traces and profiles.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.3",
        "Profiles",
        "Trace to Profiles\\*"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e43fdcd331e25519da2fbdea223ad59ec4f7ad4c",
        "sha256": "0e1c94c3c83b280306b5bf6a8543bb3a2707c17132691f3d48d3818f08b029c7",
        "lineStart": 212,
        "lineEnd": 212,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md#L212-L212"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7dd9bd1bca5e6895841e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "**Trace to profiles** lets you link your Grafana Pyroscope data source to tracing data. When configured, this connection lets you run queries from a trace span into the profile data.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.3",
        "Profiles",
        "Trace to Profiles\\*"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e43fdcd331e25519da2fbdea223ad59ec4f7ad4c",
        "sha256": "0e1c94c3c83b280306b5bf6a8543bb3a2707c17132691f3d48d3818f08b029c7",
        "lineStart": 214,
        "lineEnd": 214,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md#L214-L214"
