        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.72bb93917ce0c698b7df",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Loki's line filter syntax is great to find specific substrings of your log lines. If users want to find multiple different substrings it was cumbersome to use the regex `=~` operator. With this change it is possible to chain multiple strings with the existing filter operators.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.3",
        "Data sources",
        "Loki data source improvements: \"or\" filter syntax, filter by label types, derived fields by labels",
        "Line filter \"or\" syntax\\*"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e43fdcd331e25519da2fbdea223ad59ec4f7ad4c",
        "sha256": "0e1c94c3c83b280306b5bf6a8543bb3a2707c17132691f3d48d3818f08b029c7",
        "lineStart": 350,
        "lineEnd": 350,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md#L350-L350"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4c9232cd956a4be8da64",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana users can use the action buttons in the log details to filter for specific labels. Those would be always added as a LabelFilter expression regardless of the type of the label. Now, filtered labels will be added either to the stream selector if the label is an indexed label, or as a LabelFilter expression if the label is a parsed label or part of structured metadata.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.3",
        "Data sources",
        "Loki data source improvements: \"or\" filter syntax, filter by label types, derived fields by labels",
        "Filter based on label type\\*"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e43fdcd331e25519da2fbdea223ad59ec4f7ad4c",
        "sha256": "0e1c94c3c83b280306b5bf6a8543bb3a2707c17132691f3d48d3818f08b029c7",
        "lineStart": 360,
        "lineEnd": 360,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md#L360-L360"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f53baba72f3ab70b9b2c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Derived fields or data links are a concept to add correlations based on your log lines. Previously it was only possible to add derived fields based on a regular expression of your log line and doing it based on labels was not possible. With this change derived fields can be added either based on a regex of a log line or based on a label, parsed label or structured metadata.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.3",
        "Data sources",
        "Loki data source improvements: \"or\" filter syntax, filter by label types, derived fields by labels",
        "Derived fields based on labels\\*"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e43fdcd331e25519da2fbdea223ad59ec4f7ad4c",
        "sha256": "0e1c94c3c83b280306b5bf6a8543bb3a2707c17132691f3d48d3818f08b029c7",
        "lineStart": 364,
        "lineEnd": 364,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md#L364-L364"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3ce89ad0f752e2fa780b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The following example would add the derived field `traceID regex` based on a regular expression and another `app label` field based on the `app` label.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.3",
        "Data sources",
        "Loki data source improvements: \"or\" filter syntax, filter by label types, derived fields by labels",
        "Derived fields based on labels\\*"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e43fdcd331e25519da2fbdea223ad59ec4f7ad4c",
        "sha256": "0e1c94c3c83b280306b5bf6a8543bb3a2707c17132691f3d48d3818f08b029c7",
        "lineStart": 366,
        "lineEnd": 366,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md#L366-L366"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.71baac922f349883e3cf",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "InfluxDB introduced [a new version, 3.0](https://www.influxdata.com/blog/introducing-influxdb-3-0/), in April. With this new version, InfluxDB has put [Flux in maintenance mode](https://www.influxdata.com/blog/the-plan-for-influxdb-3-0-open-source/#heading4). But with the new version we have a new querying language, [Native SQL](https://www.influxdata.com/products/sql/). With v10.3.0, Grafana has built-in support for SQL query language in InfluxDB.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.3",
        "Data sources",
        "InfluxDB native SQL support"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e43fdcd331e25519da2fbdea223ad59ec4f7ad4c",
        "sha256": "0e1c94c3c83b280306b5bf6a8543bb3a2707c17132691f3d48d3818f08b029c7",
        "lineStart": 376,
        "lineEnd": 376,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md#L376-L376"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4c0fa7c54c00cac1dd3a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "All you need to do is set up your InfluxDB Cloud Account and create your InfluxDB data source on Grafana with the query language \"SQL\" selected.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.3",
        "Data sources",
        "InfluxDB native SQL support"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e43fdcd331e25519da2fbdea223ad59ec4f7ad4c",
        "sha256": "0e1c94c3c83b280306b5bf6a8543bb3a2707c17132691f3d48d3818f08b029c7",
        "lineStart": 378,
        "lineEnd": 378,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md#L378-L378"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.abc6260342d1f6211dc5",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We've identified a need for users who enable anonymous authentication to monitor the anonymous devices connected to their Grafana instance. This feature is part of our ongoing efforts to enhance control and transparency regarding anonymous usage.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.3",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Grafana Anonymous Access\\*"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e43fdcd331e25519da2fbdea223ad59ec4f7ad4c",
        "sha256": "0e1c94c3c83b280306b5bf6a8543bb3a2707c17132691f3d48d3818f08b029c7",
        "lineStart": 390,
        "lineEnd": 390,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md#L390-L390"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9c9e81950eee18f6cc3d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Anonymous access now allows users, including those in open-source and enterprise self-managed environments, to view and monitor their anonymous access. They can also set a device limit, configuring a specific number of anonymous devices to connect to their instance.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.3",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Grafana Anonymous Access\\*"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e43fdcd331e25519da2fbdea223ad59ec4f7ad4c",
        "sha256": "0e1c94c3c83b280306b5bf6a8543bb3a2707c17132691f3d48d3818f08b029c7",
        "lineStart": 392,
        "lineEnd": 392,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md#L392-L392"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.635c27dd451dc740ab33",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When anonymous access has been enabled, any device which accesses Grafana in the last 30 days (without logging in) is considered an active anonymous device. Users can now view anonymous devices on the users page, anonymous usage statistics, including the count of devices and users over this period.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v10.3",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Grafana Anonymous Access\\*"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e43fdcd331e25519da2fbdea223ad59ec4f7ad4c",
        "sha256": "0e1c94c3c83b280306b5bf6a8543bb3a2707c17132691f3d48d3818f08b029c7",
        "lineStart": 400,
        "lineEnd": 400,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v10-3.md#L400-L400"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f7ef55f423a44e56a3b1",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- Navigate to Administration -> Users to access the anonymous devices tab.",
