    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a58b632823c2e713eb55",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can now choose to keep the last evaluated state of an alert rule when that rule produces \"No Data\" or \"Error\" results. Simply choose the \"Keep Last State\" option for no data or error handling when editing a rule. Refer to the Alerting documentation on state and health of alert rules for more information.[](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/alerting/fundamentals/alert-rules/state-and-health/#state-and-health-of-alert-rules)",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.0",
        "Alerting",
        "Keep Last State for Grafana Managed Alerting"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-0.md",
