      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.74ab8ad4e92e1b439765",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Fetching a rule group no longer requires the **datasources:query** permission for every data source used by the rules within that group. Now, the only requirements are **alert.rules:read** and **folders:read** for the folder the group is contained in.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.1",
        "Alerting",
        "Removes requirement of datasources:query permission for reading rules"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-1.md",
