    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e8d02eccd7b3be647cb9",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When setting up Grafana with Azure AD using the SAML protocol, the Azure AD Graph API sometimes returns a follow-up Graph API call rather than the information itself. This is the case for users who belong to more than 150 groups when using SAML.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.2",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Better SAML integration for Azure AD"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ceccf569bb3670f6d3ae8c4db9fa3befbb8ef80a",
        "sha256": "e3947d9db32859fc717703f21b781da2366f7e2bda8dcfaeb51f1812ec5a1342",
        "lineStart": 265,
        "lineEnd": 265,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-2.md#L265-L265"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.795f14b98a74dc371d89",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Please refer to our [documentation](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/saml/#configure-a-graph-api-application-in-azure-ad) on how to set up an Azure AD registered application for this setup.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.2",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Better SAML integration for Azure AD"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ceccf569bb3670f6d3ae8c4db9fa3befbb8ef80a",
        "sha256": "e3947d9db32859fc717703f21b781da2366f7e2bda8dcfaeb51f1812ec5a1342",
        "lineStart": 269,
        "lineEnd": 269,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-2.md#L269-L269"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b4331204f9066af487f7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "[The SSO settings API](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/developers/http_api/sso-settings/) has been updated to include support for LDAP settings. This feature is experimental behind the feature flag `ssoSettingsLDAP`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.2",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "API support for LDAP configuration"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ceccf569bb3670f6d3ae8c4db9fa3befbb8ef80a",
        "sha256": "e3947d9db32859fc717703f21b781da2366f7e2bda8dcfaeb51f1812ec5a1342",
        "lineStart": 277,
        "lineEnd": 277,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-2.md#L277-L277"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.de80133c2f11450b89a1",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You will soon be able to configure LDAP from the UI and Terraform.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.2",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "API support for LDAP configuration"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ceccf569bb3670f6d3ae8c4db9fa3befbb8ef80a",
        "sha256": "e3947d9db32859fc717703f21b781da2366f7e2bda8dcfaeb51f1812ec5a1342",
        "lineStart": 279,
        "lineEnd": 279,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-2.md#L279-L279"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.db24d2965cba6c6a29d0",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The private key and certificate fields are no longer mandatory in the SAML form. To configure SAML without providing a private key and a certificate you have to opt out from using signed requests.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.2",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Reduce number of required fields from the SAML form"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ceccf569bb3670f6d3ae8c4db9fa3befbb8ef80a",
        "sha256": "e3947d9db32859fc717703f21b781da2366f7e2bda8dcfaeb51f1812ec5a1342",
        "lineStart": 287,
        "lineEnd": 287,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-2.md#L287-L287"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f46e871208c05568e1c7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can generate a new certificate and private key for SAML directly from the UI form. Click on the **Generate key and certificate** button from the **Sign requests** tab in the SAML form and then fill in the information you want to be embedded in your generated certificate.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.2",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Generate SAML certificate and private key"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ceccf569bb3670f6d3ae8c4db9fa3befbb8ef80a",
        "sha256": "e3947d9db32859fc717703f21b781da2366f7e2bda8dcfaeb51f1812ec5a1342",
        "lineStart": 297,
        "lineEnd": 297,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-2.md#L297-L297"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.403d046a9c187541d4e0",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Welcome to Grafana 11.3! Scenes-powered dashboards are now generally available and the Explore Logs plugin is now installed by default. The dashboard experience has also improved in other ways including the ability to trigger API calls from any canvas element with the new **Actions** option and an update to transformations so you can apply calculations to dynamic fields. We've also simplified the alert setup experience, added customizable announcement banners that admins can send to all users, and improved some default permissions.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.3"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "5eb55341a0458eac320b2317223af815e066d128",
        "sha256": "42f0fbcea86ed7f49f166bc9b279b95673f27c4ef505737f7b54ede18c391332",
        "lineStart": 23,
        "lineEnd": 23,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md#L23-L23"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.dbcf5a2598ae6d8886cd",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For even more detail about all the changes in this release, refer to the [changelog](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md). For the specific steps we recommend when you upgrade to v11.3, check out our [Upgrade Guide](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v11.3/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.3"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "5eb55341a0458eac320b2317223af815e066d128",
        "sha256": "42f0fbcea86ed7f49f166bc9b279b95673f27c4ef505737f7b54ede18c391332",
        "lineStart": 27,
        "lineEnd": 27,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md#L27-L27"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.da2d5daeaf11d2fad3c5",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For the past few months we've been working on a major update of our **Dashboards** architecture and migrated it to the Scenes library. This migration provides us with more stable, dynamic, and flexible dashboards as well as setting the foundation for what we envision the future of Grafana dashboards will be. Here are four of the improvements that are being introduced as part of this work:",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.3",
        "Scenes-powered Dashboards are generally available"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "5eb55341a0458eac320b2317223af815e066d128",
        "sha256": "42f0fbcea86ed7f49f166bc9b279b95673f27c4ef505737f7b54ede18c391332",
        "lineStart": 35,
        "lineEnd": 35,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md#L35-L35"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.836e60b1983223239d3b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "It can be difficult to efficiently navigate through the visually cluttered options during the dashboard editing process. When in View mode, the dashboard screen is less clutteed. In Edit mode, options like adding a panel and changing settings are easier to access.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.3",
        "Scenes-powered Dashboards are generally available"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "5eb55341a0458eac320b2317223af815e066d128",
        "sha256": "42f0fbcea86ed7f49f166bc9b279b95673f27c4ef505737f7b54ede18c391332",
        "lineStart": 39,
        "lineEnd": 39,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md#L39-L39"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c8ea097156ed509669cd",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We've added a new time zone URL parameter, `tz`. This allows sharing dashboards with a selected time zone, ensuring that the receiver views it in the intended time zone regardless of their local settings.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.3",
        "Scenes-powered Dashboards are generally available"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "5eb55341a0458eac320b2317223af815e066d128",
        "sha256": "42f0fbcea86ed7f49f166bc9b279b95673f27c4ef505737f7b54ede18c391332",
        "lineStart": 47,
        "lineEnd": 47,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md#L47-L47"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.028a904058372aad8cf0",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When playing a playlist or displaying a dashboard in full screen, you can see controls by default. These controls include the time range picker, refresh button, variables, annotations, and links.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.3",
        "Scenes-powered Dashboards are generally available"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "5eb55341a0458eac320b2317223af815e066d128",
        "sha256": "42f0fbcea86ed7f49f166bc9b279b95673f27c4ef505737f7b54ede18c391332",
        "lineStart": 51,
        "lineEnd": 51,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md#L51-L51"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.28994fe6abf0e4d6a842",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you prefer to hide these controls during playlist playback, new configuration options are available when starting a playlist. You can choose which controls to display while the playlist is running.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.3",
        "Scenes-powered Dashboards are generally available"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "5eb55341a0458eac320b2317223af815e066d128",
        "sha256": "42f0fbcea86ed7f49f166bc9b279b95673f27c4ef505737f7b54ede18c391332",
        "lineStart": 53,
        "lineEnd": 53,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md#L53-L53"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2eee445f8c8fb1f4cd7f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For configuring controls outside of playlist playback, you can use the following URL parameters:",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.3",
        "Scenes-powered Dashboards are generally available"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md",
