    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f4038ff5ef980224cee5",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When the **Cell inspect value** switch is toggled on, clicking the inspect icon in a cell opens the drawer. Grafana attempts to automatically detect the type of data in the cell and opens the drawer with the associated tab showing. However, you can switch back and forth between tabs.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.3",
        "Additional dashboard and visualization improvements",
        "Auto-formatted table cell values in Cell Inspect"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "5eb55341a0458eac320b2317223af815e066d128",
        "sha256": "42f0fbcea86ed7f49f166bc9b279b95673f27c4ef505737f7b54ede18c391332",
        "lineStart": 87,
        "lineEnd": 87,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md#L87-L87"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f6c7f78b53948e4a7ee6",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We've updated canvas visualizations so that now you can add actions to canvas elements, like opening an issue in GitHub or calling any API. The **Selected element** configuration now includes a **Data links and actions** section where you can add actions to elements. Each action can be configured to call an API endpoint.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.3",
        "Additional dashboard and visualization improvements",
        "Canvas actions"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "5eb55341a0458eac320b2317223af815e066d128",
        "sha256": "42f0fbcea86ed7f49f166bc9b279b95673f27c4ef505737f7b54ede18c391332",
        "lineStart": 99,
        "lineEnd": 99,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md#L99-L99"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.cf3567a93e24635d1d48",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Actions can also be configured to be triggered with a single click. To enable this functionality, select **Action** under the one **One-click** section in the **Selected element** data links and actions option. If there are multiple actions for an element, the first action in the list has the one-click functionality.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.3",
        "Additional dashboard and visualization improvements",
        "Canvas actions"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "5eb55341a0458eac320b2317223af815e066d128",
        "sha256": "42f0fbcea86ed7f49f166bc9b279b95673f27c4ef505737f7b54ede18c391332",
        "lineStart": 101,
        "lineEnd": 101,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md#L101-L101"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7978bbf52c4f55f5162a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To try out this feature, enable the `vizActions` feature toggle.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.3",
        "Additional dashboard and visualization improvements",
        "Canvas actions"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "5eb55341a0458eac320b2317223af815e066d128",
        "sha256": "42f0fbcea86ed7f49f166bc9b279b95673f27c4ef505737f7b54ede18c391332",
        "lineStart": 107,
        "lineEnd": 107,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md#L107-L107"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.cf9ebfdc725430d76481",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We've added legend support to bar gauge visualizations. This is part an effort to standardize legends and make them available across more panels. You can customize legends by navigating to the **Legend** section in panel options. By default, the legend is disabled.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.3",
        "Additional dashboard and visualization improvements",
        "Legend support in bar gauge visualizations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "5eb55341a0458eac320b2317223af815e066d128",
        "sha256": "42f0fbcea86ed7f49f166bc9b279b95673f27c4ef505737f7b54ede18c391332",
        "lineStart": 115,
        "lineEnd": 115,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md#L115-L115"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c9be516530663d126b2a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can also hide names in each bar gauge, since they are redundant to the legend. To do that, in the **Name placement** option, choose **Hidden**.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.3",
        "Additional dashboard and visualization improvements",
        "Legend support in bar gauge visualizations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "5eb55341a0458eac320b2317223af815e066d128",
        "sha256": "42f0fbcea86ed7f49f166bc9b279b95673f27c4ef505737f7b54ede18c391332",
        "lineStart": 117,
        "lineEnd": 117,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md#L117-L117"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f6f0c4d5fb51d858e7f4",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When you set up a binary operation using the **Add field from calculation** transformation (for example, dividing each column by a certain value), there's a new **All number fields** option available to select. Use this to apply a mathematical operator to multiple number fields simultaneously. This feature is particularly useful when you're scaling or offsetting data containing multiple, dynamically-named fields, allowing the transformation to be applied when dealing with unknown field names.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.3",
        "Additional dashboard and visualization improvements",
        "Apply the same binary transformation to all the number fields in a given table at once"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "5eb55341a0458eac320b2317223af815e066d128",
        "sha256": "42f0fbcea86ed7f49f166bc9b279b95673f27c4ef505737f7b54ede18c391332",
