      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c99973ffa6a87620b174",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We're excited to announce that plugins can now leverage [Grafana's role based access control](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/administration/roles-and-permissions/access-control/#about-rbac) to define their own roles and permissions in order to control access to their routes.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.3",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Developers: Support RBAC in Plugins"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "5eb55341a0458eac320b2317223af815e066d128",
        "sha256": "42f0fbcea86ed7f49f166bc9b279b95673f27c4ef505737f7b54ede18c391332",
        "lineStart": 306,
        "lineEnd": 306,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md#L306-L306"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ff9de473fb81fb0dc2a4",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To define roles and their default assignments, plugin developers need to add a `roles` section to their `plugin.json` file. Grafana will automatically register these roles and assign them to the corresponding basic roles: `Viewer`, `Editor`, `Admin`, and `Grafana Admin`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.3",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Developers: Support RBAC in Plugins"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "5eb55341a0458eac320b2317223af815e066d128",
        "sha256": "42f0fbcea86ed7f49f166bc9b279b95673f27c4ef505737f7b54ede18c391332",
        "lineStart": 308,
        "lineEnd": 308,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md#L308-L308"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.90768210710a9f86fb20",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Following is an example of defining two RBAC plugin roles and assigning them to Admins and Viewers (and thus Editors and Admins) by default:",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.3",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Developers: Support RBAC in Plugins"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "5eb55341a0458eac320b2317223af815e066d128",
        "sha256": "42f0fbcea86ed7f49f166bc9b279b95673f27c4ef505737f7b54ede18c391332",
        "lineStart": 310,
        "lineEnd": 310,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md#L310-L310"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.359142346ac06586fd66",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Protecting `includes` and `routes` is also straight forward, and can be done through the new `action` and `reqAction` field of these sections of the `plugin.json` file.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.3",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Developers: Support RBAC in Plugins"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "5eb55341a0458eac320b2317223af815e066d128",
        "sha256": "42f0fbcea86ed7f49f166bc9b279b95673f27c4ef505737f7b54ede18c391332",
        "lineStart": 337,
        "lineEnd": 337,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md#L337-L337"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e95ebd37ecf9c729e2ba",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you’d like to test this and explore RBAC for plugins further, refer to this [plugin example](https://github.com/grafana/grafana-plugin-examples/blob/main/examples/app-with-rbac/README.md) for guidance.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.3",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Developers: Support RBAC in Plugins"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "5eb55341a0458eac320b2317223af815e066d128",
        "sha256": "42f0fbcea86ed7f49f166bc9b279b95673f27c4ef505737f7b54ede18c391332",
        "lineStart": 341,
        "lineEnd": 341,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-3.md#L341-L341"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.845122f8ec0017af309b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Welcome to Grafana 11.4! This is a special release with one new feature, created in partnership with AWS. We’ve made improvements to Cloudwatch so you can query your logs using two additional query languages: Opensearch PPL and Opensearch SQL. We’ve also updated the querying experience by providing a sample of commonly-used queries, syntax highlighting in the query editor, and auto-completion suggestions for complex queries. Read on to learn more about this new feature.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.4"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ff6306de7c085c6f60b76342b28a90dd56436181",
        "sha256": "bda6f351b80b05a96a1c92d145f63bbb236b4be43910384abff78b5c0c89014a",
        "lineStart": 23,
        "lineEnd": 23,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-4.md#L23-L23"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8d29e3ab1188d2bbd3dc",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For even more detail about all the changes in this release, refer to the [changelog](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md). For the specific steps we recommend when you upgrade to v11.4, check out our [Upgrade Guide](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/upgrade-guide/upgrade-v11.4/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.4"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ff6306de7c085c6f60b76342b28a90dd56436181",
        "sha256": "bda6f351b80b05a96a1c92d145f63bbb236b4be43910384abff78b5c0c89014a",
        "lineStart": 25,
        "lineEnd": 25,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-4.md#L25-L25"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b153c37f29230473fd59",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The AWS CloudWatch data source plugin now offers two new query languages for searching through logs: OpenSearch PPL and OpenSearch SQL. You now have increased flexibility to choose a more familiar query language and to take advantage of their unique features (like the SQL JOIN command) when querying AWS CloudWatch Logs Insights. In addition to the already supported **Logs Insights QL** option, you can find the added query language options in the new **Query language** drop-down list.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.4",
        "Query Cloudwatch Logs Insights with PPL and SQL"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ff6306de7c085c6f60b76342b28a90dd56436181",
        "sha256": "bda6f351b80b05a96a1c92d145f63bbb236b4be43910384abff78b5c0c89014a",
        "lineStart": 33,
        "lineEnd": 33,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v11-4.md#L33-L33"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6284b52e81c2411250bf",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "![CloudWatch logs explore query languages drop-down list opened](/media/docs/grafana/data-sources/screenshot-awscw-query-languages-v11.4.png)",
      "headingPath": [
        "What’s new in Grafana v11.4",
        "Query Cloudwatch Logs Insights with PPL and SQL"
      ],
      "source": {
