    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8180175727859226c586",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- [**Time zones** Time zone support](#time-zone-support)",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 44,
        "lineEnd": 44,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L44-L44"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.08bc2b9e0b365d52e387",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We have redesigned the UI for editing panels. The first visible change is that we have separated panel display settings to a right-hand side pane that you can collapse or expand depending on what your focus is on. With this change we are also introducing our new unified option model and UI for defining data configuration and display options. This unified data configuration system powers a consistent UI for setting data options across visualizations, as well as making all data display settings data driven and overridable.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "New panel editor and unified data model"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 48,
        "lineEnd": 48,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L48-L48"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.41d6871517d957931332",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This new option architecture and UI will make all panels have a consistent set of options and behaviors for attributes like unit, min, max, thresholds, links, decimals. Not only that but all these options will share a consistent UI for specifying override rules and is extensible for custom panel specific options.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "New panel editor and unified data model"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 50,
        "lineEnd": 50,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L50-L50"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b45ba7357da4b997d2cf",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In previous versions of Grafana, each visualization had slightly different ways to define their options. One immediate benefit is after setting options like units or thresholds in a panel, you can seamlessly switch between visualization types and keep those options. This will bring increased ease of use and more consistency for users and plugin developers.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "New panel editor and unified data model"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 52,
        "lineEnd": 52,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L52-L52"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3b87b4b92cb476a41a56",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This release adds major support for distributed tracing, including a telemetry mode to complement the existing support for metrics and logs. Traces allow you to follow how single requests travel through a distributed system. We are starting with an integrated trace viewer and two new built-in data sources: Jaeger and Zipkin.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "New tracing UI"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 60,
        "lineEnd": 60,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L60-L60"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.35428ae8d3995b7f8f97",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can use the new trace view in Explore either directly to search for a particular trace or you can configure Loki to detect trace IDs in the log lines and link directly to a trace timeline pulled from Jaeger or Zipkin data source.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "New tracing UI"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 62,
        "lineEnd": 62,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L62-L62"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2e99d8ee2f773f29f797",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In the future we will add more workflows and integrations so that correlating between metrics, logs and traces is even easier.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "New tracing UI"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 64,
        "lineEnd": 64,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L64-L64"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.876efb6f47cc833c06e2",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The data you want to visualize can come from many different places and it is usually not in exactly the right form. Users can now transform non-time series data into tables (e.g., JSON files or even simple lookup tables) in seconds without any customization or additional overhead. They can then combine non-time series data with any other data in Grafana; data from an external database or a panel that already exists in one of their current dashboards.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Transformations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 70,
        "lineEnd": 70,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L70-L70"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0227ff855074a9286cdd",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "By chaining a simple set of point and click [transformations](../../panels-visualizations/query-transform-data/transform-data/#transformation-functions), users will be able join, pivot, filter, re-name and do calculations to get the results they need. Perfect for operations across queries or data sources missing essential data transformations.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Transformations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 72,
        "lineEnd": 72,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L72-L72"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.bdfe70cc730fb3387ed3",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "[Transformations](../../panels-visualizations/query-transform-data/transform-data/) also adds the ability to do math across queries. Lots of data sources do not support this natively, so being able to do it in Grafana is a powerful feature.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Transformations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 74,
        "lineEnd": 74,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L74-L74"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6d26f32b72de962d5553",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For users with large dashboards or with heavy queries, being able to reuse the query result from one panel in another panel can be a huge performance gain for slow queries (e.g log or sql queries). From the data source menu in the query editor, you can choose the `--dashboard--` option and then choose the query result from another panel on the same dashboard.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Transformations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 76,
        "lineEnd": 76,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L76-L76"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.184948f44b0f599a14fe",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Reduce:** Reduce all rows or data points to a single value using a function like max, min, mean or last.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Transformations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 84,
        "lineEnd": 84,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L84-L84"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4fff55dd6c3df8c588ce",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Filter by name:** Removes part of the query results using a regex pattern. The pattern can be inclusive or exclusive.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Transformations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 85,
        "lineEnd": 85,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L85-L85"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.782f3baad708a8931cc3",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Filter data by query** Filter data by query. This is useful if you are sharing the results from a different panel that has many queries and you want to only visualize a subset of that in this panel.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Transformations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 86,
        "lineEnd": 86,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L86-L86"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.414d1f8d30a48bbdd308",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Organize fields:** Allows the user to re-order, hide, or rename fields / columns. Useful when data source doesn't allow overrides for visualizing data.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Transformations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 87,
        "lineEnd": 87,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L87-L87"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c76b85c9f1d3761d3490",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- **Labels to fields:** Groups series by time and returns labels or tags as fields. Useful for showing time series with labels in a table where each label key becomes a separate column.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Transformations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
