        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d32072614941417390b1",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "With Grafana 7.0 we are introducing a new, unified data configuration system that powers a consistent UI for setting data options across visualizations as well as making all data display settings data driven and overridable. This new option architecture and UI will make all panels have a consistent set of options and behaviors for attributes like `unit`, `min`, `max`, `thresholds`, `links`, `decimals` or `value mappings`. Not only that but all these options will share a consistent UI for specifying override rules and is extensible for custom panel specific options.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Field options and overrides"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 96,
        "lineEnd": 96,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L96-L96"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.53f6394c924bc826c567",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Up until now the overrides were available only for Graph and Table panel(via Column Styles), but with 7.0 they work consistently across all visualization types and plugins.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Field options and overrides"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 98,
        "lineEnd": 98,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L98-L98"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "conditional-or-paid-restriction-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.13607422e9270efaa908",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Learn more about this feature in [Field overrides](../../panels-visualizations/configure-overrides/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Field options and overrides"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 102,
        "lineEnd": 102,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L102-L102"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d685f111550ff0ef7eb4",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Another new feature of Grafana 7.0 is the panel inspector. Inspect allows you to view the raw data for any Grafana panel as well as export that data to a CSV file. With Panel inspect you will also be able to perform simple raw data transformations like join, view query stats or detailed execution data.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Inspect panels and export data to CSV"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 108,
        "lineEnd": 108,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L108-L108"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.dfa81951a860bc82ad90",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Learn more about this feature in [Panel Inspector](../../panels-visualizations/panel-inspector/#inspect-query-request-and-response-data).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Inspect panels and export data to CSV"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 110,
        "lineEnd": 110,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L110-L110"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.575e308fbf62208e1b8d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana 7.0 comes with a new table panel (and deprecates the old one). This new table panel supports horizontal scrolling and column resize. Paired with the new `Organize fields` transformation detailed above you can reorder, hide & rename columns. This new panel also supports new cell display modes, like showing a bar gauge inside a cell.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Table panel"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 116,
        "lineEnd": 116,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L116-L116"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.15591db67aed902ac294",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This new 7.0 feature is for the gauge and stat panels. Before, stat and gauge only supported horizontal or vertical stacking: The auto layout mode just selected vertical or horizontal stacking based on the panel dimensions (whatever was highest). But in 7.0 the auto layout for these two panels will allow dynamic grid layouts where Grafana will try to optimize the usage of space and lay out each sub-visualization in a grid.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Auto grid mode for Stat panel and Gauge"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 123,
        "lineEnd": 123,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L123-L123"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9e5d12f7b9aff724bbe9",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana 7.0 adds logging support to one of our most popular cloud provider data sources. Autocomplete support for Cloudwatch Logs queries is included for improved productivity. There is support for deep linking to the CloudWatch Logs Insights console for log queries, similar to the deep linking feature for Cloudwatch metrics. Since CloudWatch Logs queries can return time series data, for example through the use of the `stats` command, alerting is supported too.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Cloudwatch Logs"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 130,
        "lineEnd": 130,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L130-L130"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6f5468632fb4dac3113a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The [platform for plugins](/developers/plugin-tools/) has been completely re-imagined and provides ready-made components and tooling to help both inexperienced and experienced developers get up and running more quickly. The tooling, documentation, and new components will improve plugin quality and reduce long-term maintenance. We are already seeing that a high quality plugin with the Grafana look and feel can be written in much fewer lines of code than previously.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Plugins platform"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 134,
        "lineEnd": 134,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L134-L134"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1524e0bef23246eda34f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Plugins can use the same React components that the Grafana team uses to build Grafana. Using these components means the Grafana team will support and improve them continually and make your plugin as polished as the rest of Grafana’s UI. The new [`@grafana/ui` components library](https://developers.grafana.com/ui) is documented with Storybook (visual documentation) and is available on NPM.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Plugins platform",
        "Front end plugins platform"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 142,
        "lineEnd": 142,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L142-L142"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0940ba4940e4beaf1508",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The `@grafana/data`, `@grafana/runtime`, `@grafana/e2e packages` (also available via NPM) aim to simplify the way plugins are developed. We want to deliver a set of [reliable APIs](/docs/grafana/v7.0/packages_api/) for plugin developers.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Plugins platform",
        "Front end plugins platform"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 144,
        "lineEnd": 144,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L144-L144"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.de561c3ec6877ce52b94",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana now officially supports [backend plugins](https://grafana.com/developers/plugin-tools/key-concepts/backend-plugins/) and the first type of plugin to be introduced is a backend component for data source plugins. You can optionally add a backend component to your data source plugin and implement the query logic there to automatically enable alerting in Grafana for your plugin. In the 7.0 release, we introduce the [Grafana Plugin SDK for Go](https://grafana.com/developers/plugin-tools/key-concepts/backend-plugins/grafana-plugin-sdk-for-go) that enables and simplifies building a backend plugin in [Go](https://golang.org/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Plugins platform",
        "Support for backend plugins"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 150,
        "lineEnd": 150,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L150-L150"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8fa743158c1cdf8f731a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Plugins can be monitored with the new metrics and health check capabilities. The new Resources capability means backend components can return non-time series data like JSON or static resources like images and opens up Grafana for new use cases.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Plugins platform",
        "Support for backend plugins"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 152,
        "lineEnd": 152,
