    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.5f83cf0634822dec5e5f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Depending on the cardinality of the data and the time range MetricTank may return rolled up (aggregated) data. This can be as subtle as potentially only 1 or 2 graphs out of nine being rolled up. The new rollup indicator is visible in the panel title and you can also inspect extensive metadata and stats about the Metrictank query result and its rollups.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Rollup indicator for Metrictank queries"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 171,
        "lineEnd": 171,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L171-L171"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.128507db835e1a720074",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "[PhantomJS](https://phantomjs.org/), have been used for rendering images of dashboards and panels and have been included with Grafana since Grafana v2.0. Since then we’ve had a lot of related bugs and security related issues, mainly due to the fact that PhantomJS have struggled with supporting modern web technologies. Throughout the years, maintaining PhantomJS support in Grafana has been a nightmare. Removing support for PhantomJS has been a high priority for the Grafana project and got stressed even more when the PhantomJS maintainer in March 2018 [announced](https://github.com/ariya/phantomjs/issues/15344) the end of the project.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Breaking change - PhantomJS removed"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 177,
        "lineEnd": 177,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L177-L177"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.990dc7f0a64caf594edd",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Since then we have been working towards removing PhantomJS. In October 2019, when Grafana v6.4 was released, we [announced](/blog/2019/10/02/grafana-v6.4-released/#phantomjs-deprecation) the deprecation of PhantomJS. Grafana v7.0 removes all PhantomJS support which means that Grafana distribution no longer will include a built-in image renderer.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Breaking change - PhantomJS removed"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 179,
        "lineEnd": 179,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L179-L179"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e35cff97aa9560537036",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "As a replacement for PhantomJS we’ve developed the [Grafana Image Renderer plugin](/grafana/plugins/grafana-image-renderer) which is a plugin that runs on the backend and handles rendering panels and dashboards as PNG images using headless Chromium/Chrome. The [Grafana Image Renderer plugin](/grafana/plugins/grafana-image-renderer) can either be installed as a Grafana plugin running in its own process side-by-side with Grafana. or runs as an external HTTP service, hosted using Docker or as a standalone application.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Breaking change - PhantomJS removed"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 181,
        "lineEnd": 181,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L181-L181"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d53dbea6e381576d8488",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The Query history feature lets you view and interact with the queries that you have previously run in Explore. You can add queries to the Explore query editor, write comments, create and share URL links, star your favorite queries, and much more. Starred queries are displayed in the Starred tab, so it is easier to reuse queries that you run often without typing them from scratch.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Query history in Explore out of beta"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 187,
        "lineEnd": 187,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L187-L187"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.fa907b07379e520a45ec",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "It was released as a beta feature in Grafana 6.7. The feedback has been really positive and it is now out of beta for the 7.0 release. Learn more about query history in [Explore](../../explore/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Query history in Explore out of beta"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 189,
        "lineEnd": 189,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L189-L189"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b1fe012a90c29a3ee03d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "[Service monitoring](https://cloud.google.com/service-monitoring) in Google Cloud Platform (GCP) enables you to monitor based on Service Level Objectives (SLOs) for your GCP services. The new SLO query builder in the Stackdriver data source allows you to display SLO data in Grafana. Read more about it in the [Stackdriver data source documentation](../../datasources/google-cloud-monitoring/#slo-service-level-objective-queries).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Stackdriver data source supports Service Monitoring"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 193,
        "lineEnd": 193,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L193-L193"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.46f63de2dd573a977635",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can now override the [time zone](../../dashboards/manage-dashboards/#dashboard-time-settings) used to display date and time values in a dashboard. One benefit of this is that you can specify the local time zone of the service or system that you are monitoring which can be helpful when monitoring a system or service that operates across several time zones.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Time zone support"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 197,
        "lineEnd": 197,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L197-L197"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b790d831003ef6527555",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The Azure Monitor data source supports multiple Azure services. Log Analytics queries in the data source now have alerting support too (Azure Monitor and Application Insights already had alerting support).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Alerting and deep linking for Azure Log Analytics"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 201,
        "lineEnd": 201,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L201-L201"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a6435a3f0a32fb4d2792",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "A new feature is [deep linking from the graph panel to the Log Analytics query editor in the Azure Portal](../../datasources/azure-monitor/#deep-link-from-grafana-panels-to-the-log-analytics-query-editor-in-azure-portal). Click on a time series in the panel to see a context menu with a link to View in Azure Portal. Clicking that link opens the Azure Log Analytics query editor in the Azure Portal and runs the query from the Grafana panel.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.0",
        "Alerting and deep linking for Azure Log Analytics"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f8a2dff1665364c77c678ce11827aaa9c6f62083",
        "sha256": "4e6c2d51a33ed64dd73b0f776a7c738b03a4cd0e49ad15073950a020ec0f53f0",
        "lineStart": 203,
        "lineEnd": 203,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-0.md#L203-L203"
      },
      "applicability": {
