    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.bf09b07cfe86811f9df8",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Support for Flux and Influx v2 has been added. The InfluxData blog post, [How to Build Grafana Dashboards with InfluxDB, Flux and InfluxQL](https://www.influxdata.com/blog/how-grafana-dashboard-influxdb-flux-influxql/) explains the changes in depth.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.1",
        "Influx data source"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c998b5d236f80c5daa3f097010e0000e828868c1",
        "sha256": "14a4ecbed46fade8d4764c9fcadd120a6a9d0369fc4df5e10a41fd0c335c6e97",
        "lineStart": 44,
        "lineEnd": 44,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-1.md#L44-L44"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.fe9a6c912accaa213bbd",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In Grafana v 7.1 we are introducing search functionality in Query history. You can search across queries and your comments. It is especially useful in combination with a time filter and data source filter. Read more about [Query history here](../../explore/#query-history).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.1",
        "Query history search"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c998b5d236f80c5daa3f097010e0000e828868c1",
        "sha256": "14a4ecbed46fade8d4764c9fcadd120a6a9d0369fc4df5e10a41fd0c335c6e97",
        "lineStart": 48,
        "lineEnd": 48,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-1.md#L48-L48"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ca4d8b06cd5119919f83",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana 7.1 includes a major change to Explore: it removes the query mode selector.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.1",
        "Explore modes unified"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c998b5d236f80c5daa3f097010e0000e828868c1",
        "sha256": "14a4ecbed46fade8d4764c9fcadd120a6a9d0369fc4df5e10a41fd0c335c6e97",
        "lineStart": 54,
        "lineEnd": 54,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-1.md#L54-L54"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e734f6d9b8b62cf7717d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Many data sources tell Grafana whether a response contains time series data or logs data. Using this information, Explore chooses which visualization to use for that data. This means that you don't need to switch back and forth between Logs and Metrics modes depending on the type of query that you want to make.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.1",
        "Explore modes unified"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c998b5d236f80c5daa3f097010e0000e828868c1",
        "sha256": "14a4ecbed46fade8d4764c9fcadd120a6a9d0369fc4df5e10a41fd0c335c6e97",
        "lineStart": 56,
        "lineEnd": 56,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-1.md#L56-L56"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e86a383ec9630f96b35f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The new internal linking feature for Elasticsearch allows you to link to other data sources from your logs. You can now create links in Elastic configuration that point to another data source (similar to an existing feature in Loki). An example would be using a traceID field from your logs to be able to link to traces in a tracing data source like Jaeger.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.1",
        "Internal links for Elasticsearch"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c998b5d236f80c5daa3f097010e0000e828868c1",
        "sha256": "14a4ecbed46fade8d4764c9fcadd120a6a9d0369fc4df5e10a41fd0c335c6e97",
        "lineStart": 60,
        "lineEnd": 60,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-1.md#L60-L60"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7f67dddb24619885dcb0",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We have added a new **Merge on time** transform that can combine many time series or table results. Unlike the join transform, this combines the result into one table even when the time values do not align / match.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.1",
        "Transformations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c998b5d236f80c5daa3f097010e0000e828868c1",
        "sha256": "14a4ecbed46fade8d4764c9fcadd120a6a9d0369fc4df5e10a41fd0c335c6e97",
        "lineStart": 64,
        "lineEnd": 64,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-1.md#L64-L64"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3580d4684689fcc8ae24",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "[Ad hoc filtering](../../dashboards/variables/add-template-variables/#add-ad-hoc-filters), a way to automatically add filters to queries without having to define template variables is now supported in the new Table panel.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.1",
        "Ad hoc filtering in the new table panel"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-1.md",
