      "id": "grafana.candidate.6e3dc0cfda8ff977e423",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Support for multiple dimensions has been added to all services in the Azure Monitor datasource. This means you can now group by more than one dimension with time series queries. With the Kusto based services, Log Analytics and Application Insights Analytics, you can also select multiple metrics as well as multiple dimensions.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.1",
        "Azure Monitor data source"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c998b5d236f80c5daa3f097010e0000e828868c1",
        "sha256": "14a4ecbed46fade8d4764c9fcadd120a6a9d0369fc4df5e10a41fd0c335c6e97",
        "lineStart": 91,
        "lineEnd": 91,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-1.md#L91-L91"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8fcb3eea3eb90bdc4e2a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Additionally, the Raw Edit mode for Application Insights Analytics has been replaced with a new service in the drop-down for the data source and is called Insights Analytics. The new query editor behaves in the same way as Log Analytics.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.1",
        "Azure Monitor data source"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c998b5d236f80c5daa3f097010e0000e828868c1",
        "sha256": "14a4ecbed46fade8d4764c9fcadd120a6a9d0369fc4df5e10a41fd0c335c6e97",
        "lineStart": 93,
        "lineEnd": 93,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-1.md#L93-L93"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.54cea9cb8b9d9b63b572",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "A new feature in Grafana 7.1 is [deep linking from Grafana panels to the Metrics Explorer in Google Cloud Console](../../datasources/google-cloud-monitoring/#deep-linking-from-grafana-panels-to-the-metrics-explorer-in-google-cloud-console). Click on a time series in the panel to see a context menu with a link to View in Metrics explorer in Google Cloud Console. Clicking that link opens the Metrics explorer in the Monitoring Google Cloud Console and runs the query from the Grafana panel there.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.1",
        "Deep linking for Google Cloud Monitoring (formerly named Google Stackdriver) data source"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c998b5d236f80c5daa3f097010e0000e828868c1",
        "sha256": "14a4ecbed46fade8d4764c9fcadd120a6a9d0369fc4df5e10a41fd0c335c6e97",
        "lineStart": 97,
        "lineEnd": 97,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-1.md#L97-L97"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f5b4896dae884d7f5876",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "With 7.1 we are updating the dashboard's time range picker to allow time zone selection. You no longer need to go to dashboard settings to change the dashboard's time zone.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.1",
        "Time range picker update"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c998b5d236f80c5daa3f097010e0000e828868c1",
        "sha256": "14a4ecbed46fade8d4764c9fcadd120a6a9d0369fc4df5e10a41fd0c335c6e97",
        "lineStart": 101,
        "lineEnd": 101,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-1.md#L101-L101"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.35717fbb6f6fd6f58fd5",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The time zone picker itself also got UX improvements. Now you can search for the timezone using country or city name, time zone abbreviations, or UTC offsets.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.1",
        "Time range picker update"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c998b5d236f80c5daa3f097010e0000e828868c1",
        "sha256": "14a4ecbed46fade8d4764c9fcadd120a6a9d0369fc4df5e10a41fd0c335c6e97",
        "lineStart": 103,
        "lineEnd": 103,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-1.md#L103-L103"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e00ceb0c73a1550cd36f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can now use HashiCorp Vault to get secrets for configuration and provisioning of Grafana Enterprise. For more information about HashiCorp Vault, refer to [vault](../../setup-grafana/configure-security/configure-database-encryption/integrate-with-hashicorp-vault/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.1",
        "Grafana Enterprise features",
        "Support for HashiCorp Vault"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c998b5d236f80c5daa3f097010e0000e828868c1",
        "sha256": "14a4ecbed46fade8d4764c9fcadd120a6a9d0369fc4df5e10a41fd0c335c6e97",
        "lineStart": 111,
        "lineEnd": 111,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-1.md#L111-L111"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "What's new in Grafana v7.1 > Grafana Enterprise features > Support for HashiCorp Vault"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2c93f25c8a765b59a37c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "With Grafana Enterprise 7.1, you can generate reports on a [monthly schedule](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/visualizations/dashboards/create-reports/#2-schedule).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.1",
        "Grafana Enterprise features",
        "Support for monthly schedules in reports"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-1.md",
