    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d965b32e5d9c4d0691a1",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The Azure Monitor query type was renamed to Metrics and Azure Logs Analytics was renamed to Logs to match the service names in Azure and align the concepts with the rest of Grafana.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.4",
        "Grafana OSS features",
        "Azure Monitor updates"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "10f50eec0a661654510f63805294c24968acadad",
        "sha256": "edb4cc6f7fd075796d11237820052a62e2220cdfb904cbc4c113af5f6734066d",
        "lineStart": 152,
        "lineEnd": 152,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-4.md#L152-L152"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.fe67761d239c4a88993d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can now use Monitoring Query Language (MQL) for querying time-series data. MQL provides an expressive, text-based interface to retrieve, filter, and manipulate time-series data.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.4",
        "Grafana OSS features",
        "MQL support added for Google Cloud Monitoring"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "10f50eec0a661654510f63805294c24968acadad",
        "sha256": "edb4cc6f7fd075796d11237820052a62e2220cdfb904cbc4c113af5f6734066d",
        "lineStart": 158,
        "lineEnd": 158,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-4.md#L158-L158"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7cb9de2a6027d738286e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Unlike the visual query builder, MQL allows you to control the time range and period of output data, create new labels to aggregate data, compute the ratio of current values to past values, and so on.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.4",
        "Grafana OSS features",
        "MQL support added for Google Cloud Monitoring"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "10f50eec0a661654510f63805294c24968acadad",
        "sha256": "edb4cc6f7fd075796d11237820052a62e2220cdfb904cbc4c113af5f6734066d",
        "lineStart": 160,
        "lineEnd": 160,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-4.md#L160-L160"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.320251334ab55c84e985",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "MQL uses a set of operations and functions. Operations are linked together using the common pipe mechanism, where the output of one operation becomes the input to the next. Linking operations makes it possible to build up complex queries incrementally.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.4",
        "Grafana OSS features",
        "MQL support added for Google Cloud Monitoring"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "10f50eec0a661654510f63805294c24968acadad",
        "sha256": "edb4cc6f7fd075796d11237820052a62e2220cdfb904cbc4c113af5f6734066d",
        "lineStart": 162,
        "lineEnd": 162,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-4.md#L162-L162"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ef83fccba030d0f01ce9",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Once query type Metrics is selected in the Cloud Monitoring query editor, you can toggle between the editor modes for visual query builder and MQL. For more information, refer to the [Google Cloud Monitoring docs](../../datasources/google-cloud-monitoring/#import-pre-configured-dashboards).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.4",
        "Grafana OSS features",
        "MQL support added for Google Cloud Monitoring"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "10f50eec0a661654510f63805294c24968acadad",
        "sha256": "edb4cc6f7fd075796d11237820052a62e2220cdfb904cbc4c113af5f6734066d",
        "lineStart": 164,
        "lineEnd": 164,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-4.md#L164-L164"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.542c54e5b834baaff477",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Google Cloud Monitoring data source ships with pre-configured dashboards for some of the most popular GCP services. These curated dashboards are based on similar dashboards in the GCP dashboard samples repository. In this release, we have expanded the set of pre-configured dashboards.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.4",
        "Curated dashboards for Google Cloud Monitoring"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "10f50eec0a661654510f63805294c24968acadad",
        "sha256": "edb4cc6f7fd075796d11237820052a62e2220cdfb904cbc4c113af5f6734066d",
        "lineStart": 170,
        "lineEnd": 170,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-4.md#L170-L170"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a34e6679e3e0a0550255",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you want to customize a dashboard, we recommend that you save it under a different name. Otherwise the dashboard will be overwritten when a new version of the dashboard is released.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.4",
        "Curated dashboards for Google Cloud Monitoring"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "10f50eec0a661654510f63805294c24968acadad",
        "sha256": "edb4cc6f7fd075796d11237820052a62e2220cdfb904cbc4c113af5f6734066d",
        "lineStart": 174,
        "lineEnd": 174,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-4.md#L174-L174"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4f8b12649220e46d5a32",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For more information, refer to the [Google Cloud Monitoring docs](../../datasources/google-cloud-monitoring/#import-pre-configured-dashboards).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.4",
        "Curated dashboards for Google Cloud Monitoring"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-4.md",
