        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.952f0f9f16b3538de66a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For more information on adding a query editor help component to your plugin, refer to [Add a query editor help component](https://grafana.com/developers/plugin-tools/how-to-guides/data-source-plugins/add-query-editor-help).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.4",
        "Curated dashboards for Google Cloud Monitoring",
        "Query Editor Help"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "10f50eec0a661654510f63805294c24968acadad",
        "sha256": "edb4cc6f7fd075796d11237820052a62e2220cdfb904cbc4c113af5f6734066d",
        "lineStart": 184,
        "lineEnd": 184,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-4.md#L184-L184"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1a6bf44fe71cb80fa76a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The variables list has an additional column indicating whether variables are referenced in queries and panel names or not. The dependencies graph provides an easy way to check variable dependencies. You can click on a variable name within the graph to make updates to the variable as needed.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.4",
        "Curated dashboards for Google Cloud Monitoring",
        "Variable inspector"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "10f50eec0a661654510f63805294c24968acadad",
        "sha256": "edb4cc6f7fd075796d11237820052a62e2220cdfb904cbc4c113af5f6734066d",
        "lineStart": 188,
        "lineEnd": 188,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-4.md#L188-L188"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0568c6fb2ec50a084049",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When determining a user’s role for billing purposes, a user who has the ability to edit and save dashboards is considered an Editor. This includes any user who is an Editor or Admin at the Org level, and who has granted Admin or Edit permissions via [Dashboard permissions](../../administration/user-management/manage-dashboard-permissions/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.4",
        "Grafana Enterprise features",
        "Licensing changes"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "10f50eec0a661654510f63805294c24968acadad",
        "sha256": "edb4cc6f7fd075796d11237820052a62e2220cdfb904cbc4c113af5f6734066d",
        "lineStart": 198,
        "lineEnd": 198,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-4.md#L198-L198"
      },
