    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.56c84c4c30be74411a1b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We have upgraded AngularJS from version 1.6.6 to 1.8.2. Due to this upgrade some old angular plugins might stop working and will require a small update. This is due to the deprecation and removal of pre-assigned bindings. So if your custom angular controllers expect component bindings in the controller constructor you need to move this code to an $onInit function. For more details on how to migrate AngularJS code open the migration guide and search for pre-assigning bindings.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.4",
        "Breaking changes",
        "Plugin compatibility"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "10f50eec0a661654510f63805294c24968acadad",
        "sha256": "edb4cc6f7fd075796d11237820052a62e2220cdfb904cbc4c113af5f6734066d",
        "lineStart": 238,
        "lineEnd": 238,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-4.md#L238-L238"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7aeec8fc61177e8c601d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In order not to break all angular panel plugins and data sources we have some custom angular inject behavior that makes sure that bindings for these controllers are still set before constructor is called so many old angular panels and data source plugins will still work.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.4",
        "Breaking changes",
        "Plugin compatibility"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "10f50eec0a661654510f63805294c24968acadad",
        "sha256": "edb4cc6f7fd075796d11237820052a62e2220cdfb904cbc4c113af5f6734066d",
        "lineStart": 240,
        "lineEnd": 240,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-4.md#L240-L240"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2cec0feb5d69585ccfc7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In order to minimize the confusion with Constant variable usage, we've removed the ability to make Constant variables visible. This change will also migrate all existing visible Constant variables to Textbox variables because which we think this is a more appropriate type of variable for this use case.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.4",
        "Breaking changes",
        "Fixes Constant variable persistence confusion"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "10f50eec0a661654510f63805294c24968acadad",
        "sha256": "edb4cc6f7fd075796d11237820052a62e2220cdfb904cbc4c113af5f6734066d",
        "lineStart": 244,
        "lineEnd": 244,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-4.md#L244-L244"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.786a70c0513789ebdd4c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This topic includes the release notes for Grafana v7.5. For all details, read the full [CHANGELOG.md](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.5"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-5.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1f762193f381b785ad3976e03c8d01c40a0022d5",
        "sha256": "16b32d97207c71fd11291c626f8e3a3697a2a6efe831270739f398e87132cc21",
        "lineStart": 24,
        "lineEnd": 24,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-5.md#L24-L24"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.543437066085e0332513",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana 7.5 comes with alerting support for Loki. With LogQL you can wrap a log query with the functions that allow for creating metrics out of the logs, such as \"rate()\". Metric queries can then be used to calculate things such as the rate of error messages. [When combined with log parsers](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H9z2V0Ib1q0), they can be used to calculate metrics from a value within the log line, such latency or request size.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.5",
        "Grafana OSS features",
        "Alerting for Loki"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-5.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1f762193f381b785ad3976e03c8d01c40a0022d5",
        "sha256": "16b32d97207c71fd11291c626f8e3a3697a2a6efe831270739f398e87132cc21",
        "lineStart": 40,
        "lineEnd": 40,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-5.md#L40-L40"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.53d2672cd98f17d36004",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "With alerting support for Loki, you can now create alerts on Loki metrics queries.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.5",
        "Grafana OSS features",
        "Alerting for Loki"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-5.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1f762193f381b785ad3976e03c8d01c40a0022d5",
        "sha256": "16b32d97207c71fd11291c626f8e3a3697a2a6efe831270739f398e87132cc21",
        "lineStart": 42,
        "lineEnd": 42,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-5.md#L42-L42"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.13d0e1f303e5eed34a96",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "A new Loki logs browser lets you construct the queries step by step: you choose labels that you like to consider, such as \"job\", then you select the values that you like, such as \"my-app1\". Note that you can select values from more than one label, and that they get facetted. This means only possible label combinations are selectable. When you're done, you can run the query either as a logs or a metrics query (a metrics query returns the log volume in a chart).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.5",
        "Grafana OSS features",
        "Loki label browser"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-5.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1f762193f381b785ad3976e03c8d01c40a0022d5",
        "sha256": "16b32d97207c71fd11291c626f8e3a3697a2a6efe831270739f398e87132cc21",
        "lineStart": 50,
        "lineEnd": 50,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-5.md#L50-L50"
      },
      "applicability": {
