    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.5ad06309ebf0f5b50af4",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- Support for region eu-south-1 has been added to the CloudWatch data source. New metrics have also been added to the namespaces AWS/Timestream, AWS/RDS (RDS Proxy metrics), AWS/NetworkFirewall, AWS/GroundStation, and AWS/DDoSProtection. Many thanks to [relvira](https://github.com/relvira), [ilyastoli](https://github.com/ilyastoli), and [rubycut](https://github.com/rubycut) for contributing!",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.5",
        "Grafana OSS features",
        "Cloudwatch data source enhancements"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-5.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1f762193f381b785ad3976e03c8d01c40a0022d5",
        "sha256": "16b32d97207c71fd11291c626f8e3a3697a2a6efe831270739f398e87132cc21",
        "lineStart": 92,
        "lineEnd": 92,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-5.md#L92-L92"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.82ccf9942dcb165081e7",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- Added a page limit to the List Metrics API call to improve speed and reduce memory consumption. You can change this limit by entering a higher value in [list_metrics_page_limit](../../setup-grafana/configure-grafana/#list-metrics-page-limit) in the Grafana configuration file.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.5",
        "Grafana OSS features",
        "Cloudwatch data source enhancements"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-5.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1f762193f381b785ad3976e03c8d01c40a0022d5",
        "sha256": "16b32d97207c71fd11291c626f8e3a3697a2a6efe831270739f398e87132cc21",
        "lineStart": 93,
        "lineEnd": 93,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-5.md#L93-L93"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.419bfcc2c457ae2bdac5",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- You can now enable or disable authentication providers and assume a role other than default by changing the [allowed_auth_providers](../../setup-grafana/configure-grafana/#allowed_auth_providers) and [assume_role_enabled](../../setup-grafana/configure-grafana/#assume_role_enabled) options in the Grafana configuration file. By default, the allowed authentication providers are _AWS SDK Default_, _Access and secret key_, and _Credentials File_, and role is _Assume role (ARN)_.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.5",
        "Grafana OSS features",
        "Cloudwatch data source enhancements"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-5.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1f762193f381b785ad3976e03c8d01c40a0022d5",
        "sha256": "16b32d97207c71fd11291c626f8e3a3697a2a6efe831270739f398e87132cc21",
        "lineStart": 94,
        "lineEnd": 94,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-5.md#L94-L94"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ad1432469705f7fe56e0",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- You can now specify a custom endpoint in the CloudWatch data source configuration page. This field is optional, and if it is left empty, then the default endpoint for CloudWatch is used. By specifying a regional endpoint, you can reduce request latency.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.5",
        "Grafana OSS features",
        "Cloudwatch data source enhancements"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-5.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1f762193f381b785ad3976e03c8d01c40a0022d5",
        "sha256": "16b32d97207c71fd11291c626f8e3a3697a2a6efe831270739f398e87132cc21",
        "lineStart": 95,
        "lineEnd": 95,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-5.md#L95-L95"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.30917ee8ae9af09fa93c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In previous versions, when querying metrics for Service Level Objectives (SLOs) in the CloudMonitoring data source, only the first 100 services were listed in the **Service** field list. To overcome this issue, the API limit for listing services has been increased to 1000.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.5",
        "Grafana OSS features",
        "Increased API limit for CloudMonitoring Services"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-5.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1f762193f381b785ad3976e03c8d01c40a0022d5",
        "sha256": "16b32d97207c71fd11291c626f8e3a3697a2a6efe831270739f398e87132cc21",
        "lineStart": 101,
        "lineEnd": 101,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-5.md#L101-L101"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3053a3ba9d0001c0df82",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We have converted Tempo to a backend data source and dropped support for tempo-query's (Jaeger) response. To configure it, you can now point to the port that is set in the Tempo configuration file.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.5",
        "Grafana OSS features",
        "Tempo as a backend data source"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-5.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1f762193f381b785ad3976e03c8d01c40a0022d5",
        "sha256": "16b32d97207c71fd11291c626f8e3a3697a2a6efe831270739f398e87132cc21",
        "lineStart": 105,
        "lineEnd": 105,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-5.md#L105-L105"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f0b2db86d22add310751",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When caching is enabled, Grafana temporarily stores the results of data source queries. When you or another user submit the same query again, the results return from the cache instead of from the data source (such as Splunk or ServiceNow).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v7.5",
        "Enterprise features",
        "Query caching"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-5.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "1f762193f381b785ad3976e03c8d01c40a0022d5",
        "sha256": "16b32d97207c71fd11291c626f8e3a3697a2a6efe831270739f398e87132cc21",
        "lineStart": 120,
        "lineEnd": 120,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v7-5.md#L120-L120"
      },
