    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.42e33fe6a1364eb2ee66",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- Removed the `never` refresh option for query variables. Existing variables will be migrated and any stored options will be removed.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.0",
        "Breaking changes",
        "Variables"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "08364874bf79c35cb3f0d907a16891c4cfb0eb1c",
        "sha256": "6f07cb510f8b0da003b838c600c8c34236d365c4cc7688913f7fe726f50a0fd7",
        "lineStart": 334,
        "lineEnd": 334,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-0.md#L334-L334"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ed1e707d5db87053e8bd",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For multi-search requests, we now use the correct application/x-ndjson content type instead of the incorrect application/json. Although this should be transparent to most of the users, if you are running Elasticsearch behind a proxy, then be sure that your proxy correctly handles requests with this content type.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.0",
        "Breaking changes",
        "Elasticsearch: Use application/x-ndjson content type for multi-search requests"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "08364874bf79c35cb3f0d907a16891c4cfb0eb1c",
        "sha256": "6f07cb510f8b0da003b838c600c8c34236d365c4cc7688913f7fe726f50a0fd7",
        "lineStart": 340,
        "lineEnd": 340,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-0.md#L340-L340"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.de3939d4cceb64894bda",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The default HTTP method for Prometheus data source is now POST, previously it was GET. The POST APIs are there since January 2018 (Prometheus 2.1.0) and they have fewer limitations than the GET APIs. Users with Prometheus instance with version < 2.1.0 that use the default HTTP method should update their HTTP method to GET.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.0",
        "Breaking changes",
        "Prometheus: Update default HTTP method to POST for existing data sources"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "08364874bf79c35cb3f0d907a16891c4cfb0eb1c",
        "sha256": "6f07cb510f8b0da003b838c600c8c34236d365c4cc7688913f7fe726f50a0fd7",
        "lineStart": 344,
        "lineEnd": 344,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-0.md#L344-L344"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7b8a93c29cb3031c022a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana 8.1 builds upon our promise of a composable, open observability platform with new panels and extends functionality launched in Grafana 8.0. We’ve got new Geomap and Annotations panels, and some great updates to the Time Series panel. We’ve also got new transformations and updates to data sources. For our enterprise customers, there are additions to fine grained access control, updates to the reporting schedule and query caching, and more. Read on to learn more.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.1"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "b54bfdf7dcc18fbe35f88f7d391c8c6f4b8f41b1",
        "sha256": "9a7f2035783113d2da54d193273dee3aed3102a8c825f1e34487836cb2423b66",
        "lineStart": 26,
        "lineEnd": 26,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-1.md#L26-L26"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1ec51e489596ccb87b0d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana 8.1 introduces the foundation for our new map panel. This new panel leverages [OpenLayers](https://openlayers.org/) and gives us a flexible solution for extending the way we use the new Geomap panel moving forward. The new Geomap panel includes multiple base layer styles (map layer options), as well as a more open data layer. The data layer can use coordinates and geo-hashed data in addition to a lookup table.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.1",
        "Geomap panel"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "b54bfdf7dcc18fbe35f88f7d391c8c6f4b8f41b1",
        "sha256": "9a7f2035783113d2da54d193273dee3aed3102a8c825f1e34487836cb2423b66",
        "lineStart": 36,
        "lineEnd": 36,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-1.md#L36-L36"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4d7d6259379d073e8f87",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The new Annotations panel shows a list of available annotations you can use to create lists of annotated data available within your organization. Various options are available to filter the list based on the tags and on the current dashboard. This panel makes it easy to find and filter annotated data within and across multiple dashboards.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.1",
        "Annotation panel"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "b54bfdf7dcc18fbe35f88f7d391c8c6f4b8f41b1",
        "sha256": "9a7f2035783113d2da54d193273dee3aed3102a8c825f1e34487836cb2423b66",
        "lineStart": 43,
        "lineEnd": 43,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-1.md#L43-L43"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.acb94a791b93908d2654",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The time series panel has been updated with the ability to color series and line by thresholds or gradient color scales. This allows users to create panels where the line color can change dynamically based on thresholds or using gradient color scales. It adds a layer of visibility to your data, making it easier to view the changes across thresholds at a glance quickly.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.1",
        "Annotation panel",
        "Time series panel updates"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "b54bfdf7dcc18fbe35f88f7d391c8c6f4b8f41b1",
        "sha256": "9a7f2035783113d2da54d193273dee3aed3102a8c825f1e34487836cb2423b66",
        "lineStart": 49,
        "lineEnd": 49,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-1.md#L49-L49"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9222b1960305e1396c30",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For more on how to configure Graphs with by value color schemes read [Graph and color schemes](../../panels-visualizations/visualizations/time-series/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.1",
        "Annotation panel",
        "Time series panel updates"
      ],
      "source": {
