    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c89ed36ac78c8b661ffb",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We’d love as much feedback as possible about this change, because we are considering making this the default behavior in a future release of Grafana.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.1",
        "Annotation panel",
        "Upcoming changes to the Select component"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "b54bfdf7dcc18fbe35f88f7d391c8c6f4b8f41b1",
        "sha256": "9a7f2035783113d2da54d193273dee3aed3102a8c825f1e34487836cb2423b66",
        "lineStart": 139,
        "lineEnd": 139,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-1.md#L139-L139"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.587bd586a8a5d457478b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We have added an experimental HA setup support for Grafana Live with Redis. This resolves the limitation when clients were connected to different Grafana instances and those instances had no shared state. For additional information, refer to [Configure Grafana Live HA setup](../../setup-grafana/set-up-grafana-live/#configure-grafana-live-ha-setup).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.1",
        "Annotation panel",
        "High availability setup support for Grafana Live"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "b54bfdf7dcc18fbe35f88f7d391c8c6f4b8f41b1",
        "sha256": "9a7f2035783113d2da54d193273dee3aed3102a8c825f1e34487836cb2423b66",
        "lineStart": 143,
        "lineEnd": 143,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-1.md#L143-L143"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6bc577aaf85404fb0154",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Role-based access control remains in beta. You can now grant or revoke permissions for Viewers, Editors, or Admins to use Explore mode, configure LDAP or SAML settings, or view the admin/stats page. These new permissions enhance the existing permissions that can be customized, namely permissions to access Users, Orgs, LDAP settings, and Reports in Grafana.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.1",
        "Enterprise features",
        "New permissions for role-based access control"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "b54bfdf7dcc18fbe35f88f7d391c8c6f4b8f41b1",
        "sha256": "9a7f2035783113d2da54d193273dee3aed3102a8c825f1e34487836cb2423b66",
        "lineStart": 151,
        "lineEnd": 151,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-1.md#L151-L151"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0d078dbf9d03144e8562",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Fine grained access control allows you to customize roles and permissions in Grafana beyond the built-in Viewer, Editor, and Admin roles. As of 8.1, you can modify some of the permissions for any of these built-in roles. This is helpful if you’d like users to have more or fewer access permissions than a given role allows for by default. For an overview of role-based access control and a complete list of available permissions, refer to the [Fine grained access control](../../administration/roles-and-permissions/access-control/) documentation.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.1",
        "Enterprise features",
        "New permissions for role-based access control"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "b54bfdf7dcc18fbe35f88f7d391c8c6f4b8f41b1",
        "sha256": "9a7f2035783113d2da54d193273dee3aed3102a8c825f1e34487836cb2423b66",
        "lineStart": 153,
        "lineEnd": 153,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-1.md#L153-L153"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.33c8ff2b66edd0d678d7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We’ve enhanced the scheduler for Reports to be more flexible, so you can send reports at just the right time. When scheduling a report, you can now choose to send a report at custom intervals such as every 4 hours or every 2 weeks. You can also send a report for a limited time period by providing a start and end date, or send a report only on weekdays or on the last day of each month. This change accompanies some other recent improvements to Reporting, like the ability to choose template variables for reports and an improved UX for authoring reports. To learn more, refer to the [reporting](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/visualizations/dashboards/create-reports/) documentation.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.1",
        "Enterprise features",
        "New and improved reporting scheduler"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "b54bfdf7dcc18fbe35f88f7d391c8c6f4b8f41b1",
        "sha256": "9a7f2035783113d2da54d193273dee3aed3102a8c825f1e34487836cb2423b66",
        "lineStart": 157,
        "lineEnd": 157,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-1.md#L157-L157"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c219f9276a64b91f7dd2",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Query caching was released in Grafana 8.0 and allows you to temporarily store the results of data source queries in a cache, so that Grafana reads repeated queries from there instead of from the data source itself. This reduces load on data sources, improves dashboard load times, and can save money for data sources that charge per query. To learn more about query caching see its [overview](../../administration/data-source-management/#query-and-resource-caching) page. To find out how to turn on encryption, refer to the [caching configuration](../../setup-grafana/configure-grafana/enterprise-configuration/#caching) documentation.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.1",
        "Enterprise features",
        "Encrypt data in the query cache"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "b54bfdf7dcc18fbe35f88f7d391c8c6f4b8f41b1",
        "sha256": "9a7f2035783113d2da54d193273dee3aed3102a8c825f1e34487836cb2423b66",
        "lineStart": 161,
        "lineEnd": 161,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-1.md#L161-L161"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.72af9aeaf3496b049323",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can now encrypt the query data cached by Grafana. This improves the security of query data, especially when your cache (like Redis) is shared with other services.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.1",
        "Enterprise features",
        "Encrypt data in the query cache"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "b54bfdf7dcc18fbe35f88f7d391c8c6f4b8f41b1",
        "sha256": "9a7f2035783113d2da54d193273dee3aed3102a8c825f1e34487836cb2423b66",
        "lineStart": 163,
        "lineEnd": 163,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-1.md#L163-L163"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.50046a6b245097666c11",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can now customize Grafana’s loading logo, which displays while Grafana is loading in a user’s browser. White labeling in Grafana Enterprise allows you to customize the look and feel of Grafana to match your product’s or company’s brand. This makes Grafana a more integrated part of your observability stack and keep Grafana consistent with other visualizations displayed in public.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.1",
        "Enterprise features",
        "White labeling for the Grafana loading logo"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "b54bfdf7dcc18fbe35f88f7d391c8c6f4b8f41b1",
        "sha256": "9a7f2035783113d2da54d193273dee3aed3102a8c825f1e34487836cb2423b66",
        "lineStart": 167,
        "lineEnd": 167,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-1.md#L167-L167"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3a45e6485422a1c68bc8",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To find out how you can configure it along with other Grafana UI elements, like the corner logo and application footer, refer to the [White labeling](../../setup-grafana/configure-grafana/configure-custom-branding/) topic of the Grafana Enterprise docs.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.1",
        "Enterprise features",
        "White labeling for the Grafana loading logo"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "b54bfdf7dcc18fbe35f88f7d391c8c6f4b8f41b1",
        "sha256": "9a7f2035783113d2da54d193273dee3aed3102a8c825f1e34487836cb2423b66",
        "lineStart": 169,
        "lineEnd": 169,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-1.md#L169-L169"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.31fcc89fe1d0859a4a86",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "With Team Sync you can map your Generic OAuth groups to teams in Grafana so that the users are automatically added to the correct teams.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.1",
        "Enterprise features",
        "Oauth2 - Team Sync to Group Mapping"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "b54bfdf7dcc18fbe35f88f7d391c8c6f4b8f41b1",
        "sha256": "9a7f2035783113d2da54d193273dee3aed3102a8c825f1e34487836cb2423b66",
        "lineStart": 173,
        "lineEnd": 173,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-1.md#L173-L173"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e5c352fa5d042fd8bf3e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana 8.2 continues to build on the foundation of Grafana 8.0 & 8.1. Grafana 8.2 also marks the start of our work to bring Grafana closer to all users with a focus on increasing Grafana’s accessibility, part of its continuing mission to democratize metrics _for everyone_.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.2"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3afee62b4a3f87040483327dc954a8953c342b5c",
        "sha256": "dcf7f229e26f311a0c0c3b5d42eb00415f636bff39eb3cac9bc5c3d848ba8005",
        "lineStart": 24,
        "lineEnd": 24,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-2.md#L24-L24"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d8f2c27927357a2f0ad4",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The plugin catalog is now on by default in Grafana 8.2. Using the plugin catalog you can now find and install official and community plugins without having to leave or restart Grafana. We’ve also updated the time picker to include configurable fiscal quarters. This update makes it easier to use Grafana to produce reports more closely aligned with common review and forecasting cycles.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.2"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3afee62b4a3f87040483327dc954a8953c342b5c",
        "sha256": "dcf7f229e26f311a0c0c3b5d42eb00415f636bff39eb3cac9bc5c3d848ba8005",
        "lineStart": 26,
        "lineEnd": 26,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-2.md#L26-L26"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.502e04b054bf13e3d017",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana Enterprise includes a revamped Stats and Licensing page, new role-based access control permissions, and improvements that make usage insights and reporting easier to access.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.2"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3afee62b4a3f87040483327dc954a8953c342b5c",
        "sha256": "dcf7f229e26f311a0c0c3b5d42eb00415f636bff39eb3cac9bc5c3d848ba8005",
        "lineStart": 28,
        "lineEnd": 28,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-2.md#L28-L28"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3d8729e7bdc02ca78422",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We’ve summarized what’s new in the release here, but you might also be interested in the announcement blog post. If you’d like all the details you can check out the [release notes](/docs/grafana/next/release-notes/release-notes-8-2-0/) and complete [CHANGELOG.md](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.2"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3afee62b4a3f87040483327dc954a8953c342b5c",
        "sha256": "dcf7f229e26f311a0c0c3b5d42eb00415f636bff39eb3cac9bc5c3d848ba8005",
        "lineStart": 30,
        "lineEnd": 30,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-2.md#L30-L30"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a5a28c675d8ef52a02c9",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana 8.2 includes a number of important community contributions including support for OAuth role mapping with GitLab accounts ([#30025](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/30025)), a new wide-to-long function ([#38670](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/38670)) included in the [prepare time series transformation](/docs/grafana/latest/panels/transformations/types-options/#prepare-time-series). A number of additions to the Azure Monitor data source were submitted, including an overview dashboard([#38801](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/38801)) and support for parsing numeric fields in the Azure Resource Graph([#38728](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/38728)). Contributions also included [regular-expression based value mapping](/docs/grafana/next/panels/value-mappings/#map-a-regular-expression) ([#38931](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/38931)) and improvements to our systemd unit for Grafana installations ([#38109](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/38109)). This list is by no means exhaustive or comprehensive. We greatly appreciate _all_ the contributions submitted for inclusion in Grafana.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.2",
        "OSS",
        "Community Contributions"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3afee62b4a3f87040483327dc954a8953c342b5c",
