    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.5e0587b138eac3d6983b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We’ve taken our first, measured but important step towards improving the accessibility of Grafana, with much needed tweaks to keyboard navigation, accessibility labeling for UI elements for Grafana viewers, and an [accessibility statement](/accessibility/) for Grafana laying out what you can expect from a Grafana focused on making our project accessible to all.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.2",
        "OSS",
        "Accessibility"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3afee62b4a3f87040483327dc954a8953c342b5c",
        "sha256": "dcf7f229e26f311a0c0c3b5d42eb00415f636bff39eb3cac9bc5c3d848ba8005",
        "lineStart": 40,
        "lineEnd": 40,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-2.md#L40-L40"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.eeab51b4d7656913b135",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The biggest change to dashboards in Grafana 8.2 is the inclusion of a configurable fiscal year in the time picker. This option enables fiscal quarters as time ranges, which can be helpful for business-focused and executive dashboards in addition to many other common use cases. Please see the [time range controls documentation](/docs/grafana/latest/dashboards/time-range-controls/) for more information.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.2",
        "OSS",
        "Dashboards"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3afee62b4a3f87040483327dc954a8953c342b5c",
        "sha256": "dcf7f229e26f311a0c0c3b5d42eb00415f636bff39eb3cac9bc5c3d848ba8005",
        "lineStart": 44,
        "lineEnd": 44,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-2.md#L44-L44"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.73e4c0f423d52e6882c0",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We have continued to improve how you manage your plugins within Grafana. The new [plugins catalog](/docs/grafana/v8.0/administration/configuration/#plugin_admin_enabled) is now enabled by default. You can use the plugin catalog to find, install, and uninstall your plugins directly from within Grafana without needing the Grafana CLI or to restart Grafana.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.2",
        "OSS",
        "Plugins management"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3afee62b4a3f87040483327dc954a8953c342b5c",
        "sha256": "dcf7f229e26f311a0c0c3b5d42eb00415f636bff39eb3cac9bc5c3d848ba8005",
        "lineStart": 50,
        "lineEnd": 50,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-2.md#L50-L50"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.df96488f11fe31b052e8",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We’ve continued to bolster the new, unified alerting system launched in Grafana 8. This update includes the addition of a UI to edit the Cortex/Loki namespace, edit the alert group name, and edit the alert group evaluation interval. We've also added a Test button to test an alert notification contact point. There's even more to explore here including custom grouping for alert manager notifications and several small but significant changes to improve creation editing and managing alert rules. Please see the [alerting documentation](/docs/grafana/v8.2/alerting/unified-alerting/) for more details and information on how you can enable the unified alerting system in your instance of Grafana.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.2",
        "OSS",
        "Grafana Alerting"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3afee62b4a3f87040483327dc954a8953c342b5c",
        "sha256": "dcf7f229e26f311a0c0c3b5d42eb00415f636bff39eb3cac9bc5c3d848ba8005",
        "lineStart": 56,
        "lineEnd": 56,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-2.md#L56-L56"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e72909bcdf62d65f6b42",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can use Grafana’s image renderer to generate images of panels and dashboards. Grafana uses these images for alert notifications, PDF exports (Grafana Enterprise), and reports sent by Grafana (Grafana Enterprise). We’ve added additional metrics to the image renderer to help you diagnose its performance, and [included guidance in our documentation](/docs/grafana/next/image-rendering/#rendering-mode) to help you configure it for the best mix of performance and resource usage. Tests show that we have reduced image load time from the 95th percentile of 10 seconds to less than 3 seconds under normal load.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.2",
        "OSS",
        "Image Renderer performance improvements and measurement"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3afee62b4a3f87040483327dc954a8953c342b5c",
        "sha256": "dcf7f229e26f311a0c0c3b5d42eb00415f636bff39eb3cac9bc5c3d848ba8005",
        "lineStart": 60,
        "lineEnd": 60,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-2.md#L60-L60"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7b77de74bd5e05bef918",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We’ve revamped the Stats and License sections of Grafana for administrators. The new combined screen makes it easier to understand a license’s term and user counts, and find out early when you need to renew or expand a license. It’s also easier to parse Grafana statistics like the number of dashboards, data sources, and alerts in a given instance. This screen also includes an interactive list of dashboard and folder permissions, which can affect your users’ licensed roles in Grafana. Learn more about Grafana Enterprise on our [website](/products/enterprise/grafana/), and more about licenses in particular in our [docs](/docs/grafana/latest/enterprise/license/license-restrictions/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.2",
        "Grafana Enterprise",
        "Brand-new license and stats screen"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3afee62b4a3f87040483327dc954a8953c342b5c",
        "sha256": "dcf7f229e26f311a0c0c3b5d42eb00415f636bff39eb3cac9bc5c3d848ba8005",
        "lineStart": 66,
        "lineEnd": 66,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-2.md#L66-L66"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "What's new in Grafana v8.2 > Grafana Enterprise > Brand-new license and stats screen"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f077581f91d04184ea42",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Role-based access control now covers data source and provisioning permissions. You can decide which roles (Viewers, Editors, and Admins) can manage data sources and data source permissions in Grafana, and which roles can reload provisioning configuration for dashboards, data sources, and other provisioned resources. We’ll continue adding role-based access control to more Grafana services, like dashboards and API Keys, in upcoming releases. Learn more about role-based access control in our [release post](/blog/2021/06/23/new-in-grafana-enterprise-8.0-fine-grained-access-control-for-reporting-and-user-management/) and our [docs](/docs/grafana/latest/enterprise/access-control/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.2",
        "Grafana Enterprise",
        "New role-based access control permissions"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3afee62b4a3f87040483327dc954a8953c342b5c",
        "sha256": "dcf7f229e26f311a0c0c3b5d42eb00415f636bff39eb3cac9bc5c3d848ba8005",
        "lineStart": 72,
        "lineEnd": 72,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-2.md#L72-L72"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "What's new in Grafana v8.2 > Grafana Enterprise > New role-based access control permissions"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.bb0e3b96e1e10f9af71d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Usage Insights Logs contain valuable information about user dashboard visits, queries, and front-end errors that are otherwise impossible to track in Grafana. You can now export those logs alongside your regular server logs to identify problematic dashboards and data sources and improve users’ experience with Grafana. Previously, these metrics could only be exported directly to Loki. Learn more in the [documentation about exporting logs](/docs/grafana/latest/enterprise/usage-insights/export-logs/)",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.2",
        "Grafana Enterprise",
        "Export usage insights logs as server logs"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3afee62b4a3f87040483327dc954a8953c342b5c",
        "sha256": "dcf7f229e26f311a0c0c3b5d42eb00415f636bff39eb3cac9bc5c3d848ba8005",
        "lineStart": 78,
        "lineEnd": 78,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-2.md#L78-L78"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "What's new in Grafana v8.2 > Grafana Enterprise > Export usage insights logs as server logs"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9a5486a211e528629e52",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Reports offer a powerful way to deliver insights directly to your email inboxes. Now you can create a report directly from any dashboard, using the Share button. This is especially useful when combined with role-based access control, which you can use to grant Editors or Viewers the ability to create reports in Grafana. To learn more, see the [reporting documentation](/docs/grafana/latest/enterprise/reporting/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.2",
        "Grafana Enterprise",
        "Create a report from the dashboard Share dialogue"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3afee62b4a3f87040483327dc954a8953c342b5c",
        "sha256": "dcf7f229e26f311a0c0c3b5d42eb00415f636bff39eb3cac9bc5c3d848ba8005",
        "lineStart": 84,
        "lineEnd": 84,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-2.md#L84-L84"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "What's new in Grafana v8.2 > Grafana Enterprise > Create a report from the dashboard Share dialogue"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.987783541e651adea0e9",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana 8.3 is an exciting release for Grafana Labs. This release includes the new Candlestick Panel, a new visualization suggestions engine and, for enterprise users, Recorded Queries.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.3"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c24dd159676a5a116da7fab704ca0f8776efcf5e",
        "sha256": "522d8ddad61c14380c5bf55c81e88cb5ed0b5701cac9d1d4624ba8683f8d4897",
        "lineStart": 24,
        "lineEnd": 24,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-3.md#L24-L24"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2314d6c06b93c67b95e5",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For Open Source users it also marks the first time Grafana Alerting, formerly unified alerting, is enabled by default for new Grafana installations. Grafana Alerting in 8.3 is the flexible, single pane of glass for all your alerts. Included in this release is expanded provisioning support for notifiers, contact points, and alert rules, alongside auditing and role-based access control for our Enterprise customers.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.3"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c24dd159676a5a116da7fab704ca0f8776efcf5e",
        "sha256": "522d8ddad61c14380c5bf55c81e88cb5ed0b5701cac9d1d4624ba8683f8d4897",
        "lineStart": 26,
        "lineEnd": 26,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-3.md#L26-L26"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.cf37a87987a7a3634872",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We’ve summarized what’s new in the release here, but you might also be interested in the announcement blog post as well. If you’d like all the details you can check out the complete [CHANGELOG.md](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.3"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c24dd159676a5a116da7fab704ca0f8776efcf5e",
        "sha256": "522d8ddad61c14380c5bf55c81e88cb5ed0b5701cac9d1d4624ba8683f8d4897",
        "lineStart": 28,
        "lineEnd": 28,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-3.md#L28-L28"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c7c322cb87e48caa9611",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana 8.3 includes many community contributions including the ability to interpolate variables in tags ([#42318](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/42318)), fly-out sub-menu support ([#41647](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/41647)), the addition of AWS RoboMaker & AWS Global Accelerator metrics to the AWS CloudWatch data source ([#41450](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/41450), [#41236](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/41236)), as well as updates to the news panel ([#41193](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/41193)), the plugin catalog ([#40917](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/40917)), and many more. The Grafana Labs team is deeply grateful for all those who take the time to contribute and participate in the development of Grafana.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.3",
        "Grafana OSS",
        "Community Contributions"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c24dd159676a5a116da7fab704ca0f8776efcf5e",
        "sha256": "522d8ddad61c14380c5bf55c81e88cb5ed0b5701cac9d1d4624ba8683f8d4897",
        "lineStart": 34,
        "lineEnd": 34,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-3.md#L34-L34"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.52472b87aec0df282f9a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We’ve continued to make progress on improving Grafana’s accessibility. In Grafana 8.3 we’ve updated the main menu with improved keyboard navigation. We’ve also improved Grafana’s behavior when navigating through elements with the tab key (tab stops) and finished our work to make Grafana’s viewer roles compatible with assistive technologies such as screen readers. You can read our accessibility statement here and reach out to us with accessibility issues using our community Slack or our community forums.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.3",
        "Grafana OSS",
        "Accessibility"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c24dd159676a5a116da7fab704ca0f8776efcf5e",
        "sha256": "522d8ddad61c14380c5bf55c81e88cb5ed0b5701cac9d1d4624ba8683f8d4897",
