    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.39336a36b9e9dc4ed370",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- Time series panel: charts are one of our main areas of limited accessibility. As of 8.4, you can also move a panel and make range selections using your keyboard. - Press arrow keys to move the cursor around. - Hold Shift to increase cursor speed. - Hold space to start rage selection.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.4",
        "OSS",
        "Ease of use",
        "Accessibility improvements"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "252f5beb8e3fcec627862bf9d7133a82ac790f48",
        "sha256": "698f50f998678faa1ffd85c3becf29427f209d103b67f78883e8ff9c47004eec",
        "lineStart": 50,
        "lineEnd": 50,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-4.md#L50-L50"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8016c9892693c433eaa2",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can read our accessibility statement [here](/accessibility/) and reach out to us with accessibility issues using our community Slack or our community forums.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.4",
        "OSS",
        "Ease of use",
        "Accessibility improvements"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "252f5beb8e3fcec627862bf9d7133a82ac790f48",
        "sha256": "698f50f998678faa1ffd85c3becf29427f209d103b67f78883e8ff9c47004eec",
        "lineStart": 51,
        "lineEnd": 51,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-4.md#L51-L51"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8e72712441fdafcf4bbf",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana is used to visualize traces and metrics, but Grafana itself can be traced as well. For example, users running a Grafana instance can export all the traces of endpoints and database requests to Jaeger, which helps you view all Grafana traffic.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.4",
        "OSS",
        "Ease of use",
        "New option to configure OpenTelemetry"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "252f5beb8e3fcec627862bf9d7133a82ac790f48",
        "sha256": "698f50f998678faa1ffd85c3becf29427f209d103b67f78883e8ff9c47004eec",
        "lineStart": 55,
        "lineEnd": 55,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-4.md#L55-L55"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c82df20fe7848dfe9630",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We’re currently using OpenTracing for this, but since the repository is being deprecated, we’ve started our work to migrate to OpenTelemetry and remove OpenTracing. This release is the first step toward this goal. It also adds the option to configure OpenTelemetry instead of OpenTracing.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.4",
        "OSS",
        "Ease of use",
        "New option to configure OpenTelemetry"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "252f5beb8e3fcec627862bf9d7133a82ac790f48",
        "sha256": "698f50f998678faa1ffd85c3becf29427f209d103b67f78883e8ff9c47004eec",
        "lineStart": 57,
        "lineEnd": 57,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-4.md#L57-L57"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f6aecce269aecd05eb8b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In Grafana 8.3, we upgraded Grafana to use envelope encryption, which adds a layer of indirection to the encryption process. Instead of encrypting all secrets in the database with a single key, Grafana uses a set of keys, called data encryption keys (DEKs), to encrypt them. These data encryption keys are themselves encrypted with a single key-encryption key (KEK).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.4",
        "OSS",
        "Ease of use",
        "Rotate your encryption key"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "252f5beb8e3fcec627862bf9d7133a82ac790f48",
        "sha256": "698f50f998678faa1ffd85c3becf29427f209d103b67f78883e8ff9c47004eec",
        "lineStart": 61,
        "lineEnd": 61,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-4.md#L61-L61"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3384c752bbb3dbf67012",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "As of 8.4, you can rotate your KEK and quickly re-encrypt your DEKs in case a key is compromised.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.4",
        "OSS",
        "Ease of use",
        "Rotate your encryption key"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "252f5beb8e3fcec627862bf9d7133a82ac790f48",
        "sha256": "698f50f998678faa1ffd85c3becf29427f209d103b67f78883e8ff9c47004eec",
        "lineStart": 63,
        "lineEnd": 63,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-4.md#L63-L63"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f499173fcdca65aeab21",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Envelope encryption is not enabled by default in version 8.4. You can enable it by adding the term `envelopeEncryption` to the list of feature toggles in your [Grafana configuration](/docs/grafana/next/administration/configuration/#feature_toggles?mdm=email), or by sending a request to support if you use Grafana Cloud.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.4",
        "OSS",
        "Ease of use",
        "Rotate your encryption key"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "252f5beb8e3fcec627862bf9d7133a82ac790f48",
        "sha256": "698f50f998678faa1ffd85c3becf29427f209d103b67f78883e8ff9c47004eec",
        "lineStart": 65,
        "lineEnd": 65,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-4.md#L65-L65"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4b1f4a3e9f108959380c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "[Mute timings](/docs/grafana/next/alerting/unified-alerting/notifications/mute-timings/) have been a popular request from the community. They are a powerful addition to the new alerting feature set and allow you to suppress specific alerts on a recurring interval or schedule, [contrary to](/docs/grafana/next/alerting/unified-alerting/notifications/mute-timings/#mute-timings-vs-silences) Silences.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.4",
        "OSS",
        "Alerting",
        "Support for mute timings"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "252f5beb8e3fcec627862bf9d7133a82ac790f48",
        "sha256": "698f50f998678faa1ffd85c3becf29427f209d103b67f78883e8ff9c47004eec",
        "lineStart": 73,
        "lineEnd": 73,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-4.md#L73-L73"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7c1cac1492db2e3cb2a0",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Paired with the existing Silences, this gives you even more control over when alerts should be sent and contact points notified.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.4",
        "OSS",
        "Alerting",
        "Support for mute timings"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "252f5beb8e3fcec627862bf9d7133a82ac790f48",
        "sha256": "698f50f998678faa1ffd85c3becf29427f209d103b67f78883e8ff9c47004eec",
        "lineStart": 75,
        "lineEnd": 75,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-4.md#L75-L75"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ee191ba8b2d6a5c7b620",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The new Alert Panel displays your alerts and associated alert instances, and supports grouping by one or more custom labels. You can also display all alert instances in an ungrouped list by choosing the custom grouping mode without any configured labels.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.4",
        "OSS",
        "Alerting",
