          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "What's new in Grafana v8.5 > Grafana Enterprise > Security > Control access to dashboards, folders, and annotations (beta)"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0fbae0061d8897e19fc4",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can already keep secrets in Grafana’s database (like data source credentials) safer by retrieving your database encryption key from a Key Management Service, like AWS KMS or Azure Key Vault. In Grafana v8.5, you can use an Azure Managed Identity to integrate with Azure Key Vault. This simplifies the Key Vault integration and keeps it consistent with Grafana data sources, like Azure Data Explorer.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.5",
        "Grafana Enterprise",
        "Security",
        "Configure Azure Key Vault using Managed Identities"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-5.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "15f3fc25db59e3bac75e15217a2aedc351624e69",
        "sha256": "786bd58d8bd4959f301bf1e3d7b428b4f76f342335b19cd744f6500e818040c8",
        "lineStart": 135,
        "lineEnd": 135,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-5.md#L135-L135"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "What's new in Grafana v8.5 > Grafana Enterprise > Security > Configure Azure Key Vault using Managed Identities"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b87c94d6ed3feed850b8",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Reports are a great way to share Grafana dashboards by email with users who don’t regularly sign in to Grafana. In 8.5, we’ve revamped the Report authoring UI to make it quicker and easier for you to create reports. View report details at a glance in list view, consider one configuration step at a time, and save reports for later. Also, Grafana will now emit a log every time a report is sent, so you can confirm its status or learn about send errors. Learn more about Reporting in our [docs](/docs/grafana/latest/enterprise/reporting/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v8.5",
        "Grafana Enterprise",
        "Configure reports more easily"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-5.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "15f3fc25db59e3bac75e15217a2aedc351624e69",
        "sha256": "786bd58d8bd4959f301bf1e3d7b428b4f76f342335b19cd744f6500e818040c8",
        "lineStart": 139,
        "lineEnd": 139,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v8-5.md#L139-L139"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "What's new in Grafana v8.5 > Grafana Enterprise > Configure reports more easily"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2e478dff2dc679ce2af1",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "As tradition goes, GrafanaCon — our yearly community event for Grafana open source users — is also where we launch the latest software release of Grafana. Keeping up with tradition, we are excited to be announcing Grafana v9.0: a release that elevates Grafana’s ease of use, discovery of data through new and improved visualizations and a default Grafana Alerting experience.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 24,
        "lineEnd": 24,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L24-L24"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.19f31a34fe362f74df88",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "A big focus for Grafana is making observability and data visualization and analytics easier and more accessible for everyone. For popular data sources like Prometheus and Loki, writing and understanding queries can be hard. This is why we are excited to announce that Grafana 9 comes with new visual query builders for both these data sources. These visual query builders will lower the barrier of entry and they help anyone to compose, understand and learn how the underlying query languages.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 26,
        "lineEnd": 26,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L26-L26"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.86346bd643116b817c25",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The release also includes a brand-new powerful and fast heatmap visualization, a more accessible navigation menu, improvements to dashboard search, advanced security and authentication features, and more.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 28,
        "lineEnd": 28,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L28-L28"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b9fedf0c9e4e251ac1f0",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We’ve summarized what’s new in the release here. If you’d like all the details you can check out the complete [changelog](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 30,
        "lineEnd": 30,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L30-L30"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.36e58e877e5516196b33",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Prometheus queries are not the easiest to write or understand. The PromQL query language is very complex and advanced. Even relatively simple queries are hard to compose and read for new users. This is why we are introducing a new UI query builder that allows anyone to compose and learn how Prometheus queries work.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Prometheus query builder"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 34,
        "lineEnd": 34,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L34-L34"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c4ab0871fd896675175e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This new query builder allows you to easily search and select a metric as well as building label filters. You can start either the selecting a metric or a label filter as they both act as filters on each other. The metric selector allow you to search on multiple parts of the metric name at the same time, just separate each search string with a whitespace.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Prometheus query builder",
        "Metric and label filters"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 40,
        "lineEnd": 40,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L40-L40"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a0366d5cbff0585c8e37",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "All functions, aggregations and binary operations are added via the + Operation button. Operations are presented in the order they are executed, not in the inverted order they are written in the text query. This makes queries a lot easier to read and reason about as you now clearly see what function parameter is going to which function as well as information about parameter names and function documentation integrated into the builder.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Prometheus query builder",
        "Operations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 44,
        "lineEnd": 44,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L44-L44"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1031bf17ed5b37dccc58",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The query builder will automatically manage and add the range selector. It will be shown as a parameter to the operations that require a range vector (rate, delta, increase, etc).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Prometheus query builder",
        "Range vector"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 48,
        "lineEnd": 48,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L48-L48"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d5781ca7686b0beff540",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Simple binary operations like multiplication or division by a scalar are represented via simple operation boxes like other functions. The builder also supports binary operations on nested query expressions.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Prometheus query builder",
        "Binary operations"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 52,
        "lineEnd": 52,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L52-L52"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3759c65a583eb0fa1bee",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can switch between the text edit mode (Code) and the UI builder mode while having your text changes preserved as the visual builder model is derived from the text query using a full featured PromQL query parser.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Prometheus query builder",
        "Switch between code and builder"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 56,
        "lineEnd": 56,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L56-L56"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.732aaf64977cab319ad1",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Loki also has complex and powerful query language in LogQL. In many ways it’s more complex and has more syntax to remember than PromQL. Luckily the new query builder we are introducing in Grafana v 9.0 will help you write and understand Loki queries without knowing any of the syntax. Take a look at this example log query.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Loki query builder"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 60,
        "lineEnd": 60,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L60-L60"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a2e852c18f63a9c7419c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In the query builder you can add and edit label filters, line filters, parsers and functions. The image above shows a log query but you can also do metric queries.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Loki query builder"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 64,
        "lineEnd": 64,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L64-L64"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d23937fc89a53d6daf0d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The Loki query builder supports all the features listed for the prometheus query builder above, including support for nested binary operations, explain mode and switching between text editor and builder while preserving changes.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Loki query builder"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
