    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ae45d038655110de4302",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The new heatmap by default assumes that the data is pre-bucketed. So if your query returns time series each series is seen as separate bucket (y axis tick). The panel is so much faster than the old one so it can render many time series with thousands of data points each without issue.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "New heatmap panel"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 85,
        "lineEnd": 85,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L85-L85"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b9668cebbeb06240c44e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana Alerting is now on by default if you upgrade from an earlier version of Grafana. If you have been using legacy alerting in an earlier version of Grafana and you upgrade to Grafana 9 your alert rules will be automatically migrated and the legacy alerting interface will be replaced by the Grafana Alerting interface.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Grafana Alerting is the default in Grafana 9"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 91,
        "lineEnd": 91,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L91-L91"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.54452acc4756a7f3d792",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana Alerting, called unified alerting in Grafana 8, has been available since June, 2021 now provides feature parity with legacy alerting and many additional benefits. To find out more on the process to revert back to legacy alerts if needed, click [here](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/v10.2/alerting/set-up/migrating-alerts/#opt-out). Note that if you do revert back (by setting the Grafana config flag GF_UNIFIED_ALERTING_ENABLED to false), that we expect to remove legacy alerting in the next major Grafana release, Grafana 10.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Grafana Alerting is the default in Grafana 9"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 93,
        "lineEnd": 93,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L93-L93"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.21c00841a6e0e1c53858",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Alert state history for Grafana managed alerts indicates the cause of the state. Alert rules can be configured to use the \"Alerting\" or \"OK\" states when rule evaluations result in Error or NoData conditions. This change tracks the difference between, for example, Alerting, Alerting (NoData), and Alerting (Error). This change also updates the UI to handle the new serialized states: filtering, sorting, and coloring.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Grafana Alerting is the default in Grafana 9",
        "Alert state history for Grafana managed alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 97,
        "lineEnd": 97,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L97-L97"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ac1094c1a3467e8bd478",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana Alerting now provides the ability to capture an image for Grafana managed alerts and deliver it via a notification. This is configurable via the contact points tab of Grafana Alerting . This functionality was available in legacy dashboard alerting, but was missing in Grafana Alerting. It requires the alert to be related to a specific dashboard panel using the “Dashboard UID” and “Panel ID” annotations.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Grafana Alerting is the default in Grafana 9",
        "Images in notifications for Grafana managed alerts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 101,
        "lineEnd": 101,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L101-L101"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8a8b60fae9e8709aa5a0",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana now uses envelope encryption to encrypt secrets in the database. Envelope encryption adds a layer of indirection to the encryption process. Instead of encrypting all secrets in the database with a single key, Grafana uses a set of keys called data encryption keys (DEKs) to encrypt them. These data encryption keys are themselves encrypted with a single key encryption key (KEK). This allows you to rotate your KEK and quickly re-encrypt your DEKs in case a key is compromised. In Grafana Enterprise, you can also store your KEK in an external key management service (KMS) like AWS KMS or Azure Key Vault, for extra security. Learn more about envelope encryption in the [database encryption documentation](../../setup-grafana/configure-security/configure-database-encryption/#envelope-encryption).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Envelope encryption is generally available and enabled by default"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 105,
        "lineEnd": 105,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L105-L105"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1dc97d65078ee62be44f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The dashboard previews initially came to life during our internal [Grafana Labs Hackathon](/blog/2022/01/14/all-about-the-grafana-labs-hackathon-2.0/?), and are now ready for an opt-in beta release. The previews provide an overview of all available dashboards and help you quickly find the right dashboard when the dashboard names aren’t enough.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Dashboard previews (opt-in beta)"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 111,
        "lineEnd": 111,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L111-L111"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.fc2289794aa6fdd1de40",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana 9 has a feature toggle `panelTitleSearch`. When enabled, it tells Grafana to use a new search engine. Instead of using SQL queries, the new search uses an in-memory full-text index. That provides a better search experience and additionally allows searching through panel titles.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Panel title search (opt-in beta)"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 117,
        "lineEnd": 117,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L117-L117"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.740a462fdbe2e9af8bb7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can expand the navigation bar for a better overview of Grafana’s features and installed integrations. This is the first improvement to Grafana’s navigation, with more to come in future releases.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Expanding the navigation bar"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 121,
        "lineEnd": 121,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L121-L121"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b060ac941291ea244bee",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "As part of the upcoming improvements to Grafana’s navigation, you can now directly access your starred dashboards from the navigation bar. This is currently an opt-in feature that can be accessed by enabling the savedItems feature flag.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Starred dashboards in the navigation bar"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 127,
        "lineEnd": 127,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L127-L127"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b5061ff7e49bd9f847d4",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "It is now possible to create panels and/or dashboards directly from Explore. When clicking on the “Add to dashboard” button in the Explore toolbar users can now create a panel in a new dashboard or in an existing one. The generated panel contains all the pane’s queries and a default visualization automatically picked from the current results shown in Explore. Dashboards are not automatically saved so that users can go through the current save flow. Optionally, dashboards can be opened in a new tab to preserve Explore’s state.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Explore to Dashboard"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 133,
        "lineEnd": 133,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L133-L133"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4db04b76226d628c4f2b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Using cmd+k (macOS) or ctrl+k (Linux/Windows), users can pull up a palette of commands that allow easier navigation and other tasks. <!-- Currently available commands:-->",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Command palette"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 139,
        "lineEnd": 139,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L139-L139"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a05a8577f08d5f5aaf82",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In order to support debugging issues in Grafana, error alerts that appear in Grafana include a trace ID, and these alerts can be accessed under your Profile. This is currently an opt-in feature that can be accessed by enabling two feature flags:",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "List of errors with trace IDs"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 143,
        "lineEnd": 143,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L143-L143"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.666b4958dfcfe0ab537f",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- `tracing` - enables the tracing id in error messages",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "List of errors with trace IDs"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
