    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.411e4d1bd81f13f0678a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Query history is a panel that keeps track of all queries that are run in Explore. So far the history was saved in browser local storage causing some problems, for example running out of storage space or not being able to use the same query history in different browsers. Not anymore! We’re migrating all entries from browser local storage to the database. Migration will happen behind the senses when query history panel is opened. This feature can be disabled using config entry query_history in custom.ini.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Query History migration"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 152,
        "lineEnd": 152,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L152-L152"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.12f459ce0e20f4ee00f7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Fine-grained access control is now called role-based access control, or RBAC. It is now enabled by default in Grafana Enterprise and Grafana Cloud, so you can create and define custom roles like Annotations Writer, Users Viewer, and Dashboard Permissions Writer for users, teams, or service accounts. Learn more about RBAC in the [docs](/docs/grafana/next/enterprise/access-control/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Enterprise",
        "RBAC is generally available"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 162,
        "lineEnd": 162,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L162-L162"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ee8890762451db8ebfbd",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you have information spread across several dashboards that you’d like to send out to a group of recipients periodically, you can now add multiple dashboards to a single report and send it all in one email. Learn more about Reporting in the [Reporting docs](/docs/grafana/latest/enterprise/reporting/#reporting).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Reporting",
        "Add multiple dashboards to a single report"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 170,
        "lineEnd": 170,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L170-L170"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8c72dccb1a52fd11e2c8",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Reporting is all about convenience - getting info to eyeballs as quickly as possible. Now you can embed an image of a dashboard directly within a report email, so your recipients can see it right when they open the message instead of opening an attached PDF. This is especially handy for SLOs, financial results, or other at-a-glance data. Learn more about Reporting in the [Reporting docs](/docs/grafana/latest/enterprise/reporting/#reporting).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Reporting",
        "Embed an image of a dashboard in a report"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 174,
        "lineEnd": 174,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L174-L174"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e4e46682a9f9570e6fdd",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- Built-in roles are now called basic roles. They now consist of permissions, not roles.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Breaking changes",
        "Role-based access control: changes for general release"
      ],
      "source": {
