    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.95dfe22914136c1b0673",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- Basic roles no longer support permission inheritance. Previously, when permissions of a Viewer basic role were modified, it was propagated to the Editor and Admin basic roles. With the Grafana 9.0 release, this is not the case anymore.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Breaking changes",
        "Role-based access control: changes for general release"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 189,
        "lineEnd": 189,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L189-L189"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.22cd93c94695e1ddf3cf",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- Several role-based access control actions have been renamed. All the database entries that use legacy action names will be migrated to use the new names, but provisioning files and scripts will have to be updated by the user. This change also means that if Grafana is downgraded from 9.0 to a lower version, some role-based access control permissions will not be resolved correctly.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Breaking changes",
        "Role-based access control: changes for general release"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 190,
        "lineEnd": 190,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L190-L190"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ba25b6818a06e849ac4b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In the Loki data source, the data format used to represent Loki logs-data has been changed to a more efficient format. (NOTE: this change applies to logs data only, it does not apply to numeric data) The logs are represented by a single dataframe with a \"labels\" field added, instead of separate dataframes for every label combination. Displaying logs data in explore, or in a dashboard using the logs panel will continue to work without changes. But, when displaying logs data in other dashboard panels, for example in a table visualization, changes will be visible, and configurations might need to be adjusted. For example, if the \"Labels to fields\" transformation was used, it has to be replaced with an “Extract fields” transformation, where the “labels” field is chosen as the source.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Breaking changes",
        "Loki: logs data format changed"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 194,
        "lineEnd": 195,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L194-L195"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.cf9147af0c2cbf9f178c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In the Loki data source, when grafana receives numeric data from Loki, it may contain NaN (not a number) values. For consistency and performance reasons we changed how we represent such values in Grafana. In previous versions, the behavior was different between alerting queries and other queries (like dashboard queries or explore queries). Alerting queries kept NaN values unchanged, but other queries converted these values to “null”. Starting with grafana 9.0.0, we will always keep these values unchanged. In other words, queries in dashboards and explore will behave the same as alerting queries in this regard.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Breaking changes",
        "Loki: NaN values representation changed in numeric data"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 199,
        "lineEnd": 199,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L199-L199"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.5ad3456f53b044bfc7b7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Support for Elasticsearch versions that are after their end of life ( based on https://www.elastic.co/support/eol ) was removed. This means that versions older than Elasticseach 7.10.0 will not be supported in Grafana 9.0.0.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Breaking changes",
        "Elasticsearch: Support for versions after their end of life was removed"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 203,
        "lineEnd": 203,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L203-L203"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.97ed01c9d9464b876ed7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In the Elasticsearch data source, browser access mode was deprecated in grafana 7.4.0 and removed in 9.0.0. If you used this mode, please switch to server access mode on the data source configuration page.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Breaking changes",
        "Elasticsearch: Support for browser access mode removed"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 207,
        "lineEnd": 207,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L207-L207"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1af992b2347ed07fe808",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In the Prometheus data source, when grafana receives numeric data from Prometheus, it may contain NaN (not a number) values. For consistency and performance reasons we changed how we represent such values in Grafana. In previous versions, the behavior was different between alerting queries and other queries (like dashboard queries or explore queries). Alerting queries kept NaN values unchanged, but other queries converted these values to “null”. Starting with grafana 9.0.0, we will always keep NaN values unchanged for all queries.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Breaking changes",
        "Prometheus: NaN values representation changed in numeric data"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 211,
        "lineEnd": 211,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L211-L211"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1987113f53eedd1b512f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In the InfluxDB data source, browser access mode was deprecated in grafana 8.0.0 and we are removing this feature in 9.0.0. If you are using this mode, you need to [switch to server access mode](../../datasources/influxdb/##influxql-classic-influxdb-query) on the data source configuration page or you can do this via provisioning. -->",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Breaking changes",
        "Prometheus: NaN values representation changed in numeric data"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 215,
        "lineEnd": 215,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L215-L215"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3830a90f538f57fb65f1",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The rename by regex transformation has been improved to allow global patterns of the form `/<stringToReplace>/g`. Depending on the regex match used, this may cause some transformations to behave slightly differently. You can guarantee the same behavior as before by wrapping the match string in forward slashes (`/`), for example, `(.*)` would become `/(.*)/`. ([Github Issue #48179](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/48179))",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Breaking changes",
        "Transformations: Allow more complex regex expressions in rename by regex"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 219,
        "lineEnd": 219,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L219-L219"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.960cd6e70eb442eb3248",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We have updated [clock panel](/grafana/plugins/grafana-clock-panel/) to version `2.0.0` to make it compatible with Grafana 9. The previous version `1.3.1` will cause the Grafana 9 to [crash](https://github.com/grafana/clock-panel/issues/106) when being used in a dashboard, we encourage you to update the panel before migrating to Grafana 9.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Breaking changes",
        "Clock Panel"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
