    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.cbb97f69c5af24c240f4",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In v9.0, the `envelopeEncryption` feature toggle is replaced in favor of `disableEnvelopeEncryption`, and Grafana uses the envelope encryption mechanism by default.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Breaking changes",
        "Envelope encryption enabled by default"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 248,
        "lineEnd": 248,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L248-L248"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7c6b722ed584334a9a70",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Therefore, any secret created or updated in Grafana v9.0 won't be decryptable by any previous Grafana version, unless the Grafana version is at least v8.5 and the feature toggle `envelopeEncryption` is enabled. If not properly configured, this can cause issues in high availability setups, progressive rollouts, or any situation that involves rolling back to a previous Grafana version.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Breaking changes",
        "Envelope encryption enabled by default"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 250,
        "lineEnd": 250,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L250-L250"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6665f99ea00b20ff562b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We strongly recommend that you enable `envelopeEncryption` for older versions to deploy envelope encryption. You can alternatively configure the `disableEnvelopeEncryption` feature toggle before upgrading to v9.0; however, this feature toggle might be removed in a future Grafana release.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Breaking changes",
        "Envelope encryption enabled by default"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 252,
        "lineEnd": 252,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L252-L252"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.189134d53aca1cd66e26",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For more details, and workarounds for potential issues, refer to the [documentation](../../setup-grafana/configure-security/configure-database-encryption/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "Breaking changes",
        "Envelope encryption enabled by default"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 254,
        "lineEnd": 254,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L254-L254"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0f72f0b211fe939a051a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When we release Grafana 9.0 on June 14th, Grafana will no longer enforce viewers and editor-admins differently. That means that regardless of whether your Grafana Enterprise license is tiered or combined, instead of seeing this on the Stats & Licensing page:",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "A note on Grafana Enterprise licensing"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 258,
        "lineEnd": 258,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L258-L258"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "What's new in Grafana v9.0 > A note on Grafana Enterprise licensing"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ee3fd9ac3f8696957901",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "It also means that Grafana will count all users the same, regardless of their role, including org roles (Viewer, Editor, Admin) and fine-grained roles (Dashboard Editor, Reports Editor, etc.). You won’t see a separate warning banner or see users locked out if you hit your limit of viewers or editor-admins, only your total combined limit of active users.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "A note on Grafana Enterprise licensing"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 266,
        "lineEnd": 266,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L266-L266"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "What's new in Grafana v9.0 > A note on Grafana Enterprise licensing"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.45f52f4e14638688f07d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For example, if you have a license for 10 active admins and 100 active viewers in your Grafana Enterprise license, then starting in v9.0 you will have a limit of 110 active users, and it doesn’t matter what roles those users have, they will all be counted and enforced the same.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.0",
        "A note on Grafana Enterprise licensing"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3391f04dcb99b5fd7f3dc4839fe6fdf0d4bf3bae",
        "sha256": "39f11e18287d80cebb61272008eb6acbd2b991b12fd2ca34601c0b2454aa3aa1",
        "lineStart": 268,
        "lineEnd": 268,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-0.md#L268-L268"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "What's new in Grafana v9.0 > A note on Grafana Enterprise licensing"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.5bf379b5e0f329fb94e2",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We're excited to announce Grafana v9.1, with a variety of improvements that focus on Grafana's usability, performance, and security. Read on to learn about new options to share and embed dashboards, search and navigation enhancements, new panel options, and additional authentication features. You can also find out more about new single sign-on and role-based access control options in Grafana Enterprise, and more. For details, see the complete [changelog](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.1"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7f2b514efd5a050fef62ef5f9f55cac366248b28",
        "sha256": "d693aa46fe2713a3b657e9a37d23a3275c0fd01c2a3d5ed47c565a3c3019c53a",
        "lineStart": 24,
        "lineEnd": 27,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md#L24-L27"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.88e5314ff1e247ccc829",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Service accounts are an evolution in machine access within Grafana. You can create multiple API tokens per service account with independent expiration dates, and temporarily disable a service account without deleting it. These benefits make service accounts a more flexible way for Terraform and other apps to authenticate with Grafana.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.1",
        "OSS",
        "Auth and security",
        "Grafana service accounts are generally available"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7f2b514efd5a050fef62ef5f9f55cac366248b28",
        "sha256": "d693aa46fe2713a3b657e9a37d23a3275c0fd01c2a3d5ed47c565a3c3019c53a",
        "lineStart": 35,
        "lineEnd": 37,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md#L35-L37"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3f7b8f01f96fa53a6a92",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Service accounts also work with [role-based access control](../../administration/roles-and-permissions/access-control/) in [Grafana Enterprise](../../introduction/grafana-enterprise/). You can improve security by granting service accounts specific roles to limit the functions they can perform. Service accounts have been in beta since Grafana v8.5. During that time, we've improved the UI and migration path from API keys, made it possible to add service accounts to teams, and inherit team permissions. To learn more about service accounts, see the [documentation](../../administration/service-accounts/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.1",
        "OSS",
        "Auth and security",
        "Grafana service accounts are generally available"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7f2b514efd5a050fef62ef5f9f55cac366248b28",
        "sha256": "d693aa46fe2713a3b657e9a37d23a3275c0fd01c2a3d5ed47c565a3c3019c53a",
        "lineStart": 39,
        "lineEnd": 43,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md#L39-L43"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c91db656a481bbd8f762",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can now easily embed Grafana in other applications by adding a JWT token directly in the Grafana's URL, for example,`https://example.grafana.net/dashboard/uuid?aut_token=<jwt_token>`. When the JWT token is passed through the request URL to Grafana, Grafana validates and authenticates the token linked to a specific user, allowing access to dashboards which that user can view. To see JWT URL embedding in action, see the [sample project](https://github.com/grafana/grafana-iframe-oauth-sample).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.1",
        "OSS",
        "Auth and security",
        "JWT URL embedding"
      ],
      "source": {
