    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.bf0f6ac43e62385f0dbc",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We've improved the performance of searching by panel title. If a panel's title matches your search query, it will be displayed in the search results. This feature will be rolled out to Grafana Cloud users over the course of several weeks, or can be accessed by enabling the `panelTitleSearch` feature toggle.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.1",
        "OSS",
        "Search and navigation",
        "(Beta) Panel title search and search improvements"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7f2b514efd5a050fef62ef5f9f55cac366248b28",
        "sha256": "d693aa46fe2713a3b657e9a37d23a3275c0fd01c2a3d5ed47c565a3c3019c53a",
        "lineStart": 71,
        "lineEnd": 73,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md#L71-L73"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.749492b684846d35fc79",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Panel title search uses our updated dashboard search approach. Previously, Grafana used SQL database queries to find dashboards by title. With the feature toggle enabled, Grafana can build an in-memory index of all dashboards. To learn more about search in Grafana, see the [documentation](../../dashboards/use-dashboards/#dashboard-search).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.1",
        "OSS",
        "Search and navigation",
        "(Beta) Panel title search and search improvements"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7f2b514efd5a050fef62ef5f9f55cac366248b28",
        "sha256": "d693aa46fe2713a3b657e9a37d23a3275c0fd01c2a3d5ed47c565a3c3019c53a",
        "lineStart": 75,
        "lineEnd": 78,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md#L75-L78"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e828804ae42d353b1e5a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "As part of the upcoming improvements to Grafana's navigation, you can now directly access your [starred dashboards](../../dashboards/use-dashboards/) from the navigation bar.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.1",
        "OSS",
        "Search and navigation",
        "Starred dashboards in the navigation bar"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7f2b514efd5a050fef62ef5f9f55cac366248b28",
        "sha256": "d693aa46fe2713a3b657e9a37d23a3275c0fd01c2a3d5ed47c565a3c3019c53a",
        "lineStart": 84,
        "lineEnd": 84,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md#L84-L84"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c979fdd809535c85818e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The beta heatmap announced in version 9.0 is now used throughout Grafana. Its performance is improved, and it now supports [exemplars](../../fundamentals/exemplars/). To learn more about the heatmap panel, see the [documentation](../../panels-visualizations/visualizations/heatmap/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.1",
        "OSS",
        "Panels",
        "Heatmap improvements"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7f2b514efd5a050fef62ef5f9f55cac366248b28",
        "sha256": "d693aa46fe2713a3b657e9a37d23a3275c0fd01c2a3d5ed47c565a3c3019c53a",
        "lineStart": 92,
        "lineEnd": 94,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md#L92-L94"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.d888843d2120293af492",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can now measure both distances and areas on Geomap visualizations by using the panel's new [measure tools](../../panels-visualizations/visualizations/geomap/#show-measure-tools). To learn more about the Geomap panel, see the [documentation](../../panels-visualizations/visualizations/geomap/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.1",
        "OSS",
        "Panels",
        "Geomap"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7f2b514efd5a050fef62ef5f9f55cac366248b28",
        "sha256": "d693aa46fe2713a3b657e9a37d23a3275c0fd01c2a3d5ed47c565a3c3019c53a",
        "lineStart": 100,
        "lineEnd": 101,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md#L100-L101"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3d0a34eafa5170e4ef20",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can now link metrics queries to your traces. This feature can be accessed by enabling the `traceToMetrics` feature toggle. Grafana Cloud users can access this feature by [opening a support ticket in the Cloud Portal](/profile/org#support).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.1",
        "OSS",
        "Panels",
        "(Beta) Trace to metrics"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7f2b514efd5a050fef62ef5f9f55cac366248b28",
        "sha256": "d693aa46fe2713a3b657e9a37d23a3275c0fd01c2a3d5ed47c565a3c3019c53a",
        "lineStart": 107,
        "lineEnd": 109,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md#L107-L109"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9d05f43719e714e4ce19",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In your tracing datasource configuration, select a metrics datasource, add tags, and write your queries. Each query appears as a link on each span. The configured tag values are dynamically added to your metrics queries. You can link to any metric you'd like. Metrics for span durations, counts, and errors filtered by service or span are a great starting point. The metrics generator introduced in Tempo 1.4 pairs extremely well with the trace to metrics feature. To learn more about the metrics generator, see the [blog post](/blog/2022/05/02/new-in-grafana-tempo-1.4-introducing-the-metrics-generator/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.1",
        "OSS",
        "Panels",
        "(Beta) Trace to metrics"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7f2b514efd5a050fef62ef5f9f55cac366248b28",
        "sha256": "d693aa46fe2713a3b657e9a37d23a3275c0fd01c2a3d5ed47c565a3c3019c53a",
        "lineStart": 111,
        "lineEnd": 117,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md#L111-L117"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.5fecb870afc1d0e7e0e2",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can now get Application Performance Management (APM) data with Grafana. The data is shown in a table in the Tempo datasource under the Service Graph tab. To access the feature, enable the `tempoApmTable` feature toggle. To receive the data for the APM table, you must also enable the metrics generator.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.1",
        "OSS",
        "Panels",
        "(Beta) APM table"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7f2b514efd5a050fef62ef5f9f55cac366248b28",
        "sha256": "d693aa46fe2713a3b657e9a37d23a3275c0fd01c2a3d5ed47c565a3c3019c53a",
        "lineStart": 123,
        "lineEnd": 126,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md#L123-L126"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7fbfb66733fb13b24f80",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana Cloud users can access this feature by [opening a support ticket in the Cloud Portal](/profile/org#support).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.1",
        "OSS",
        "Panels",
        "(Beta) APM table"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7f2b514efd5a050fef62ef5f9f55cac366248b28",
        "sha256": "d693aa46fe2713a3b657e9a37d23a3275c0fd01c2a3d5ed47c565a3c3019c53a",
        "lineStart": 128,
        "lineEnd": 128,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md#L128-L128"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.416bbef57d40a5755965",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The APM table displays rate, errors, and duration (RED) metrics. To view your top five RED span metrics, use the table summary view. The span metrics are created using the Tempo [metrics generator](/blog/2022/05/02/new-in-grafana-tempo-1.4-introducing-the-metrics-generator/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.1",
        "OSS",
        "Panels",
        "(Beta) APM table"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7f2b514efd5a050fef62ef5f9f55cac366248b28",
        "sha256": "d693aa46fe2713a3b657e9a37d23a3275c0fd01c2a3d5ed47c565a3c3019c53a",
        "lineStart": 130,
        "lineEnd": 132,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md#L130-L132"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3dbb14bd111db11e9d25",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We also embedded several links directly into the table. These links direct you to a Prometheus query to further investigate the data. We also provide a link from the table directly to Tempo search, making it easier for you to investigate your APM metrics.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.1",
        "OSS",
        "Panels",
        "(Beta) APM table"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7f2b514efd5a050fef62ef5f9f55cac366248b28",
        "sha256": "d693aa46fe2713a3b657e9a37d23a3275c0fd01c2a3d5ed47c565a3c3019c53a",
        "lineStart": 134,
        "lineEnd": 136,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md#L134-L136"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b72804bd884ec109a768",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Public dashboards are available as an alpha feature that can be enabled with the `publicDashboards` feature toggle. Grafana Cloud users can access this feature by [opening a support ticket in the Cloud Portal](/profile/org#support).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.1",
        "OSS",
        "Sharing",
        "(Alpha) Public dashboards"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7f2b514efd5a050fef62ef5f9f55cac366248b28",
        "sha256": "d693aa46fe2713a3b657e9a37d23a3275c0fd01c2a3d5ed47c565a3c3019c53a",
        "lineStart": 146,
        "lineEnd": 147,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md#L146-L147"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f53d2d24569bfaaa756e",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can generate a link for dashboards that you'd like to share publicly. Anyone with the link will be able to access that dashboard, and nothing else.",
