      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8e8b63be3b9ab15eca05",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can also control who can view, edit, or administer dashboard and data source usage insights, as well as data source query caching configuration. For more details, see the [RBAC documentation](../../administration/roles-and-permissions/access-control/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.1",
        "Grafana Enterprise",
        "Authentication and security",
        "RBAC for app plugins, usage insights, and query caching"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7f2b514efd5a050fef62ef5f9f55cac366248b28",
        "sha256": "d693aa46fe2713a3b657e9a37d23a3275c0fd01c2a3d5ed47c565a3c3019c53a",
        "lineStart": 217,
        "lineEnd": 218,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md#L217-L218"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "What's new in Grafana v9.1 > Grafana Enterprise > Authentication and security > RBAC for app plugins, usage insights, and query caching"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2b880e5aaa7e9003a6fb",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In Grafana version 9.0, we [revamped](../whats-new-in-v9-0/#envelope-encryption-is-generally-available-and-enabled-by-default) the method Grafana uses to encrypt secrets, like data source credentials, so that you can rotate encryption keys and integrate with a key management system like Hashicorp Vault, AWS Key Management Service, or Azure Key Vault.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.1",
        "Grafana Enterprise",
        "Authentication and security",
        "Rotate your database encryption keys using Grafana's API"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7f2b514efd5a050fef62ef5f9f55cac366248b28",
        "sha256": "d693aa46fe2713a3b657e9a37d23a3275c0fd01c2a3d5ed47c565a3c3019c53a",
        "lineStart": 224,
        "lineEnd": 224,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md#L224-L224"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "What's new in Grafana v9.1 > Grafana Enterprise > Authentication and security > Rotate your database encryption keys using Grafana's API"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.fdcf21907cdbb1d8bbb2",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Now, you can rotate keys and re-encrypt secrets via API. This makes it easier to configure Grafana to be secure while deploying it. To learn more, see our guide to [configuring database encryption](../../setup-grafana/configure-security/configure-database-encryption/#configure-database-encryption).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.1",
        "Grafana Enterprise",
        "Authentication and security",
        "Rotate your database encryption keys using Grafana's API"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7f2b514efd5a050fef62ef5f9f55cac366248b28",
        "sha256": "d693aa46fe2713a3b657e9a37d23a3275c0fd01c2a3d5ed47c565a3c3019c53a",
        "lineStart": 226,
        "lineEnd": 228,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md#L226-L228"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "What's new in Grafana v9.1 > Grafana Enterprise > Authentication and security > Rotate your database encryption keys using Grafana's API"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1a2dc9ac1ebf1b5941a2",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Auditing logs helps you manage and mitigate activity and meet compliance requirements. By default, Grafana emits an audit log with every action that changes something (like a user creating or updating a dashboard or updating another user's permissions). If you want to record all actions on the Grafana server, including GETs and page views, you can now turn on `verbose mode`. This results in more logs, but it can be useful to debug specific issues or make sure you catch everything happening in Grafana for security or compliance reasons. To learn more, see the [configuration documentation](../../setup-grafana/configure-grafana/enterprise-configuration/#verbose).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.1",
        "Grafana Enterprise",
        "Authentication and security",
        "Audit all actions in Grafana using verbose logging"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7f2b514efd5a050fef62ef5f9f55cac366248b28",
        "sha256": "d693aa46fe2713a3b657e9a37d23a3275c0fd01c2a3d5ed47c565a3c3019c53a",
        "lineStart": 232,
        "lineEnd": 236,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md#L232-L236"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "What's new in Grafana v9.1 > Grafana Enterprise > Authentication and security > Audit all actions in Grafana using verbose logging"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.47f16565eb1d4ec38003",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When you synchronize users from a SAML, LDAP, or OAuth provider, some user settings, such as name and email address, are synchronized from your identity provider. Previously, you could edit those settings in the Grafana UI, but they would revert back. To make user management clearer, you can now see which settings are synchronized from your identity provider, but you cannot edit those settings. To learn more about authentication, see the [documentation](../../setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.1",
        "Grafana Enterprise",
        "Authentication and security",
        "See (and don't edit) users synced from SAML, LDAP, and OAuth identity providers"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7f2b514efd5a050fef62ef5f9f55cac366248b28",
        "sha256": "d693aa46fe2713a3b657e9a37d23a3275c0fd01c2a3d5ed47c565a3c3019c53a",
        "lineStart": 242,
        "lineEnd": 245,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md#L242-L245"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "What's new in Grafana v9.1 > Grafana Enterprise > Authentication and security > See (and don't edit) users synced from SAML, LDAP, and OAuth identity providers"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.45773f08b0b21fc144e7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Team sync lets you set up synchronization between your authentication provider's teams and Grafana teams. To leverage your existing Active Directory in an efficient way without having to create multiple teams, you can now use wildcards when configuring LDAP groups, so that multiple Active Directory groups can be added at once to a single team.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.1",
        "Grafana Enterprise",
        "Authentication and security",
        "Support wildcards for LDAP groups in team sync"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7f2b514efd5a050fef62ef5f9f55cac366248b28",
        "sha256": "d693aa46fe2713a3b657e9a37d23a3275c0fd01c2a3d5ed47c565a3c3019c53a",
        "lineStart": 251,
        "lineEnd": 252,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md#L251-L252"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "What's new in Grafana v9.1 > Grafana Enterprise > Authentication and security > Support wildcards for LDAP groups in team sync"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a000eaa5ad32b8a956be",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "SAML Single Logout allows users to log out from all applications associated with the current IdP (Identity Provider) session established via SAML Single Sign-On (SSO). To enable integration of more use cases, we have added support for an HTTP-Redirect binding for a Single Logout.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.1",
        "Grafana Enterprise",
        "Authentication and security",
        "Redirect binding support for AzureAD SAML Single Logout"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "7f2b514efd5a050fef62ef5f9f55cac366248b28",
        "sha256": "d693aa46fe2713a3b657e9a37d23a3275c0fd01c2a3d5ed47c565a3c3019c53a",
        "lineStart": 258,
        "lineEnd": 259,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-1.md#L258-L259"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-paid-or-hosted-section-heading",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ],
        "restriction": "What's new in Grafana v9.1 > Grafana Enterprise > Authentication and security > Redirect binding support for AzureAD SAML Single Logout"
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ea800dbe8b1148aa7ad8",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Welcome to Grafana v9.2, a hefty minor release with a swath of improvements that help you create and share dashboards and alerts. Read on to learn about progress on public dashboards, our new panel help menu, custom branding in Grafana Enterprise, and improvements to access control. If you'd prefer to dig into the details, check out the complete [changelog](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.2"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "29f4614f2b0b22815fe82fbd43861ad5f04f9429",
        "sha256": "cd73053418ebf3229746062873d2d9c4a7c6a1724b919803082bb07d21ae60db",
        "lineStart": 22,
        "lineEnd": 24,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md#L22-L24"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ec824e56f580b68367c6",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Dashboard panel issues can occur for all kinds of reasons, from problems processing data to issues with rendering or configuration. Shorten your communication time when reporting issues and requesting help from Grafana Labs by retrieving a panel's query response data and panel settings. This will help the support team reproduce, diagnose, and fix the issue as quickly as possible. See our [documentation](/docs/grafana/latest/troubleshooting/send-panel-to-grafana-support/) for more info.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.2",
        "Panel help menu"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "29f4614f2b0b22815fe82fbd43861ad5f04f9429",
        "sha256": "cd73053418ebf3229746062873d2d9c4a7c6a1724b919803082bb07d21ae60db",
        "lineStart": 30,
        "lineEnd": 33,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md#L30-L33"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.19b9ff64477ab3ad4203",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For details, see [GitHub issue #55005](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/55005) and [\"Send a panel to Grafana Labs support\"](/docs/grafana/latest/troubleshooting/send-panel-to-grafana-support/) in the documentation.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.2",
        "Panel help menu"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "29f4614f2b0b22815fe82fbd43861ad5f04f9429",
        "sha256": "cd73053418ebf3229746062873d2d9c4a7c6a1724b919803082bb07d21ae60db",
        "lineStart": 35,
        "lineEnd": 35,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md#L35-L35"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8284713060f7615bac3b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Introducing the Canvas panel, a new panel that combines the power of Grafana with the flexibility of custom elements. Canvas visualizations are extensible form-built panels that allow you to explicitly place elements within static and dynamic layouts. This empowers you to design custom visualizations and overlay data in ways that aren't possible with standard Grafana panels, all within Grafana's UI. If you've used popular UI and web design tools, then designing Canvas panels will feel very familiar.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.2",
        "Canvas panel"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "29f4614f2b0b22815fe82fbd43861ad5f04f9429",
        "sha256": "cd73053418ebf3229746062873d2d9c4a7c6a1724b919803082bb07d21ae60db",
        "lineStart": 43,
        "lineEnd": 44,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md#L43-L44"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6e48c83362633d67ef80",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For example, you can place image layers and then overlay text that's updated by Grafana data sources, and display icons that can change color conditionally based on data.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.2",
        "Canvas panel"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "29f4614f2b0b22815fe82fbd43861ad5f04f9429",
        "sha256": "cd73053418ebf3229746062873d2d9c4a7c6a1724b919803082bb07d21ae60db",
        "lineStart": 46,
        "lineEnd": 46,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md#L46-L46"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.414a7e0c8e40ce112b27",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can now use Google Analytics 4 (GA4) to track usage of Grafana. To enable tracking with GA4, specify your property's measurement ID in Grafana's configuration file. Read more [in our documentation](/docs/grafana/latest/setup-grafana/configure-grafana/#google_analytics_4_id).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.2",
        "Support for Google Analytics 4 properties"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "29f4614f2b0b22815fe82fbd43861ad5f04f9429",
        "sha256": "cd73053418ebf3229746062873d2d9c4a7c6a1724b919803082bb07d21ae60db",
        "lineStart": 56,
        "lineEnd": 58,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md#L56-L58"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.227847f2da114de33b2c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Google Analytics 4 replaces Universal Analytics, which will stop processing hits in 2023 (July 1 for free accounts, October 1 for Google Analytics 360). You can continue using Universal Analytics with Grafana and send analytics data to both types of properties.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.2",
        "Support for Google Analytics 4 properties"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "29f4614f2b0b22815fe82fbd43861ad5f04f9429",
        "sha256": "cd73053418ebf3229746062873d2d9c4a7c6a1724b919803082bb07d21ae60db",
        "lineStart": 60,
        "lineEnd": 61,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md#L60-L61"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1817c0509a884306ca51",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The Alertmanager used for Grafana-managed alert rules is now based on the latest release of the Prometheus Alertmanager, v0.24. We continue to unify the different Alertmanagers that you can use with Grafana Alertmanager and will provide updates on this topic in a future release of Grafana.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.2",
        "Alertmanager updated to be based on Prometheus Alertmanager v0.24"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "29f4614f2b0b22815fe82fbd43861ad5f04f9429",
        "sha256": "cd73053418ebf3229746062873d2d9c4a7c6a1724b919803082bb07d21ae60db",
        "lineStart": 67,
        "lineEnd": 68,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md#L67-L68"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8c40f7b809caa5ccf006",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Error rules created with Grafana Alerting were previously switching to an Alerting state when the rule was facing an execution error or timeout. New error rules now switch by default to the `Error` state when failing to execute or timing out. You can change this default to either `Alerting` or `OK`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.2",
        "Grafana Alerting alert rules now return an Error state by default on execution error or timeout"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "29f4614f2b0b22815fe82fbd43861ad5f04f9429",
        "sha256": "cd73053418ebf3229746062873d2d9c4a7c6a1724b919803082bb07d21ae60db",
        "lineStart": 76,
        "lineEnd": 78,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md#L76-L78"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e5793caba0736d44689c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "External alertmanagers should now be configured as data sources using Grafana Configuration from the main Grafana navigation menu. This enables you to manage the contact points and notification policies of external alertmanagers from within Grafana and also encrypts HTTP basic authentication credentials that were previously visible when configuring external alertmanagers by URL.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.2",
        "Configure external alertmanagers as data sources"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "29f4614f2b0b22815fe82fbd43861ad5f04f9429",
        "sha256": "cd73053418ebf3229746062873d2d9c4a7c6a1724b919803082bb07d21ae60db",
        "lineStart": 91,
        "lineEnd": 91,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md#L91-L91"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7056e7e90ea6482e95de",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "_Available in Experimental in Grafana Open Source, Enterprise, and Cloud._ _To enable public dashboards, you must enable a feature flag or request this feature from support._",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.2",
        "Public dashboards"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "29f4614f2b0b22815fe82fbd43861ad5f04f9429",
        "sha256": "cd73053418ebf3229746062873d2d9c4a7c6a1724b919803082bb07d21ae60db",
        "lineStart": 95,
        "lineEnd": 96,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md#L95-L96"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ee16d6628a4a4e255c92",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "[Public dashboards](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/dashboards/share-dashboards-panels/shared-dashboards) launched as an experimental feature in Grafana v9.1. We've received lots of great feedback on this much-anticipated feature and thank everyone who has helped us improve it. The team has been hard at work polishing public dashboards, and we've closed quite a few bugs related to community reports. If you're trying out public dashboards, let us know how it is going in the [open discussion in GitHub](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/discussions/49253). Beyond bug fixes, we're excited to share some new features:",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.2",
        "Public dashboards"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "29f4614f2b0b22815fe82fbd43861ad5f04f9429",
        "sha256": "cd73053418ebf3229746062873d2d9c4a7c6a1724b919803082bb07d21ae60db",
        "lineStart": 98,
        "lineEnd": 102,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md#L98-L102"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f85cbacd4ca1f45ed312",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We have added the ability to use [expressions](/docs/grafana/latest/panels/query-a-data-source/use-expressions-to-manipulate-data/about-expressions/) for your public dashboards.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.2",
        "Public dashboards",
        "Expression support"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "29f4614f2b0b22815fe82fbd43861ad5f04f9429",
        "sha256": "cd73053418ebf3229746062873d2d9c4a7c6a1724b919803082bb07d21ae60db",
        "lineStart": 106,
        "lineEnd": 106,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md#L106-L106"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1856a25a98ff6693acb4",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We have introduced a new role called \"Public Dashboard writer\" that grants access to publish new public dashboards to additional roles and users. By default, only admins can share dashboards publicly.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.2",
        "Public dashboards",
        "Use RBAC to allow any user to share dashboards publicly"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "29f4614f2b0b22815fe82fbd43861ad5f04f9429",
        "sha256": "cd73053418ebf3229746062873d2d9c4a7c6a1724b919803082bb07d21ae60db",
        "lineStart": 122,
        "lineEnd": 123,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md#L122-L123"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.345cd55fea0804c9f987",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The Google Cloud monitoring data source UI has been brought up to date with the latest Grafana UI design. This new interface provides a more consistent experience as you switch between different data sources. It also groups query builder items together more logically, so it's easier to write queries. In the case of Cloud monitoring, the query builder's groupings should more closely match the groupings in Google's Cloud console.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.2",
        "Revamped UI for Google Cloud monitoring"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "29f4614f2b0b22815fe82fbd43861ad5f04f9429",
        "sha256": "cd73053418ebf3229746062873d2d9c4a7c6a1724b919803082bb07d21ae60db",
        "lineStart": 131,
        "lineEnd": 134,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md#L131-L134"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.00fdeee00c86e442b95a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Plugin developers can mark certain fields as secure to encrypt those fields in Grafana's database. This is important for sensitive fields like data source passwords or API keys. Previously, plugin developers needed to manually track which fields were labeled secure. We have extended our plugins platform to simplify this, which means one less thing for developers to worry about and better security for all users' data. For details on using this functionality, see [GitHub pull request #55313](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/55313) and our [plugin examples](https://github.com/grafana/grafana-plugin-examples) repository.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.2",
        "App Plugins: better handling for secure fields"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "29f4614f2b0b22815fe82fbd43861ad5f04f9429",
        "sha256": "cd73053418ebf3229746062873d2d9c4a7c6a1724b919803082bb07d21ae60db",
        "lineStart": 140,
        "lineEnd": 144,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md#L140-L144"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6e3e50f694a2c549adbe",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "[Transformations](../../panels-visualizations/query-transform-data/transform-data/) allow you to shape raw data from data sources, like metrics series or GitHub issues, into a format that's appropriate for the chosen visualization. We have extended the [Join transformation](../../panels-visualizations/query-transform-data/transform-data/#join-by-field) to support INNER JOINs in addition to OUTER JOINs. These work similarly to SQL JOINs.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.2",
        "Transformations: INNER JOINs"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "29f4614f2b0b22815fe82fbd43861ad5f04f9429",
        "sha256": "cd73053418ebf3229746062873d2d9c4a7c6a1724b919803082bb07d21ae60db",
        "lineStart": 148,
        "lineEnd": 149,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md#L148-L149"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.95d4f93a22debd9681c1",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Also, you can now click on the `x` to clear values in the select fields for the OUTER JOIN and Grouping to Matrix transformations as expected.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.2",
        "Transformations: INNER JOINs"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "29f4614f2b0b22815fe82fbd43861ad5f04f9429",
        "sha256": "cd73053418ebf3229746062873d2d9c4a7c6a1724b919803082bb07d21ae60db",
        "lineStart": 153,
        "lineEnd": 153,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md#L153-L153"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b8a197fe93d36c04797a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We have significantly simplified and improved the way you can create template variable queries for Loki data sources in dashboards. Use drop-downs to choose query type, label, and stream selector, without needing to worry about templating query syntax. For more information, refer to [Loki data source documentation](/docs/grafana/latest/datasources/loki/#query-variable).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.2",
        "Simplified UI to create template variable queries for Loki data source"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "29f4614f2b0b22815fe82fbd43861ad5f04f9429",
        "sha256": "cd73053418ebf3229746062873d2d9c4a7c6a1724b919803082bb07d21ae60db",
        "lineStart": 159,
        "lineEnd": 161,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md#L159-L161"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.507bcd7c99a91407d9cd",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can now leave a team empty without any users, or have only Members in a team. This helps you sync teams and users from a single sign-on provider like Active Directory or Okta, or if you use teams as collections of permissions. Previously, teams required at least one Admin user to be in a team.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.2",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Teams can be empty or without any Admin user"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "29f4614f2b0b22815fe82fbd43861ad5f04f9429",
        "sha256": "cd73053418ebf3229746062873d2d9c4a7c6a1724b919803082bb07d21ae60db",
        "lineStart": 171,
        "lineEnd": 173,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md#L171-L173"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.19f7fb3cc10798174e45",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can now choose a team's roles and permissions when creating a new team or editing an existing team, which helps you grant permissions to teams more efficiently. Previously, you could assign roles only when looking at a list of all teams.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.2",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Role-based access control is easier to use",
        "Role picker when creating and editing teams"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "29f4614f2b0b22815fe82fbd43861ad5f04f9429",
        "sha256": "cd73053418ebf3229746062873d2d9c4a7c6a1724b919803082bb07d21ae60db",
        "lineStart": 183,
        "lineEnd": 184,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md#L183-L184"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.edd890b0c5ed235f0fc4",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you create many custom roles in Grafana – for example, different roles for editing specific dashboards or folders, or specific roles for certain teams in your company – you can now organize them into groups for more efficient navigation, browsing, and custom role assignment. For more information on custom roles, see the [documentation](/docs/grafana/latest/developers/http_api/access_control/#create-a-new-custom-role).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.2",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Role-based access control is easier to use",
        "RBAC: Organize custom roles into groups"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "29f4614f2b0b22815fe82fbd43861ad5f04f9429",
        "sha256": "cd73053418ebf3229746062873d2d9c4a7c6a1724b919803082bb07d21ae60db",
        "lineStart": 190,
        "lineEnd": 191,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md#L190-L191"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.68b25c306b112d3e5d60",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can now assign fixed and custom roles to users, teams, and service accounts with the Grafana role_assignment resource in Terraform. This allows you to provision user permissions in a version-able, repeatable way if you use Terraform. Learn more in the [documentation](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/grafana/grafana/latest/docs/resources/role_assignment) for Grafana's Terraform provider.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.2",
        "Authentication and authorization",
        "Role-based access control is easier to use",
        "RBAC: Terraform resource for assigning fixed and custom roles to users, teams, and service accounts"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "29f4614f2b0b22815fe82fbd43861ad5f04f9429",
        "sha256": "cd73053418ebf3229746062873d2d9c4a7c6a1724b919803082bb07d21ae60db",
        "lineStart": 197,
        "lineEnd": 199,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md#L197-L199"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9481c55a547a88684083",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can now use `*` as the Grafana organization in the mapping to add all users from a given SAML Organization to all existing Grafana organizations. For more information, see [\"Configure SAML authentication\"](/docs/grafana/next/setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/saml/#configure-organization-mapping) in the documentation.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.2",
        "SAML role mapping improvements",
        "Map a user to all organizations in Grafana"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "29f4614f2b0b22815fe82fbd43861ad5f04f9429",
        "sha256": "cd73053418ebf3229746062873d2d9c4a7c6a1724b919803082bb07d21ae60db",
        "lineStart": 207,
        "lineEnd": 208,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md#L207-L208"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f06efad171e05f587afc",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you use a SAML identity provider to manage your users but prefer to assign roles and permissions in the Grafana UI or via API, you can now enable a configuration option to skip user organization and roles synchronization with your SAML provider.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.2",
        "SAML role mapping improvements",
        "Skip organization role sync"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "29f4614f2b0b22815fe82fbd43861ad5f04f9429",
        "sha256": "cd73053418ebf3229746062873d2d9c4a7c6a1724b919803082bb07d21ae60db",
        "lineStart": 214,
        "lineEnd": 214,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md#L214-L214"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6027a80b5249ab9efa42",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Use the `skip_org_role_sync` configuration option when configuring SAML to prevent synchronization with SAML roles and make user roles editable from within Grafana.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.2",
        "SAML role mapping improvements",
        "Skip organization role sync"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "29f4614f2b0b22815fe82fbd43861ad5f04f9429",
        "sha256": "cd73053418ebf3229746062873d2d9c4a7c6a1724b919803082bb07d21ae60db",
        "lineStart": 216,
        "lineEnd": 216,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md#L216-L216"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.04adefae2e6e88688e62",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For more information, see the [SAML configuration documentation](/docs/grafana/<GRAFANA_VERSION>/setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/saml/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.2",
        "SAML role mapping improvements",
        "Skip organization role sync"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-2.md",
