    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b4f7d7a44ae64aaa2002",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Because dashboards appear on a screen and reports are PDFs, it can be challenging to render data just the way you want to. Sometimes the report doesn't show enough columns in a table, or the titles appear too small. Now you can adjust the scale of your report to zoom in and make each text field and panel larger or zoom out to show more data.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.3",
        "Reporting: Zoom in and out to fit your data better into a PDF"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "acf11473ed5777a12056a218dd89128f81813beb",
        "sha256": "64900ffbe97db576e8db0598932deb044076d62fbd415d6bfd717f2d4b707209",
        "lineStart": 136,
        "lineEnd": 136,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-3.md#L136-L136"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2637d17a8c47a7197a5d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The zoom feature is located in the **Format Report** section of your reporting configuration. To learn more about reporting, refer to [Create and manage reports](../../dashboards/create-reports/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.3",
        "Reporting: Zoom in and out to fit your data better into a PDF"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "acf11473ed5777a12056a218dd89128f81813beb",
        "sha256": "64900ffbe97db576e8db0598932deb044076d62fbd415d6bfd717f2d4b707209",
        "lineStart": 138,
        "lineEnd": 138,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-3.md#L138-L138"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1036951306a084c71f73",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "As part of our efforts to improve the security of Grafana, we are introducing a long-awaited feature that enhances Grafana's OAuth 2.0 compatibility. When a user logs in using an OAuth provider, Grafana verifies on each request that the user's access token has not expired. Grafana uses the refresh token provided (if any exists) when an access token expires to obtain a new access token.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.3",
        "Users and access",
        "OAuth: token handling improvements"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "acf11473ed5777a12056a218dd89128f81813beb",
        "sha256": "64900ffbe97db576e8db0598932deb044076d62fbd415d6bfd717f2d4b707209",
        "lineStart": 150,
        "lineEnd": 150,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-3.md#L150-L150"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.79846ff82e4b517b10c1",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Because this feature introduces a breaking change, it is behind the `accessTokenExpirationCheck` feature toggle and is disabled by default. Enabling this functionality without configuring refresh tokens for the specific OAuth provider will sign users out after their access token has expired, and they would need to sign in again every time.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.3",
        "Users and access",
        "OAuth: token handling improvements"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "acf11473ed5777a12056a218dd89128f81813beb",
        "sha256": "64900ffbe97db576e8db0598932deb044076d62fbd415d6bfd717f2d4b707209",
        "lineStart": 152,
        "lineEnd": 152,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-3.md#L152-L152"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.3630a80b16f581d6748f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Complete documentation on how to configure obtaining a refresh token can be found on the [authentication configuration page](../../setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/), in the instructions for your Oauth identity provider.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.3",
        "Users and access",
        "OAuth: token handling improvements"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "acf11473ed5777a12056a218dd89128f81813beb",
        "sha256": "64900ffbe97db576e8db0598932deb044076d62fbd415d6bfd717f2d4b707209",
        "lineStart": 154,
        "lineEnd": 154,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-3.md#L154-L154"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9d7a71928abb97af7736",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In the older versions of Grafana, usernames were case-sensitive. This created conflicts, where a user might sign in using two different methods (like SAML and OAuth) and have two accounts created, like `elastigirl@incredibles.com` and `ElastiGirl@incredibles.com`. Users in this situation might think they have lost their preferences and permissions. If this has occurred in your Grafana instance, you can use a new Grafana CLI command to resolve user identity conflicts between users within Grafana.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.3",
        "Users and access",
        "Resolve user conflicts in Grafana's CLI"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "acf11473ed5777a12056a218dd89128f81813beb",
        "sha256": "64900ffbe97db576e8db0598932deb044076d62fbd415d6bfd717f2d4b707209",
        "lineStart": 158,
        "lineEnd": 158,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-3.md#L158-L158"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.c47c9634b36a8b0a9e7c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "> Note: If you use Grafana Cloud or you run Grafana with MySQL as your database, you will not experience any user identity conflicts and you do not need to use this tool.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.3",
        "Users and access",
        "Resolve user conflicts in Grafana's CLI"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "acf11473ed5777a12056a218dd89128f81813beb",
        "sha256": "64900ffbe97db576e8db0598932deb044076d62fbd415d6bfd717f2d4b707209",
        "lineStart": 160,
        "lineEnd": 160,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-3.md#L160-L160"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.76f12996e5397f9c263c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you use an LDAP directory to authenticate to Grafana but prefer to assign organizations and roles in the Grafana UI or via API, you can now skip user organization role synchronization with your LDAP directory.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.3",
        "Users and access",
        "LDAP: Role mapping improvements"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "acf11473ed5777a12056a218dd89128f81813beb",
        "sha256": "64900ffbe97db576e8db0598932deb044076d62fbd415d6bfd717f2d4b707209",
        "lineStart": 180,
        "lineEnd": 182,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-3.md#L180-L182"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.97751d7f799d23ca764b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Use the `skip_org_role_sync` [LDAP authentication configuration option](../../setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/ldap/#disable-org-role-synchronization) when configuring LDAP authentication to prevent the synchronization between your LDAP groups and organization roles and make user roles editable manually.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.3",
        "Users and access",
        "LDAP: Role mapping improvements"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "acf11473ed5777a12056a218dd89128f81813beb",
        "sha256": "64900ffbe97db576e8db0598932deb044076d62fbd415d6bfd717f2d4b707209",
        "lineStart": 184,
        "lineEnd": 186,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-3.md#L184-L186"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8ae423cd1f7e317ed81a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "If you use Azure AD OAuth2 authentication and use `SecurityEnabled` groups that you don't want Azure to embed in the authentication token, you can configure Grafana to use Microsoft's Graph API instead.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.3",
        "Users and access",
        "Azure AD OAuth2: New option to always fetch groups from the Graph API"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "acf11473ed5777a12056a218dd89128f81813beb",
        "sha256": "64900ffbe97db576e8db0598932deb044076d62fbd415d6bfd717f2d4b707209",
        "lineStart": 192,
        "lineEnd": 193,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-3.md#L192-L193"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8432b2e82997ff48aa22",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Use the [`force_use_graph_api` configuration option](../../setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/azuread/#force-fetching-groups-from-microsoft-graph-api) when configuring Azure AD authentication to force Grafana to fetch groups using Graph API.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.3",
        "Users and access",
        "Azure AD OAuth2: New option to always fetch groups from the Graph API"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "acf11473ed5777a12056a218dd89128f81813beb",
        "sha256": "64900ffbe97db576e8db0598932deb044076d62fbd415d6bfd717f2d4b707209",
        "lineStart": 195,
        "lineEnd": 196,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-3.md#L195-L196"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6b95f4983c23acc92f8f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We added a new endpoint to help users diagnose permissions-related issues with user and token authorization. [This endpoint](../../developers/http_api/access_control/#list-your-permissions) allows users to get the full list of RBAC permissions associated with their token.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.3",
        "Users and access",
        "RBAC: List token's permissions"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-3.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "acf11473ed5777a12056a218dd89128f81813beb",
        "sha256": "64900ffbe97db576e8db0598932deb044076d62fbd415d6bfd717f2d4b707209",
