      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f4b5f0c166d561e7b22d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "When you start your journey to create a dashboard or explore your data, but you don't have a data source connected yet, you’ll be shown a page that guides you to set up a first connection.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.4",
        "Dashboards and visualizations",
        "New data source connection page in Dashboards and Explore"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "45ce56665ca4f35f5a04a6213b45a29d1a3ddfc8",
        "sha256": "0149bcb00d079050a094ddb9bace1bde360efead88bd7cff979538dbd3130f77",
        "lineStart": 74,
        "lineEnd": 74,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md#L74-L74"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2fcc9e2154d8f88de43c",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Administrators can choose between selecting one of the most popular data sources or viewing the entire list. Editors are guided to contact their administrator to configure data sources. In both cases, there's also an option to continue without setting up a data source and to use sample data instead.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.4",
        "Dashboards and visualizations",
        "New data source connection page in Dashboards and Explore"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "45ce56665ca4f35f5a04a6213b45a29d1a3ddfc8",
        "sha256": "0149bcb00d079050a094ddb9bace1bde360efead88bd7cff979538dbd3130f77",
        "lineStart": 76,
        "lineEnd": 76,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md#L76-L76"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8a1888256d78cb72d74d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We added support to validate queries and visually display errors as a query is being written, without having to execute it to receive this feedback. This feature supports single and multi-line queries, with and without variables.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.4",
        "Dashboards and visualizations",
        "Loki datasource query validation"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "45ce56665ca4f35f5a04a6213b45a29d1a3ddfc8",
        "sha256": "0149bcb00d079050a094ddb9bace1bde360efead88bd7cff979538dbd3130f77",
        "lineStart": 94,
        "lineEnd": 94,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md#L94-L94"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e51a231ff912990d31f5",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For Loki metric queries in Explore, you can now see the sample of log lines that contributed to the displayed results. To see these logs, click on the collapsed **Logs sample** panel under your graph or table panel. If you want to interact with your log lines or modify the log query, click on the \"Open logs in split view\" button and the log query will be executed in the split view.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.4",
        "Dashboards and visualizations",
        "Loki logs sample in Explore"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "45ce56665ca4f35f5a04a6213b45a29d1a3ddfc8",
        "sha256": "0149bcb00d079050a094ddb9bace1bde360efead88bd7cff979538dbd3130f77",
        "lineStart": 104,
        "lineEnd": 104,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md#L104-L104"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b1c87e63b3b79de08790",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Canvas is a new panel that combines the power of Grafana with the flexibility of custom elements. Canvas visualizations are extensible form-built panels that allow you to explicitly place elements within static and dynamic layouts. This empowers you to design custom visualizations and overlay data in ways that aren’t possible with standard Grafana panels, all within Grafana’s UI. If you’ve used popular UI and web design tools, then designing Canvas panels will feel very familiar.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.4",
        "Canvas panel"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "45ce56665ca4f35f5a04a6213b45a29d1a3ddfc8",
        "sha256": "0149bcb00d079050a094ddb9bace1bde360efead88bd7cff979538dbd3130f77",
        "lineStart": 112,
        "lineEnd": 112,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md#L112-L112"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.aa735d79b540d065f576",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "In Grafana v9.4, we have added the ability to create connections (arrows). Connections enable you to connect elements together to create more complex visualizations. We also added support for data links and a brand new server element. To learn more about the Canvas panel, refer to [Canvas](../../panels-visualizations/visualizations/canvas/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.4",
        "Canvas panel"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "45ce56665ca4f35f5a04a6213b45a29d1a3ddfc8",
        "sha256": "0149bcb00d079050a094ddb9bace1bde360efead88bd7cff979538dbd3130f77",
        "lineStart": 114,
        "lineEnd": 114,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md#L114-L114"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.120595f7166957088000",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We have added a configuration option that enables you to require an expiration date limit for all newly created service account tokens.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.4",
        "Auth and security",
        "Service account expiration dates"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "45ce56665ca4f35f5a04a6213b45a29d1a3ddfc8",
        "sha256": "0149bcb00d079050a094ddb9bace1bde360efead88bd7cff979538dbd3130f77",
        "lineStart": 126,
        "lineEnd": 126,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md#L126-L126"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.df810084c2d86bfc236f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This change will not affect existing tokens. However, newly created tokens will require an expiration date that doesn't exceed the configuration option `token_expiration_day_limit`. This option is disabled by default.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.4",
        "Auth and security",
        "Service account expiration dates"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "45ce56665ca4f35f5a04a6213b45a29d1a3ddfc8",
        "sha256": "0149bcb00d079050a094ddb9bace1bde360efead88bd7cff979538dbd3130f77",
        "lineStart": 128,
        "lineEnd": 128,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md#L128-L128"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.cc8172616270474f6bdb",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "While Grafana integrates with many different auth providers, we have received requests for a feature that enables you to bypass organization role synchronization for individual providers rather than for all configured providers. This option is now available for users who want to be able to use Grafana to manage their org roles.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.4",
        "Auth and security",
        "OAuth providers setting for skip org role sync"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "45ce56665ca4f35f5a04a6213b45a29d1a3ddfc8",
        "sha256": "0149bcb00d079050a094ddb9bace1bde360efead88bd7cff979538dbd3130f77",
        "lineStart": 134,
        "lineEnd": 134,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md#L134-L134"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a17c67911104765ecabf",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This option enables you to skip synchronization from your configured OAuth provider specifically in the auth provider section under `skip_org_role_sync`. Previously users could only do this for certain providers using the `oauth_skip_org_role_sync_update` option, but this would include all of the configured providers.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.4",
        "Auth and security",
        "OAuth providers setting for skip org role sync"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "45ce56665ca4f35f5a04a6213b45a29d1a3ddfc8",
        "sha256": "0149bcb00d079050a094ddb9bace1bde360efead88bd7cff979538dbd3130f77",
        "lineStart": 136,
        "lineEnd": 136,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md#L136-L136"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b268002b328c3507502a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Learn more about Oauth in our [Oauth configuration guide](../../setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/generic-oauth/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.4",
        "Auth and security",
        "OAuth providers setting for skip org role sync"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "45ce56665ca4f35f5a04a6213b45a29d1a3ddfc8",
        "sha256": "0149bcb00d079050a094ddb9bace1bde360efead88bd7cff979538dbd3130f77",
        "lineStart": 138,
        "lineEnd": 138,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md#L138-L138"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.b60ba251b8c3297420ed",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We're rolling out RBAC support to Grafana plugins, with Grafana OnCall being the first plugin to fully support RBAC. Previously, Grafana OnCall relied on the Grafana basic roles (for example, Viewer, Editor, and Admin) for authorization within the plugin.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.4",
        "Auth and security",
        "RBAC support for Grafana OnCall plugin"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "45ce56665ca4f35f5a04a6213b45a29d1a3ddfc8",
        "sha256": "0149bcb00d079050a094ddb9bace1bde360efead88bd7cff979538dbd3130f77",
        "lineStart": 142,
        "lineEnd": 143,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md#L142-L143"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.1c4fedd94715abdfc0f0",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Before RBAC support in Grafana OnCall, it was only possible to allow your organization's users to either view everything, edit everything, or be an admin (which allowed edit access plus a few additional behaviors). With this new functionality, organizations will be able to harness fine-grained access control within Grafana OnCall.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.4",
        "Auth and security",
        "RBAC support for Grafana OnCall plugin"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "45ce56665ca4f35f5a04a6213b45a29d1a3ddfc8",
        "sha256": "0149bcb00d079050a094ddb9bace1bde360efead88bd7cff979538dbd3130f77",
        "lineStart": 145,
        "lineEnd": 145,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md#L145-L145"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.be4ad4ae72287bef073f",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For example, you can assign a Viewer basic role to a user in your organization (users must still have a basic role assigned) and also assign them the new Grafana OnCall RBAC role of **Schedules Editor**. This assignment enables the user to view everything in Grafana OnCall, and edit OnCall schedules.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.4",
        "Auth and security",
        "RBAC support for Grafana OnCall plugin"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "45ce56665ca4f35f5a04a6213b45a29d1a3ddfc8",
        "sha256": "0149bcb00d079050a094ddb9bace1bde360efead88bd7cff979538dbd3130f77",
        "lineStart": 147,
        "lineEnd": 147,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md#L147-L147"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.97a2fa2d297b95d388ba",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "We've added auto-login support for SAML authentication, which you can turn on with the `auto_login` configuration option. We also have a unified configuration style among all authentication providers. Instead of using `oauth_auto_login`, use the new `auto_login` option to enable automatic login for specific OAuth providers.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.4",
        "Auth and security",
        "SAML auto login"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "45ce56665ca4f35f5a04a6213b45a29d1a3ddfc8",
        "sha256": "0149bcb00d079050a094ddb9bace1bde360efead88bd7cff979538dbd3130f77",
        "lineStart": 153,
        "lineEnd": 155,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md#L153-L155"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6fd1cc15e0777442b829",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Learn more about SAML setup in our [SAML configuration guide](../../setup-grafana/configure-access/configure-authentication/saml/).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.4",
        "Auth and security",
        "SAML auto login"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "45ce56665ca4f35f5a04a6213b45a29d1a3ddfc8",
        "sha256": "0149bcb00d079050a094ddb9bace1bde360efead88bd7cff979538dbd3130f77",
        "lineStart": 157,
        "lineEnd": 157,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md#L157-L157"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.292e34776aa35bfcaa81",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This feature adds support to push analytics events and auditing logs to Loki with multi-tenancy mode, by specifying a tenant id. Learn more about [auditing](../../setup-grafana/configure-security/audit-grafana/) and [usage insights](../../setup-grafana/configure-security/export-logs/) in our docs.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.4",
        "Auditing and Usage Insights: Support for Loki multi-tenancy"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-4.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "45ce56665ca4f35f5a04a6213b45a29d1a3ddfc8",
