    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.cbfb23c524b04ea6f885",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Get additional help while configuring your Alertmanager. If you enter an invalid Alertmanager configuration, an error message displays, and you can choose from a previous working configuration to restart it.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.5",
        "Alerting",
        "Guidance for configuring your Alertmanager"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-5.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c2c2ff159ae288e6085e71233ed9e2f0d46eabfc",
        "sha256": "69c3976fa8ae84946bf60b2e847f4f05be57eaa6bf5eb5a975253df501005387",
        "lineStart": 162,
        "lineEnd": 162,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-5.md#L162-L162"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.5cb38993478f507e7c16",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Grafana v9.4 provided the ability to configure synchronization of organization roles for each OAuth provider. With synchronization on, the organization role was applied to the user from the OAuth provider upon signing in. However, after the user signed in, you could still change the user’s organization role during the session.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.5",
        "Auth: Lock organization roles synced from auth providers"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-5.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c2c2ff159ae288e6085e71233ed9e2f0d46eabfc",
        "sha256": "69c3976fa8ae84946bf60b2e847f4f05be57eaa6bf5eb5a975253df501005387",
        "lineStart": 175,
        "lineEnd": 175,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-5.md#L175-L175"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.5c359c3dc1b6f2f698ea",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "With this release, we are reinforcing organization role syncing behavior by introducing a new feature toggle called `onlyExternalOrgRoleSync`. Once enabled, users signing in to Grafana cannot change organization roles that have been synchronized from an external authentication provider, like Active Directory or Google OAuth. This can help ensure the right users maintain the right level of access at all times.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.5",
        "Auth: Lock organization roles synced from auth providers"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-5.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c2c2ff159ae288e6085e71233ed9e2f0d46eabfc",
        "sha256": "69c3976fa8ae84946bf60b2e847f4f05be57eaa6bf5eb5a975253df501005387",
        "lineStart": 177,
        "lineEnd": 177,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-5.md#L177-L177"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9b109834fced51878a78",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This feature should be used if you want to enforce strict role synchronization from your auth provider to the organization roles.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.5",
        "Auth: Lock organization roles synced from auth providers"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-5.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c2c2ff159ae288e6085e71233ed9e2f0d46eabfc",
        "sha256": "69c3976fa8ae84946bf60b2e847f4f05be57eaa6bf5eb5a975253df501005387",
        "lineStart": 179,
        "lineEnd": 179,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-5.md#L179-L179"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f9e79428da28ede51140",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To use this feature, enable the `onlyExternalOrgRoleSync` feature toggle. If you’re using Grafana Cloud and would like to enable this feature, please contact customer support. We'll also be automatically enabling this feature for Grafana Cloud instances over the upcoming weeks.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.5",
        "Auth: Lock organization roles synced from auth providers"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-5.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c2c2ff159ae288e6085e71233ed9e2f0d46eabfc",
        "sha256": "69c3976fa8ae84946bf60b2e847f4f05be57eaa6bf5eb5a975253df501005387",
        "lineStart": 181,
        "lineEnd": 181,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-5.md#L181-L181"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "mixed-edition-statement-requires-review",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f0499aaf3b132d0a5e50",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can also _prevent_ the synchronization of organization roles from a given authentication provider. Learn more in our [skip org role sync](../../setup-grafana/configure-grafana/#authgrafana_com-skip_org_role_sync/)! documentation.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.5",
        "Auth: Lock organization roles synced from auth providers"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-5.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c2c2ff159ae288e6085e71233ed9e2f0d46eabfc",
        "sha256": "69c3976fa8ae84946bf60b2e847f4f05be57eaa6bf5eb5a975253df501005387",
        "lineStart": 183,
        "lineEnd": 183,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-5.md#L183-L183"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2d606953063517912b08",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "This feature adds support for using JWT tokens to store rendering keys instead of relying on “remote caching”. It covers most rendering use cases, though some still rely on the remote cache as a store. You can enable this by enabling the feature flag `renderAuthJWT` in the `custom.ini` configuration file.",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.5",
        "Experimental support for using JWTs as auth method"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-5.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c2c2ff159ae288e6085e71233ed9e2f0d46eabfc",
        "sha256": "69c3976fa8ae84946bf60b2e847f4f05be57eaa6bf5eb5a975253df501005387",
        "lineStart": 197,
        "lineEnd": 197,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-5.md#L197-L197"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e8ec09909c99032cfbd2",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "One of the major changes coming in Grafana 10 will be our upgrade to React 18 and use of the new React client rendering API. There are many significant benefits we gain from this: access to new React features like [transitions](https://react.dev/reference/react/useTransition) and concurrent rendering, as well as other general performance and security improvements. These changes have now been delivered to the core `grafana` repo with [PR 64428](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/64428).",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.5",
        "Note for plugin developers"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-5.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c2c2ff159ae288e6085e71233ed9e2f0d46eabfc",
        "sha256": "69c3976fa8ae84946bf60b2e847f4f05be57eaa6bf5eb5a975253df501005387",
        "lineStart": 201,
        "lineEnd": 201,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/whatsnew/whats-new-in-v9-5.md#L201-L201"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.83e105bc624cea62678b",
      "syntaxRole": "list-item",
      "sourceText": "- Review the React 18 [upgrade docs](https://react.dev/blog/2022/03/08/react-18-upgrade-guide)",
      "headingPath": [
        "What's new in Grafana v9.5",
        "Note for plugin developers"
      ],
      "source": {
